{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers","id":1521633,"title":"Do you use Brawling and Martial Arts maneuvers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-29T17:58:37-07:00","id":1521633,"title":"Do you use Brawling and Martial Arts maneuvers","content":"I\u2019m finally approaching Session 0 and character creation for the Mage game I\u2019ve agreed to run, and I\u2019m considering ditching most of the close combat maneuvers. I don\u2019t want to go into why just yet, as that isn\u2019t my question, but I may further down-thread if people are interested. Suffice it to say that they don\u2019t seem to fit that well with what I want to do with this game.<br /> <br /> But before I commit to that, I\u2019m wanting to ask\u2026<br /> <br /> Do you use them? Do you have characters (of your own or in games you run) built with the required level of Brawl plus background for Dirty Fighting and/or Martial Arts/Do for 2 martial arts maneuvers per dot? Do your players deliberately choose between Punch and Kick from the general maneuvers (as opposed to simply always defaulting to Punch, the most basic maneuver)?<br /> <br /> Do you find that they add value to the play experience? If so, how have you found that they improve your games?<br /> <br /> Basically, what do you think would be lost by simply ignoring them?<br /> <br /> (This is another topic about how actual play aligns with the rulebook. I\u2019m not contending that there is no value in these rules.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T18:34:20-07:00","id":1521635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers#post1521633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m finally approaching Session 0 and character creation for the Mage game I\u2019ve agreed to run, and I\u2019m considering ditching most of the close combat maneuvers. I don\u2019t want to go into why just yet, as that isn\u2019t my question, but I may further down-thread if people are interested. Suffice it to say that they don\u2019t seem to fit that well with what I want to do with this game.<br /> <br /> But before I commit to that, I\u2019m wanting to ask\u2026<br /> <br /> Do you use them? Do you have characters (of your own or in games you run) built with the required level of Brawl plus background for Dirty Fighting and/or Martial Arts/Do for 2 martial arts maneuvers per dot? Do your players deliberately choose between Punch and Kick from the general maneuvers (as opposed to simply always defaulting to Punch, the most basic maneuver)?<br /> <br /> Do you find that they add value to the play experience? If so, how have you found that they improve your games?<br /> <br /> Basically, what do you think would be lost by simply ignoring them?<br /> <br /> (This is another topic about how actual play aligns with the rulebook. I\u2019m not contending that there is no value in these rules.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean all maneuvers, like grapple and sweep? I don't see a reason to remove them, they seem ok.<br /> <br /> Also, it makes sense for a martial artists to use other attacks besides punches. If you really don't like them, I'd say to use the default diff 6 and str dmg for all attacks, but don't restrict players to punch only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T19:31:48-07:00","id":1521638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521635#post1521635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean all maneuvers, like grapple and sweep? I don't see a reason to remove them, they seem ok.<br /> <br /> Also, it makes sense for a martial artists to use other attacks besides punches. If you really don't like them, I'd say to use the default diff 6 and str dmg for all attacks, but don't restrict players to punch only.</div> </div> </div> </div>We obviously need some mechanics to handle restraining an enemy, rendering an enemy prone, or moving an enemy against their will. Grapple and sweep are in that category.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t necessarily need 9 variations of \u201cdeal damage to an enemy\u201d, of which punch and kick are two. But that doesn\u2019t mean describing every damage-dealing attack as a punch.<br /> <br /> But you\u2019ve jumped ahead of the conversation, by not answering the questions about whether you use them and what value they bring to your games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T12:08:25-07:00","id":1521686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521638#post1521638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We obviously need some mechanics to handle restraining an enemy, rendering an enemy prone, or moving an enemy against their will. Grapple and sweep are in that category.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t necessarily need 9 variations of \u201cdeal damage to an enemy\u201d, of which punch and kick are two. But that doesn\u2019t mean describing every damage-dealing attack as a punch.<br /> <br /> But you\u2019ve jumped ahead of the conversation, by not answering the questions about whether you use them and what value they bring to your games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought it was kinda implicit in my answer. Yes, we use them. It adds options and cool factor for characters that are into martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T12:21:13-07:00","id":1521687,"title":"","content":"We use a house-ruled version of them. The concept of added maneuvers with increased training is fine, the execution isn't great.<br /> <br /> A lot of our changes are also motivated by the idea that having three different traits for bare-handed fighting is ridiculous rules bloat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T13:49:04-07:00","id":1521694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521687#post1521687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We use a house-ruled version of them. The concept of added maneuvers with increased training is fine, the execution isn't great.<br /> <br /> A lot of our changes are also motivated by the idea that having three different traits for bare-handed fighting is ridiculous rules bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why you think the execution isn't good?<br /> <br /> And you don't need 3 traits, you can have any one of them, so why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T14:32:00-07:00","id":1521696,"title":"","content":"The combat maneuvers (both basic and the ones you get from the close combat abilities) have no mechanical rigor to them. Some of them are utterly pointless to exist: Kick being a great example, as a the trade off of increased difficulty for increased damage is only beneficial in an extremely narrow range of situations, is a net change of zero most of the time, and actively a bad choice in many situations as well, there's never a point to using Kick instead of just making a targeted attack, because they you get the chance of some additional effect on top of more damage for your increased difficulty. So if you just Kick, you get +1 diff, +1 damage. If you strike someone in the arm, you get +1 diff, +1 damage, and they might be forced to drop a weapon they're holding or some other bonus.<br /> <br /> There's basically a lot of, &quot;these numbers sound good, lets not bother play testing it and just go with those.&quot; in how they feel.<br /> <br /> And I didn't say you need three traits, as in someone's going to bother making a character where they raise all three to high levels (though there's generally enough of a reason to take at least Brawl 3 and either Do 5 is you qualify for Do, or MA 5 if you don't get Do). As I said, the problem is bloat. If I take Melee 3 I can do anything that involves swinging a weapon around at people. Everything from stabbing someone with a shiv, to clobbering someone with a baseball bat, to exquisite fencing techniques, to hacking away at someone with a battle ax? It's all just Melee. Brawl, MA, and Do needlessly clog up the system with pointless granularity (which is also probably why so many of the moves are poorly designed). The CofD was completely correct to have Brawl, and if you want to train to do cool tricks you buy Fighting Styles as something that boosts Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T21:24:10-07:00","id":1521723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521696#post1521696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The combat maneuvers (both basic and the ones you get from the close combat abilities) have no mechanical rigor to them. Some of them are utterly pointless to exist: Kick being a great example, as a the trade off of increased difficulty for increased damage is only beneficial in an extremely narrow range of situations, is a net change of zero most of the time, and actively a bad choice in many situations as well, there's never a point to using Kick instead of just making a targeted attack, because they you get the chance of some additional effect on top of more damage for your increased difficulty. So if you just Kick, you get +1 diff, +1 damage. If you strike someone in the arm, you get +1 diff, +1 damage, and they might be forced to drop a weapon they're holding or some other bonus.<br /> <br /> There's basically a lot of, &quot;these numbers sound good, lets not bother play testing it and just go with those.&quot; in how they feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. However, I think that kick is the only example that seems worst and has no apparent benefit. Of course, we are talking about the regular, no-technique kick. The martial art, Do or dirty figthing kicks have benefits.<br /> <br /> Still, one could argue that a kick might have some implicit benefits compared to a punch. First, the kick probably has a higher range. Second, the kick might bring greater consequences than a punch. Being kicked in the face is way worse and more intimidating than being punched. I could see a ST giving a bonus for intimidation/fear or even getting the target dazed. Being sucker punched might be bad, but being sucker kicked seems way worse.<br /> <br /> I know those are not raw, and overall the kick is useless, though. But to be honest, most characters that are into fighting are going to kick using other maneuvers (there are several that covers kicks). The regular kick could even represent a kick being delivered by someone that has no training, and as kicks are harder to throw than a punch, they are less efficient (again, for non trained people).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521696#post1521696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I didn't say you need three traits, as in someone's going to bother making a character where they raise all three to high levels (though there's generally enough of a reason to take at least Brawl 3 and either Do 5 is you qualify for Do, or MA 5 if you don't get Do). As I said, the problem is bloat. If I take Melee 3 I can do anything that involves swinging a weapon around at people. Everything from stabbing someone with a shiv, to clobbering someone with a baseball bat, to exquisite fencing techniques, to hacking away at someone with a battle ax? It's all just Melee. Brawl, MA, and Do needlessly clog up the system with pointless granularity (which is also probably why so many of the moves are poorly designed). The CofD was completely correct to have Brawl, and if you want to train to do cool tricks you buy Fighting Styles as something that boosts Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems they wanted Do to be something extraordinary and with equaly extraordinary costs. Combining everything in martial arts and making Do just fluff wouldn't work due to the several mechanics benefits Do can provide. I would say that they could have added dirty fighting and brawl within martial arts, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T02:56:58-07:00","id":1521735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521723#post1521723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> think that kick is the only example that seems worst and has no apparent benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting into more complex examples: Snap Kick has no reason to exist when Elbow/Knee Strike does. Snap Kick does the exact same thing, but with more restrictive prerequisites (anyone that takes MA can take Elbow/Knee Strike, but Snap Kicks are only for Hard Styles).<br /> <br /> Like I said, there's a lot of bloat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, one could argue that a kick might have some implicit benefits compared to a punch. </div> </div> </div>Those arguments will fall on deaf ears for me. Maneuvers are mechanical widgets to give you more mechanical options in combat. If something isn't in the mechanics, it doesn't matter. There's already a rule for having a reach advantage in the game, if Kick was supposed to grant you that, it should say so. Otherwise you're just house ruling a bad maneuver to make it work using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being kicked in the face is way worse and more intimidating than being punched. </div> </div> </div>This simply isn't true. Many boxers would gladly demonstrate exactly how devastating a well executed cross to the face is.<br /> <br /> Do you have any combat training? Even self-defense training? I've been hit, a lot, and technique is vastly more important than what part of the body delivers the strike. The human body, for all the impressive things it can do, is not hard to damage if you know what you're doing. You only need to rely on raw strength (of either your muscles or the move you're trying to do) if you don't know how to best apply the attack you're using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (again, for non trained people). </div> </div> </div>This is, of course, part of the problem Brawl 5 is not a &quot;non-trained&quot; person. But Kick gets worse the more dice you have, because you're giving up on average more roll-over damage than the +1 damage you get from the kick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems they wanted Do to be something extraordinary and with equaly extraordinary costs. Combining everything in martial arts and making Do just fluff wouldn't work due to the several mechanics benefits Do can provide. I would say that they could have added dirty fighting and brawl within martial arts, though.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Do doesn't have extraordinary costs. It gets the best perks, sure, but it's also bullshit. If you want to mix magic and martial arts, we have preexisting rules for that. As well, there's the Esoterica Ability added in M20 that already has the ability to give extra perks to other Abilities while used in-line with the philosophic concepts of whatever Esoterica your character has studied. Esoterica (Do) makes the Akashayana more in-line with the rest of the mages, and also lets Do be a far more holistic concept like its always been described as being but was never backed up because the rules cared more about cool kung-fu monks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T10:28:52-07:00","id":1521760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521735#post1521735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those arguments will fall on deaf ears for me. Maneuvers are mechanical widgets to give you more mechanical options in combat. If something isn't in the mechanics, it doesn't matter. <b>There's already a rule for having a reach advantage in the game</b>, if Kick was supposed to grant you that, it should say so. Otherwise you're just house ruling a bad maneuver to make it work using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if this is a stupid question, but what is the rule for reach advantage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T11:31:57-07:00","id":1521764,"title":"","content":"Forgot that didn't make it into M20... in the past, it was a +1 diff to attack you if you had a significant reach advantage (usually like a spear vs unarmed)/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T15:15:35-07:00","id":1521786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521764#post1521764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot that didn't make it into M20... in the past, it was a +1 diff to attack you if you had a significant reach advantage (usually like a spear vs unarmed)/</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it did. It\u2019s in the sidebar at the top of page 420.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, that rule is slightly different: -1 die, rather than +1 diff. Either they changed it from earlier editions, or you misremembered the rule; I don\u2019t know which. But the rule reflects a similar intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 08-31-2023, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T16:23:11-07:00","id":1521788,"title":"","content":"I don't use them. However, I've read enough of them in different books that I apply them in general to the games as a consequence of people's attack descriptions. So If you say you want to do something, I'm going to adjust difficulty and apply colorful effects based on what you want to achieve. I find that flows much better than looking for lists with unique rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T16:23:30-07:00","id":1521789,"title":"","content":"So it is, I hate how inconsistent things can be between game lines and editions. MRev was also -1 die, but this was a full rule called &quot;Close&quot; not an optional sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T18:56:07-07:00","id":1521796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521735#post1521735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without getting into more complex examples: Snap Kick has no reason to exist when Elbow/Knee Strike does. Snap Kick does the exact same thing, but with more restrictive prerequisites (anyone that takes MA can take Elbow/Knee Strike, but Snap Kicks are only for Hard Styles).<br /> <br /> Like I said, there's a lot of bloat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Those arguments will fall on deaf ears for me. Maneuvers are mechanical widgets to give you more mechanical options in combat. If something isn't in the mechanics, it doesn't matter. There's already a rule for having a reach advantage in the game, if Kick was supposed to grant you that, it should say so. Otherwise you're just house ruling a bad maneuver to make it work using.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This simply isn't true. Many boxers would gladly demonstrate exactly how devastating a well executed cross to the face is.<br /> <br /> Do you have any combat training? Even self-defense training? I've been hit, a lot, and technique is vastly more important than what part of the body delivers the strike. The human body, for all the impressive things it can do, is not hard to damage if you know what you're doing. You only need to rely on raw strength (of either your muscles or the move you're trying to do) if you don't know how to best apply the attack you're using.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is, of course, part of the problem Brawl 5 is not a &quot;non-trained&quot; person. But Kick gets worse the more dice you have, because you're giving up on average more roll-over damage than the +1 damage you get from the kick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do doesn't have extraordinary costs. It gets the best perks, sure, but it's also bullshit. If you want to mix magic and martial arts, we have preexisting rules for that. As well, there's the Esoterica Ability added in M20 that already has the ability to give extra perks to other Abilities while used in-line with the philosophic concepts of whatever Esoterica your character has studied. Esoterica (Do) makes the Akashayana more in-line with the rest of the mages, and also lets Do be a far more holistic concept like its always been described as being but was never backed up because the rules cared more about cool kung-fu monks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are traits bloat. I can't deny that. The whole secondary traits thing smells like bloat to me. I just don't think it's a big deal. Do with combat maneuvers the sane thing you probably do to secondary abilities. Use what you want and ignore what is bad.<br /> There sre several other kick options in all 3 combat traits afterall.<br /> <br /> Yes, I practiced Muay Thai and yeah, a kick *is* stronger than a punch. Get someone who knows how to land both and you will see that the legs lash out more damage.<br /> But I wasn't even talking about pure damage, but the psychological effect of getting punched in the face vs. being kicked in the face. I grant, however, that any side effect of this kind would be a house rule.<br /> <br /> Raw, it's only the trade of +1 diff for +1 dmg and maybe -1 dice for the range difference.<br /> <br /> About Do, I think it's cool that mages have a whole awsone martial art that gives perks without magick. Esoterica doesn't really apply for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T21:28:12-07:00","id":1521803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521796#post1521796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there are traits bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying though, is there's also combat maneuver bloat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...yeah, a kick *is* stronger than a punch. </div> </div> </div>OK, I'm going to get a bit pedantic here:<br /> <br /> Kicks have a greater potential kinetic energy than punches. Punches transmit more of their energy into damage than kicks. &quot;Strength&quot; is too subjective of a word. And importantly, a skilled fighter can throw a punch or a kick with vastly more force than necessary to break bones or cause damage like a concussion. The added force a kick has is in excess of what you need to actually hit someone in a fashion that's demoralizing. Kicks have more kinetic energy because your legs (usually) are more massive than your arms, but they also means kicks spread out their impact over a larger surface area. This is fantastic for a waist-height kick to the gut, because that aids in doing maximum damage. It's horrible for the face because the skull has some of the strongest bones in the body that will get in the way of your kick crushing many of the weakest bones in the body, or perfectly hitting the numerous nerve clusters that can be fight stoppers because of how sensitive they are. All the potential of a kick is wasted trying to hit the chin, vomer, or eyes, because you're going to be sacrificing that raw power for accuracy to do that, while a punch can impact almost all of its power into those weak spots with ease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About Do, I think it's cool that mages have a whole awsone martial art that gives perks without magick. Esoterica doesn't really apply for combat. </div> </div> </div>One Tradition has an awesome martial art that gives perks without magic, despite all of the ancient combat traditions associated with many of the cultures that tend to feed into other Traditions. Why don't the Euthanatos get hyped up version of pankration from their Greek side, or bahuyudda from the Chakravanit? Why haven't the Chorus been able to leverage the esoteric martial arts of the dervishes and Sikh practioners of gatka? No, only the Chinese-coded Asian martial arts Tradition gets a super cool martial art that's mechanically superior to every other form of unarmed combat that doesn't use magic.<br /> <br /> And why doesn't Esoterica apply for combat? One of the examples in the book is ninjustu for stealth (and thus ambushes, because you're a ninja), while the Body Control side-box lists t'ai chi and qigong next to yoga as esoteric practices, and both of those are martial arts as well as holistic body training. If I can take Esoterica (Qigong) and then get access to the Body Control rules, why can't I get an Esoterica bonus from that to targeted shots as qigong focuses on precise strikes to nerve clusters and pressure points in order to incapacitate with minimal permanent damage? A good number of the Do maneuvers are based on qigong anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T07:22:15-07:00","id":1521812,"title":"","content":"Well, at this point I\u2019m pretty much certain I\u2019ll be dropping maneuvers as written. Before M20 they weren\u2019t even in the core rulebook, so I think we probably can get by without them.<br /> <br /> The problem I\u2019m seeing, at least as far as the game I intend to run is concern, is that these maneuvers put the decisions at the wrong times.<br /> <br /> The first aspect of this is how maneuvers are used in a combat scene. They require the player to say what move their character will attempt, then roll dice to see whether that move succeeds. But\u2026 that\u2019s not how a fight generally works. In a real fight, the 3-10 seconds that is a WoD action turn is a hell of a long time. Nobody competent goes into that fight planning to deliver Spinning Kick, and if you can\u2019t to do nothing at all. Even if you have a general hope of landing a spinning kick, a fight is very fluid, and if you\u2019re got skills (enough to warrant giving the character Spinning Kick in the first place) you\u2019re going to be adjusting to make use of whatever opportunity arises. In under three seconds, that intent to deliver a spinning kick becomes shoving someone into a bar stool.<br /> <br /> But then there\u2019s also a longer-scale aspect to this. Once a character has Spinning Kick, there\u2019s no point to Punch, mechanically (as has been noted by others). The character opens the fight with a Spinning Kick, follows up with Spinning Kick, and finally pulls out the big finishing move, Spinning Kick. Sure, we might make some different choices to make things interesting, but that\u2019s what the system incentivises. And really, this is setting the character\u2019s combat choices, to a large extent, in character creation.<br /> <br /> This flow - both the short and the long term - is backwards to what I want from combat. For a fight to be dramatic, it needs to be dynamic, with players making significant choices in the moment, and those choices revealing things about the character, adding to the story.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s what I don\u2019t want. What do I want instead?<br /> <br /> On the round-by-round scale, I want our play to always proceed forward, description leading to mechanic which leads to more description. Rather than saying exactly what move their character hopes to pull off - \u201cI\u2019ll do a Spinning Kick\u201d - I want a more general statement of intent - \u201cI want to harm the bruiser in front of me.\u201d Then we roll Dexterity + Melee, and we check how many successes came up. If it\u2019s a lot of successes, then we might describe the dramatic spinning kick, with a bunch of extra damage dice being rolled as this extremely powerful blow lands on the bruiser\u2019s jaw (or maybe a precise nerve strike, or a kidney punch, is more this character\u2019s style). Because we have the guidance of the number of successes before describing the detail, we can match our description to the outcome - no describing a Spinning Kick, only to have to back out with \u201cBut the bruiser dodges, and it hits only air\u201d when the roll is bad.<br /> <br /> None of that means we can\u2019t see tactical choices being made, where players make trade offs with the mechanics. We\u2019ve got that talk up-thread about how Kick is just a poor choice compared to Punch, giving no real increase in average damage, so why would anybody choose Kick? Well, the answer is that nobody should choose kick, but a similar mechanic describes something else - a character who is accepting a high chance of not landing a blow (that matters) on their enemy in exchange for a heightened chance of doing a particularly high amount of damage. (-1 diff for +1 damage die possibly doesn\u2019t actually do this, but -1 for +2 might, or -2 for +2. I\u2019d need to run some numbers.) That tells us something general about the character - what their appetite for risk is at the moment, how desperate they are getting. (And then we get the detail of what they actually do after the roll.) And those sorts of trade-offs are general enough that it doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense to buy them during character creation. You\u2019d buy high enough skill to allow you to have risky strategies pay off more often, but you wouldn\u2019t be buying the specific maneuver.<br /> <br /> And that brings us to character creation. We already have a 0-5 rating in our choice of Brawl or Martial Arts representing general skill, we shade that to an extent with Athletics (for the dodge), the physical attributes, and similar. But we also have specialties, and we can let them play more of a role. Rather than buying specific maneuvers, I have plans to allow characters to buy specialties in Throws, Damaging Blows, Immobilising - the name of the specialty doesn\u2019t matter; a player can have a specialty in Judo and we agree that this means that 10s count as two successes for throws.<br /> <br /> And obviously this means that I still need a mechanic for throws, and a mechanic for grappling, and some other things. But those can be generalised a bit from the very specific maneuvers the book gives.<br /> <br /> The one thing missing from all of this is the ultra-special named martial arts move - the One-Finger Death Strike or the Thunder Crane Kick. The thing that a martial artist hunted for a master for years to learn, said to be truly unstoppable. A staple of old pulp martial arts stories. But the thing about those moves is that they really seem like something properly magical. For that, we have rotes.<br /> <br /> Despite the length of this post, I really haven\u2019t hit on some key mechanics that I\u2019m settling on, but I\u2019m tired and have typed enough for now. Maybe later, when I have time and a hand that isn\u2019t aching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-01-2023, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T08:14:27-07:00","id":1521813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521803#post1521803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm saying though, is there's also combat maneuver bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. To be honest, I don't think it's bloat, just bad ruling. If kick had other benefits that made it worth it, it wouldn't be considered bloat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521803#post1521803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I'm going to get a bit pedantic here:<br /> <br /> Kicks have a greater potential kinetic energy than punches. Punches transmit more of their energy into damage than kicks. &quot;Strength&quot; is too subjective of a word. And importantly, a skilled fighter can throw a punch or a kick with vastly more force than necessary to break bones or cause damage like a concussion. The added force a kick has is in excess of what you need to actually hit someone in a fashion that's demoralizing. Kicks have more kinetic energy because your legs (usually) are more massive than your arms, but they also means kicks spread out their impact over a larger surface area. This is fantastic for a waist-height kick to the gut, because that aids in doing maximum damage. It's horrible for the face because the skull has some of the strongest bones in the body that will get in the way of your kick crushing many of the weakest bones in the body, or perfectly hitting the numerous nerve clusters that can be fight stoppers because of how sensitive they are. All the potential of a kick is wasted trying to hit the chin, vomer, or eyes, because you're going to be sacrificing that raw power for accuracy to do that, while a punch can impact almost all of its power into those weak spots with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kicks are more powerful than punches because legs are heavier and faster than arms. More muscles and a bigger size also increase the angular momentum (from a roundhouse kick for example). Anyway, it is unquestionable that kicks deliver more damage than punches (considering both from the same fighter and well trained in both strikes), and you can see or read that in any martial arts documentary or paper.<br /> However, kicks are harder to land than punches, and also leave the attacker open for some countrr strikes, also unsermining the attacker stability.<br /> <br /> So, the trade seems to work: it is harder to land (+diff), but it's more powerful (+dmg). I just think it should not be a 1:1. Maybe being +3 dmg would be better.<br /> <br /> But again, there are several other kicks in the maneuvers list, so just don't use this one...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521803#post1521803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Tradition has an awesome martial art that gives perks without magic, despite all of the ancient combat traditions associated with many of the cultures that tend to feed into other Traditions. Why don't the Euthanatos get hyped up version of pankration from their Greek side, or bahuyudda from the Chakravanit? Why haven't the Chorus been able to leverage the esoteric martial arts of the dervishes and Sikh practioners of gatka? No, only the Chinese-coded Asian martial arts Tradition gets a super cool martial art that's mechanically superior to every other form of unarmed combat that doesn't use magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Euthanatos aren't as much into martial art as Akashics, and having one trait for each tradition is crazy.<br /> <br /> I do not like the idea that *only* akashics can learn Do, though. I tend to be way more liberal with Do. <br /> Although, the charavter still have to follow all those Do philosophies and practice every day, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521803#post1521803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why doesn't Esoterica apply for combat? One of the examples in the book is ninjustu for stealth (and thus ambushes, because you're a ninja), while the Body Control side-box lists t'ai chi and qigong next to yoga as esoteric practices, and both of those are martial arts as well as holistic body training. If I can take Esoterica (Qigong) and then get access to the Body Control rules, why can't I get an Esoterica bonus from that to targeted shots as qigong focuses on precise strikes to nerve clusters and pressure points in order to incapacitate with minimal permanent damage? A good number of the Do maneuvers are based on qigong anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do can make you deal lethal, block melee with bare hands and decrease attacks difficulties. <br /> Esoterica application for combat is body control, like ignoring dmg penalties. What are you suggesting? Ditch Do and use Esoterica?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a><br /> <br /> 1) Fights are fast, but that doesn't mean you can't plan what you gonna do. It's not all instincts. And I'd say the more professional you get, the more you plan and wait for the right opening. Good MMA fighters spend a lot of time just checking, scaning and flintching each other before landing a blow. I don't see the issue with a player (and character) thinking &quot;I'm gonna do a shin to the tights now&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) There are reasons for punching: you dont need much room to throw a punch, while a spinning kick requires the right amount of room around and distance from the target. You can punch while fighting on the ground. Spinning kicks gets you tired way faster than punches. Just to give some examples. The thing is, each maneuver is different and should have their own complications and perks. Don't treat them just as numbers.<br /> <br /> 3) I feel that vague statements like &quot;I wanna bruise someone&quot; it's way worse for roleplaying than &quot;I wanna do a spinning kick&quot;. How exactly you want to bruise the target? It's a punch? A knee to the stomach? An humiliating teep to the face? The answer will also say how the target reacts and then the combat gets dynamic. <br /> If you are limited by &quot;bruise&quot;,&quot;dodge&quot;,&quot;attack&quot;, it becomes a game of pure numbers.<br /> <br /> 4) Deciding what is done by the result of the dice removes freedom for the player and also undermines roleplay, in my opinion. I prefer detailed descriptions, like &quot;I land a right cross to the liver&quot;. Doesn't matter how much successes you get, if you hit you will hit the liver, not the face. I believe better descriptions add realism to the fight.<br /> <br /> 5) The best and &quot;special&quot; maneuvers, like the death strike, are not even close to be as good as combat magick. Also, vampires have fangs, garou have bites and claws, I find it very cool for mages to have martial arts as their option for mundane combat advantages. <br /> <br /> And again, why remove them completely? The weak/bad maneuvers will probably not be used by players anyway...<br /> <br /> All that are *my* opinions. It seems you kinda have your mind made here, so go for what you believe will work for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T08:15:25-07:00","id":1521814,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Storypath combat systems? It doesn't do a lot with martial arts techniques, but it seems like a structure you'd enjoy more than the default Storyteller system M20 uses.<br /> <br /> The basic reason I bring this up, in in Storypath, you do actually just declare that you're attacking someone, with only your Skill + Attribute selection as a the decision you make at that point. After you roll your attack dice and account for their Defense, you have a pool of successes you spend on various options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T08:56:24-07:00","id":1521815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Fights are fast, but that doesn't mean you can't plan what you gonna do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you plan, but if you\u2019re good, you\u2019ve planned a bunch of contingencies too. I\u2019m no MMA fighter, but I had enough training back in the day to be able to see where RPG combat systems fall short.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) There are reasons for punching: you dont need much room to throw a punch, while a spinning kick requires the right amount of room around and distance from the target. You can punch while fighting on the ground. Spinning kicks gets you tired way faster than punches. Just to give some examples. The thing is, each maneuver is different and should have their own complications and perks. Don't treat them just as numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take it up with the system designers. In the system, they are just numbers, and if I need to heavily house rule to change that, I might as well do it now so I can be up front about it with the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I feel that vague statements like &quot;I wanna bruise someone&quot; it's way worse for roleplaying than &quot;I wanna do a spinning kick&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the players are not limited to the vague statements. They still get to give the detail. It just comes a little later in the process. (And they get to give detail that stands, not detail they only hope will be supported by the rolls.) Description feeds mechanics, mechanics feed back into description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Deciding what is done by the result of the dice</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026was not suggested at any point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) The best and &quot;special&quot; maneuvers, like the death strike, are not even close to be as good as combat magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they don\u2019t really fit the part of the ultra-special move that the mystical martial artist hunts for years for a master to learn from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T10:24:59-07:00","id":1521820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521815#post1521815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take it up with the system designers. In the system, they are just numbers, and if I need to heavily house rule to change that, I might as well do it now so I can be up front about it with the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they aren't. All the dots in a sheet aren't just numbers and the game designers say so all the time in the book. I gave several examples of why one could throw a punch, but couldn't throw a spinning kick.<br /> <br /> Also, if someone wanta to constantly use spinning kicks (or any other attack), why bother? It's their favorite move. You never played against that anoying friend that uses hadouken all the time? Lol<br /> <br /> Also, that means he is a predictable opponent and any enemy with a brain will adapt their strategy, considering the dighter practically only uses the same attack.<br /> <br /> This is a TTRPG, don't treat it as a video game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521815#post1521815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why they don\u2019t really fit the part of the ultra-special move that the mystical martial artist hunts for years for a master to learn from.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanted them to be stronger, then?<br /> <br /> I think I didn't understand what you have in mind for combat, could you care to provide an example of game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T10:49:44-07:00","id":1521822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521813#post1521813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Euthanatos aren't as much into martial art as Akashics, and having one trait for each tradition is crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Euthanatos are considering the best killer sin the Traditions, and plenty of them do it up close (aka use martial arts).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are you suggesting? Ditch Do and use Esoterica? </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T20:07:27-07:00","id":1521850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521814#post1521814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at the Storypath combat systems? It doesn't do a lot with martial arts techniques, but it seems like a structure you'd enjoy more than the default Storyteller system M20 uses.<br /> <br /> The basic reason I bring this up, in in Storypath, you do actually just declare that you're attacking someone, with only your Skill + Attribute selection as a the decision you make at that point. After you roll your attack dice and account for their Defense, you have a pool of successes you spend on various options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Storypath is not far off where I\u2019m settling. Not that I\u2019m planning to buy another system to tell me how and then try to integrate with M20 - more work than it\u2019s worth. But the basic concept is about right.<br /> <br /> We already have that in Storyteller, conceptually. It\u2019s just hidden. When you attack, you roll your Dex+MA, subtract successes on defence (which defaults to 0, but dodge, parry, and the like give successes that subtract from attack successes), then your first success buys Strength dice of damage, and every success after that buys an extra die of damage.<br /> <br /> If we just add an extra option for spending those extra successes, and let the players decide how to spend them after the roll, we\u2019ve basically got Storypath.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s pretty much where I\u2019ve landed. There\u2019s a few effects that I want players to be able to apply in combat - immobilise/hold, knock down, forcibly move, outmaneuver, Violence Enhances Magick, maybe a couple of others - and I figure each of them can be applied by spending successes. You could achieve combination effects - say, knock down with injury - by having the player fully state their intent and adding up the number of successes required, then having the player roll to see if they get enough successes, but\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 I\u2019m thinking, why bother with that much detail in the intent? If the player doesn\u2019t roll enough successes, the cool move doesn\u2019t happen and what does happen usually falls flat by comparison. Instead, I\u2019ll just get something brief and general as intent, and then if the player rolls a lot of successes, they can be pleasantly surprised, spend the successes for some desirable combination of effects, and describe a cool move that they think suits the degree of success rolled. I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019ll hear more cool moves described this way, because the players don\u2019t have to worry about what happens if they don\u2019t pull it off. And more varied cool moves, because nobody has their initial expectations set by that Spinning Kick on their character sheet; they have more opportunity to adapt to the situation.<br /> <br /> And if what the player wants is a lot of damage and the character\u2019s signature Spinning Kick, they can have that too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T03:07:10-07:00","id":1521863,"title":"","content":"I had people over for Session 0 and character creation. We didn\u2019t get much actual character building done (good session 0 discussion and some strong concepts for the game I\u2019m intending) but when one player mentioned creating the bruiser of the group (because we had none) I mentioned that I was looking to drop maneuvers as they stand, and others just said yeah, they\u2019d rather have the descriptive detail after seeing the mechanical result too.<br /> <br /> (\u201cEspecially when rolling multiple dice\u201d, said one player, referring to how a dice pool gives a degree of success, not just a success/failure binary.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T08:25:04-07:00","id":1521875,"title":"","content":"So, for you combat will literally just be &quot;roll dex and brawl&quot; and that's it?<br /> <br /> Seems really limited","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T08:37:05-07:00","id":1521876,"title":"","content":"No, the concept is that you roll first, and pick what it does second. So you don't have to sit there deciding between a targeted attack at their legs, or a bunch of different (thanks to M20s combat maneuver bloat) other knockdown options before you attack and try to figure out the pros and cons of each adjustment to the rules they impart, and what that means for your likely outcomes. You roll Dex + [Ability] and then spend your successes towards different effects to achieve your intent as best you can once you know what you're working with.<br /> <br /> It's like using the optional dividing successes rules for casting magic: if you roll 4 more successes than you need for the base effect, you get to decide how much goes into extra damage, extra duration, extra targets, etc. instead of that being predetermined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:11:57-07:00","id":1521881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521876#post1521876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the concept is that you roll first, and pick what it does second. So you don't have to sit there deciding between a targeted attack at their legs, or a bunch of different (thanks to M20s combat maneuver bloat) other knockdown options before you attack and try to figure out the pros and cons of each adjustment to the rules they impart, and what that means for your likely outcomes. You roll Dex + [Ability] and then spend your successes towards different effects to achieve your intent as best you can once you know what you're working with.<br /> <br /> It's like using the optional dividing successes rules for casting magic: if you roll 4 more successes than you need for the base effect, you get to decide how much goes into extra damage, extra duration, extra targets, etc. instead of that being predetermined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand.<br /> <br /> If you roll before you decide what you do...how do you know what your pool is?<br /> <br /> Also, all of that stuff has been there since revised. M20 didn't invent it, just gather it together","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-02-2023, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:14:31-07:00","id":1521882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521876#post1521876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the concept is that you roll first, and pick what it does second. So you don't have to sit there deciding between a targeted attack at their legs, or a bunch of different (thanks to M20s combat maneuver bloat) other knockdown options before you attack and try to figure out the pros and cons of each adjustment to the rules they impart, and what that means for your likely outcomes. You roll Dex + [Ability] and then spend your successes towards different effects to achieve your intent as best you can once you know what you're working with.<br /> <br /> It's like using the optional dividing successes rules for casting magic: if you roll 4 more successes than you need for the base effect, you get to decide how much goes into extra damage, extra duration, extra targets, etc. instead of that being predetermined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand.<br /> <br /> If you roll before you decide what you do...how do you know what your pool is?<br /> <br /> Also, all of that stuff has been there since revised. M20 didn't invent it so much as gather it together.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:25:52-07:00","id":1521884,"title":"","content":"Your pool is based on how your attacking, just like always. Dex + Brawl for unarmed, Melee for armed, Athetics for some ranged, Firearms for the rest of ranged.<br /> <br /> And yeah, M20 did gather a bunch of stuff together that existed before, but a lot of it didn't exist together either. Collecting and not trimming excess/redundancies diminished the end result; even for an Anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:40:29-07:00","id":1521885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521875#post1521875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for you combat will literally just be &quot;roll dex and brawl&quot; and that's it?<br /> <br /> Seems really limited</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said. Not having the action descrpition kills all the realism of the game. If combat is players declaring &quot;I attack&quot; and others &quot;I dodge&quot;, then you better play Mortal Kombat lol.<br /> <br /> I also don't understand what is this rolling first about. You roll at which difficulty? A punch in the face is easier to land than a double flying kick, so you cant uae the same difficulty for both. <br /> <br /> Also, deciding after wont stop players from sitting there and deciding what maneuver would fit better into what they got.<br /> <br /> And lastly, the dividing successea rule does not allow you to choose your effect after rolling. You have to clearly state what you want to do before (like any spellcasting) and the roll. If you fall a little short of successes, then you can choose what to do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T10:57:53-07:00","id":1521895,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I don't see what the problem is. Most of the combat maneuvers give you options given circumstances.<br /> <br /> - Targeting, lets you increase damage pool in exchange to increasing diff to hit up to 3, can also ignore armor depending on circumstance<br /> - Bite and Claw attacks are for those who invest in Life 3 style wildshape magicks<br /> - Disarming is when you want to aim at their weapon with your own weapon<br /> - Flanking/rear attacks are just a way to reduce diff<br /> - Grappling is an age old option for RPGs across the field, but they also allow you direct contact with someone, which can make magic requiring direct contact far easier, or possible, to do.<br /> - Kicking is just a more difficult punch, but lets you use your legs if you are otherwise unable to use your arms, such as if you were hanging on to something, or lying down as they approach your feet, or if grappled such that your arms are immobalised.<br /> - Punching is... well, it's punching, and is the standard assumed thing people do when rolling brawl<br /> - Reading an Opponent just lets you get more dice<br /> - Sweeps let you force your opponent in to the Knocked Down condition (which gives you or others a -2 diff to hit them while they are down)<br /> - Tackling allows you a way both hit and sweep simultaneously. It's basically two rolls, one to hit for damage, and one contested roll to see if they get knocked down<br /> <br /> And that is all the basic combat maneuvers for brawl, it boils down to punching (or biting/clawing is you can do that), kicking when punching isn't a choice, surrounding them for reduced diff, causing them to be knocked down for reduced diff, disarming, or grappling them. It isn't all that bloated at all.<br /> <br /> All the other options are specialist options if you have specific talents or skills.<br /> <br /> Dirty fighting can usually only be done if you have at least 3 dots of brawl, and an appropriate reason why you would be prone to such techniques. but it allows you to:<br /> <br /> - blind the opponent: Basically making them unable to use defensive actions and forcing a +2 diff to their actions<br /> - Body Slam: lets you do more damage following a successful grapple than usual<br /> - Curbstomp: A way to do lethal damage via brawl against a stunned or immobalised opponent<br /> - Haymaker: A more powerful punch that provides some knock back<br /> - Head Butt: A way to use your head, good for when you are otherwise immobalised such as by a grapple.<br /> - Jab pistol: A way to turn your firearm into a brawl attack<br /> - Low blow: This forces the opponent to be stunned, making them unable to act for the next few rounds<br /> - Pistol Whip: A melee effect that a brawler can employ to force a stun and do lethal damage with something that would otherwise do bashing damage<br /> <br /> These options are essentially extensions of the basic options, and are geared around capitalising or causing immobilisation or stunning, or in translating your damage to lethal<br /> <br /> Martial Arts works in a completely different way. Instead of being a large list of things you can do, each dot in martial arts lets you choose 2 martial arts maneuvers from the list to have in your repertoire, some of which require dots in other abilities are prerequisites. It's a bit more involved and works a bit more like a skill tree than the brawl ones, which are available to all characters, or the dirty fighting techniques, which are available to particularly trained brawlers.<br /> <br /> Do is sort of the same concept, but expanded into a way of life. It is not only about having the requirements to access these techniques, but you must also live in a particular manner or else you will lose access to these abilities as the ST sees appropriate.<br /> Speak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T11:36:06-07:00","id":1521898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521885#post1521885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I said. Not having the action descrpition <b>kills all the realism of the game</b>. If combat is players declaring &quot;I attack&quot; and others &quot;I dodge&quot;, then you better play Mortal Kombat lol.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> The storyteller system is not that realistic to begin, it lacks too many details to support all the manoeuvres that they included in the rules.<br /> It is a shame I really like the idea of having a detailed manoeuvre-based combat system, but the game's rules don't really distinguish between a punch a kick or an elbow strike.<br /> Also having both varying dice pool and roll difficulties makes the game math not trivial either for the player or for the game designer.<br /> I always dreamed of converting the cWoD main supplement to a The Riddle of the Steel-like combat system, but I'm not so familiar with the TRotS and I do not have enough time for this conversion and how to expand the TRotS-like system to support superhuman or clearly non-human creatures.<br /> <br /> While I <b>really </b>love games with s complex players-centred combat systems a games where the players do not have to choose beforehand what it does have a different flavour in terms of meta-game because you can play a good fighter even if you do not master the combat system you just like you could play a good hacker/painter/economists/physician even if you don't know anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T14:47:46-07:00","id":1521910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521885#post1521885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't understand what is this rolling first about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you looked at the Storypath stuff at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You roll at which difficulty? </div> </div> </div>Whatever would be normal (so 6, unless you'd get a bonus like flanking or prone).. Harder to pull off effects require more successes to buy instead of modifying difficulty. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A punch in the face is easier to land than a double flying kick, so you cant uae the same difficulty for both. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what's clear here: if you roll one success, you describe it as a simple jab to the face. If you roll five successes then you describe it as pulling off a double flying kick to the face (all damage), or solid sidekick that hits hard and pushes someone back as well (mixing damage with forced movement). You pick the action that matches your roll, and how you priorities effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, deciding after wont stop players from sitting there and deciding what maneuver would fit better into what they got. </div> </div> </div>Yes it does, because there aren't maneuvers to pick. You just describe it in a fashion that matches the roll and the allocation of successes. As long as the effect is the same, you can describe it however it makes sense. A sweep and a hip throw don't require separate maneuver, both are just describing rolling enough successes to do a bit of damage and get a guaranteed knocked down.<br /> <br /> The decision isn't in how to describe it, just what you want it to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T16:11:23-07:00","id":1521923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521910#post1521910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A sweep and a hip throw don't require separate maneuver, both are just describing rolling enough successes to do a bit of damage and get a guaranteed knocked down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but, hip throw? where is this manoeuvre written?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T17:29:00-07:00","id":1521924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521923#post1521923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry but, hip throw? where is this manoeuvre written?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not, unless you consider it covered by Throw on page 426. But that\u2019s part of the attraction of moving away from maneuvers - we\u2019re no long confined to the list in the book. If the player wants their character to do a hop throw, they just say the result is a hip throw (and if someone else at the table doesn\u2019t know what a hop throw is, they can say what a hip throw is).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T17:43:32-07:00","id":1521925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521924#post1521924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not, unless you consider it covered by Throw on page 426. But that\u2019s part of the attraction of moving away from maneuvers - we\u2019re no long confined to the list in the book. If the player wants their character to do a hop throw, they just say the result is a hip throw (and if someone else at the table doesn\u2019t know what a hop throw is, they can say what a hip throw is).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you objection was there were too many manoeuvres. It seems inconsistent to then say there are not enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T17:49:50-07:00","id":1521926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521910#post1521910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at the Storypath stuff at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I wasn\u2019t even aware it was a thing that existed. In my current situation I also have no desire to drop money on something there\u2019s a good chance I might think isn\u2019t at all what I want and will therefore never use.<br /> <br /> So could you maybe provide some examples of these maneuvers you can spend successes on instead of beating around the bush? I presume things like knock downs, pushes, stuns, etc.<br /> <br /> Or was \u201cjust describe the damage as coming from a more impressive looking manuever\u201d it? I would presume not or there would be no need to reference another system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T17:59:34-07:00","id":1521927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521895#post1521895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I don't see what the problem is. Most of the combat maneuvers give you options given circumstances.<br /> <br /> - Targeting, lets you increase damage pool in exchange to increasing diff to hit up to 3, can also ignore armor depending on circumstance<br /> [\u2026]<br /> - Flanking/rear attacks are just a way to reduce diff</div> </div> </div> </div>Targeting isn\u2019t even presented as a maneuver. Flanking is presented as a maneuver, but I don\u2019t know why because it\u2019s really more of an adjustment that combines with various other maneuvers and would seem to fit better alongside Targeting Location and Cover and Concealment (also not a maneuver).<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that characters should not be able to do the things maneuvers described by maneuvers. I\u2019m pretty sure we all have access to the rulebook, so we know what they do. We\u2019re just talking about moving the decision points around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-02-2023, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T18:09:39-07:00","id":1521928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521927#post1521927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Targeting isn\u2019t even presented as a maneuver. Targeting is presented as a maneuver, but I don\u2019t know why because it\u2019s really more of an adjustment that combines with various other maneuvers and would see, to fit better alongside Targeting Location and Cover and Concealment (also not a maneuver).<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that characters should not be able to do the things maneuvers described by maneuvers. I\u2019m pretty sure we all have access to the rulebook, so we know what they do. We\u2019re just talking about moving the decision points around.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>and I\u2019m saying I don\u2019t recognise the validity of the complaint. Which if I understand correctly was that thr manoeuvres present were too complicated and unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I presented this breakdown to demonstrate that they were in fact quite simple and each one provided different means of interacting with the combat scenario. In addition, these are move that the ST can choose to use on the player in order to create new obstacles for them to overcome.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t recognise the proclaimed problem that players spend a lot of time trying to choose what to do because of manoeuvres. Typically during declarations, I ask what my players wish to do, and if they say \u201cI want to punch him\u201d so I say, ok, dex and brawl diff 6. or \u201cI want to knock him to the ground\u201d I ask \u201cyou going to tackle him? Or just hit his legs?\u201d And they go \u201chit their legs\u201d so I say \u201cok, that\u2019s a sweep, dex and brawl diff 8\u201d<br /> <br /> very little problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T21:59:01-07:00","id":1521945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521926#post1521926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I wasn\u2019t even aware it was a thing that existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path makes five games (four own outright by them, and one partner game) that use the system. They put out free updated preview documents for free on DTRPG every two years or so. This is on top of any free or cheap previews and quick-starts for the specific games. This regularly comes up in the forum announcements; including live plays of the games. Even if for whatever reasons you've glazed over all that in the past four years, there's plenty of free things out there if you apply the Google.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So could you maybe provide some examples of these maneuvers you can spend successes on instead of beating around the bush? I presume things like knock downs, pushes, stuns, etc. </div> </div> </div>I provided an example of using five successes to either land a massive hit, or to do less damage but add a forced movement effect. Knock down/back, disarms, initiating grapples, feints, etc You seem to understand just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521928#post1521928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I\u2019m saying I don\u2019t recognise the validity of the complaint. Which if I understand correctly was that thr manoeuvres present were too complicated and unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me simplify the complaint a bit then:<br /> <br /> The current implementation of the rules makes combat a mess. The rules are inconsistent, lacking in mechanical rigor, can be highly rewarding or extremely punishing for no reasons that map to either what the game says it wants out of combat, fun for people that enjoy tactical depth, or even give it a sense of verisimilitude. Thus, it's a mess.<br /> <br /> The fact that your players don't actually know the maneuvers and just rely on you to pick for them is more of an illustration of the point than you seem to think: players should know what their characters are capable of. Do any of your players have the Martial Arts or Do traits? How did they select which special moves they got if they need to ask you for the rules on what the moves actually do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T02:03:16-07:00","id":1521959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521945#post1521945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me simplify the complaint a bit then:<br /> <br /> The current implementation of the rules makes combat a mess. The rules are inconsistent, lacking in mechanical rigor, can be highly rewarding or extremely punishing for no reasons that map to either what the game says it wants out of combat, fun for people that enjoy tactical depth, or even give it a sense of verisimilitude. Thus, it's a mess.<br /> <br /> The fact that your players don't actually know the maneuvers and just rely on you to pick for them is more of an illustration of the point than you seem to think: players should know what their characters are capable of. Do any of your players have the Martial Arts or Do traits? How did they select which special moves they got if they need to ask you for the rules on what the moves actually do?</div> </div> </div> </div>you have proclaimed they lack rigor, but have yet to demonstrate as such. The way that combat works in wod is everyone in the first turn at least can do something, their choices are to attack, defend, or make theirs or another's actions easier to do.<br /> <br /> Since damage is not rolled until phase 3 of combat, everyone has a chance to contribute something before damage starts to remove dice from one\u2019s pool.<br /> <br /> My illustration was to demonstrate that one need not have a comprehensive understanding of the rules in order play. This is also true for the magic casting system in general, and how I often teach new players the rules. As things come up, they learn what is possible. Another means I use is by having my NPCs use these moves on them.<br /> <br /> However, the only thing players need to do to understand their options is have a look at pg420-422, it\u2019s all there. With the list of conditions on pg416<br /> <br /> it\u2019s really not a lot of reading, and if they needed a quick reff, pg 448 can provide that. It\u2019s honestly not nearly the insurmountable task you make it out to be.<br /> <br /> As for martial arts and Do, those decisions are made when they get the dots. They look through the list of maneuvers and pick two. They write them down on their sheet, and know that these are now options which are open to them. Since they pick them, it\u2019s on them to know what they do and decide when to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T03:07:51-07:00","id":1521965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521928#post1521928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which if I understand correctly was that thr manoeuvres present were too complicated and unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Others might find the maneuvers too complicated, but I didn\u2019t say anything like that. I said that the significant decisions are being made at the wrong times for what I want to do with the game.<br /> <br /> The maneuvers are certainly unnecessary, but the entire system is unnecessary. The question is never what game mechanics are necessary; it\u2019s always about what mechanics enhance the play experience. And that\u2019s why I asked my original questions: Do you use the maneuvers (especially the ones that aren\u2019t available to everyone by default), and if so what do you find they add to your game? Because the reality check for me is what my players will miss out on if I just ditch that aspect of M20.<br /> <br /> The timing issue isn\u2019t about how long players spend making decisions, it\u2019s about when they make those decisions. When a player writes a maneuver on their character sheet, that becomes an anchored expectation - we will probably see it used repeatedly. That decision tells us one thing - that the character has trained to use that maneuver. And when a player chooses a maneuver before the roll, it tells us another thing - that the character hopes to use that maneuver. But I don\u2019t much care about those decisions. I care about what the character hopes to achieve (not the move, the aim of the move) in the moment before the roll, and I care about what the character actually does in the moment after the roll. (Not just wherever the character succeeds or fails at using a particular move; I want to hear how the character makes the best of the situation if the roll gives less successes than what they hoped for; or how they utilize an unexpected opportunity if they get a great roll.) Those are the decisions I am more interested it hearing from my players.<br /> <br /> More simply, I don\u2019t want to hear about what might happen, so much as what does happen.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying you should want the same thing, or that the system is necessarily wrong in any particular way. Just that the maneuvers didn\u2019t seem to be fulfilling my objectives, and on consultation with the players they don\u2019t seem to fit their objectives either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T03:45:53-07:00","id":1521967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521965#post1521965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others might find the maneuvers too complicated, but I didn\u2019t say anything like that. I said that the significant decisions are being made at the wrong times for what I want to do with the game.<br /> <br /> The maneuvers are certainly unnecessary, but the entire system is unnecessary. The question is never what game mechanics are necessary; it\u2019s always about what mechanics enhance the play experience. And that\u2019s why I asked my original questions: Do you use the maneuvers (especially the ones that aren\u2019t available to everyone by default), and if so what do you find they add to your game? Because the reality check for me is what my players will miss out on if I just ditch that aspect of M20.<br /> <br /> The timing issue isn\u2019t about how long players spend making decisions, it\u2019s about when they make those decisions. When a player writes a maneuver on their character sheet, that becomes an anchored expectation - we will probably see it used repeatedly. That decision tells us one thing - that the character has trained to use that maneuver. And when a player chooses a maneuver before the roll, it tells us another thing - that the character hopes to use that maneuver. But I don\u2019t much care about those decisions. I care about what the character hopes to achieve (not the move, the aim of the move) in the moment before the roll, and I care about what the character actually does in the moment after the roll. (Not just wherever the character succeeds or fails at using a particular move; I want to hear how the character makes the best of the situation if the roll gives less successes than what they hoped for; or how they utilize an unexpected opportunity if they get a great roll.) Those are the decisions I am more interested it hearing from my players.<br /> <br /> More simply, I don\u2019t want to hear about what might happen, so much as what does happen.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying you should want the same thing, or that the system is necessarily wrong in any particular way. Just that the maneuvers didn\u2019t seem to be fulfilling my objectives, and on consultation with the players they don\u2019t seem to fit their objectives either.</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer your question, I use manuvers, and I find they offer options to players during combat.<br /> <br /> I find it odd that your problem with combat in wod is that it follows the usual line of cause and effect.<br /> <br /> - you decide to do a thing<br /> - what you decide to do and how determines the dice pool and difficulty<br /> - the result of the roll determines the outcome<br /> <br /> every single roll in WoD works like this, with magic rolls being the most obvious of the lot, you don\u2019t even know what the difficulty of such a roll is until you\u2019ve decided what you effect is and what you do to achieve it, and you have no idea how the effect turns out until you see how many successes it garners.<br /> <br /> Instead, you suggest a system of<br /> <br /> - roll what the ST tells you to roll<br /> - see what happens<br /> - decide retroactively what it was you wanted to do.<br /> <br /> the major problems with this are 3 fold<br /> <br /> 1. The declaration round is entirely done away with, meaning you have no idea when it is best to go offensive, to dodge, or to protect another. The way combat is meant to work is those in higher initiative can decide what to do based on what those in lower initiative choose to do, so if you see slow but ultra powerful winding up a shot then you know you should defend. If instead you see your buddy is about to grapple them, you can get in to position to jab them after their turn. None of this happens if you only know what everyone is doing after they\u2019ve rolled. You have fewer options. It incentivise only offensive actions when rolls are high.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Rolls become less a series of decisions, and more a \u201clet the dice tell me how well I do\u201d system. There are no real tactics since tactics are based on when what you do may fail, you become less a fighter making decisions and more a narrator saying what your guy does based on how the dice roll. And as a result, combat becomes very trivial and meaningless. It also gives way to munchkiny behaviour since they can decide after they roll what it was they wanted to do in the first place. \u201coh, I only got 1 success? Ok, that\u2019s a dodge roll\u201d or \u201coh, I got 6 successes? Ok, make that a tackle, so they are hit for more damage and they are now knocked down\u201d To me, what you suggest is not dissimilar to spending willpower after making the roll. It entirely undermines the risk/reward nature of combat<br /> <br /> 3. How to handle Botches. Botch effects are very much determined by what it is the player was trying to do. If they were trying hit someone, they may be easier to hit, if they try to tackle, they might fall prone, if they attempting to grapple, they themselves become may become grappled.<br /> under your system, the botched roll becomes far more nebulous. Either you as ST decide what the player was trying to do and how it backfires, taking power away from you let your players choose what it was they did that botched, giving them all the power to underplay it to the point of triviality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T04:35:36-07:00","id":1521972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521967#post1521967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The declaration round is entirely done away with,</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no declaration round in M20, by rules as written. The WoD games don\u2019t share all their system details. Some games have a declaration round, others don\u2019t. M20 is one that doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> M20 asks for a declaration of intent before the attack made by the acting character (rather than everybody declaring their actions before anybody starts taking actions). And I intend to retain a similar declaration of intent. When I described my intended approach to combat for my upcoming game, I said this: \u201cI\u2019ll just get something brief and general as intent, and then if the player rolls a lot of successes, they can be pleasantly surprised, spend the successes for some desirable combination of effects, and describe a cool move that they think suits the degree of success rolled.\u200b\u201d<br /> <br /> But if I did want to use a reverse-initiative-order declaration round like some WoD games, that brief and general statement of intent would still serve to allow that.<br /> <br /> Everything else you\u2019re telling me will go wrong is based on that false assumption that there will be no indication of intent before a player rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T06:01:52-07:00","id":1521976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521972#post1521972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no declaration round in M20, by rules as written. The WoD games don\u2019t share all their system details. Some games have a declaration round, others don\u2019t. M20 is one that doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> M20 asks for a declaration of intent before the attack made by the acting character (rather than everybody declaring their actions before anybody starts taking actions). And I intend to retain a similar declaration of intent. When I described my intended approach to combat for my upcoming game, I said this: \u201cI\u2019ll just get something brief and general as intent, and then if the player rolls a lot of successes, they can be pleasantly surprised, spend the successes for some desirable combination of effects, and describe a cool move that they think suits the degree of success rolled.\u200b\u201d<br /> <br /> But if I did want to use a reverse-initiative-order declaration round like some WoD games, that brief and general statement of intent would still serve to allow that.<br /> <br /> Everything else you\u2019re telling me will go wrong is based on that false assumption that there will be no indication of intent before a player rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that M20 fully intended to include the declaration phase of action scenes, as evidenced by this line under defence: \u201cYou can declare a defensive maneuver at any point in your turn, so long as your character has an action left to perform that turn. If you had already declared a different action for that turn, the Storyteller may have you make a Willpower roll (difficulty 6), or else spend a Willpower point in order to change your character\u2019s mind in the blur of combat\u200b.\u201d<br /> <br /> under the system you state is raw, when would this circumstance ever come up that player would declare their action and then change their mind if they were to roll immediately after stating what they wish to do? It simply would never happen. Delaying lets you even delay the declaration wince going raw all you say is \u201cI save this action for later\u201d letting them declare at the time they wish to use the action. The only time I could imagine someone needing to roll wp to change their action is if they said something like \u201cI want to attack them\u2026wait\u2026hang on\u2026I\u2019ll defend myself instead.\u201d And I highly doubt this is what you are seriously intending was intended.<br /> <br /> indeed, every other modern 20th game runs it with reverse declaration in tact, leading me to conclude that this was a careless omission. Especially considering that all other times the book has intentionally changed something from previous editions, it discusses the change.<br /> <br /> now, regarding your specific house rule, if the player are still declaring what they wish to do before the roll, what exactly are you changing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T07:22:47-07:00","id":1521979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521976#post1521976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that M20 fully intended to include the declaration phase of action scenes,</div> </div> </div> </div>But the writers did not do that, and rules <i>as written</i> do need to be written. It\u2019s in the term. It doesn\u2019t matter how or why or what else the game designers considered, or even whether evidence of alternatives from earlier drafts was not edited out of the final draft.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I\u2019m not interested in remaining beholden to the rules as written. If I think something in the rules as written is not good for my game, I\u2019ll change it, and I encourage you to do the same. But neither of us can cite house rules to others as <i>the</i> rules of the game while contradicting the actual written rules.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure there\u2019s an older thread on this forum discussing the details of the lack of a declaration phase in M20, although it\u2019s possible I\u2019m thinking of one on rpg.net. You might want to see if you can track it down, if you\u2019re interested in that sort of thing. I lack the time for that debate now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521976#post1521976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now, regarding your specific house rule, if the player are still declaring what they wish to do before the roll, what exactly are you changing?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the declaration of intent is concerned, just the level of detail in the declaration. \u201cI will attack &lt;target&gt;, unarmed, attempting to inflict harm\u201d is enough detail. We\u2019re just leaving out whether the attack is a punch, kick, haymaker, spinning kick, death strike, or whichever of the other unarmed damaging maneuvers can be used under M20 RAW.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s enough to determine that the roll is Dex+Brawl/MA. The player makes the roll, and then describes their character\u2019s attack in a way that fits with the number of successes. A high number of successes may be a very well-placed punch, or it may be a spinning kick, or any of a large number of possible close combat moves. A single success could be a typical punch, or a fancy martial arts move that the target sees coming at the last second and moves enough to sustain merely a glancing blow. More narrative detail is added at this point.<br /> <br /> And to this point, this isn\u2019t really unusual. Mage: the Ascension existed for 20 years without having maneuvers in the core rulebook. That form of declaration was the default through three editions of the game.<br /> <br /> The only other change I\u2019m looking at is adding the option to turn extra successes into something other than bonus damage dice. So then a player might get a good roll, and decide that rather than just doing more damage, it would be cool for their character to, say, grab their target\u2019s arm and twist, inflicting injury and causing them to drop their gun - basic Strength dice of damage plus a disarm effect, But I haven\u2019t set the details on how those extra successes can buy those extra effects yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T09:17:05-07:00","id":1521984,"title":"","content":"First, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> , I make your words, mine. I agree with 100% you posted in this thread and I share you opinion and feeling that they are not making much sense in their complains.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> so, you are saying that the combat system is a mess, which you didn't quite made your point yet (we provided examples for the use of kicks), and then your solution is to simplify it so much to the point of not even having different difficulties?<br /> <br /> How would that be better?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a> , declaring &quot;I want to hurt him&quot; is not declaring an action. You *are* choosing the action itself retroactively and all the arguments Saikou made will indeed happen.<br /> <br /> The player is &quot;declaring&quot; a very, very basic description and then, after the rolls are made, they choose what *really* happens. It doesnt seems fair to get to choose your action after you know how much you have rolled.<br /> <br /> Now, if the ST (you) will choose what the action will in fact be, then you are removing freedom from the players: &quot;you wanted to hurt him and you got 5 successes. Ok, that will be a flying kick&quot;. But the player didn't choose to go with a flying kick. What if, instead, he wants to throw a punch, which is way safer for the attacker than a flying kick? Can't punches do 5 successes in damage?<br /> <br /> If you let the player choose what the action will be in fact (after rolling), then you are not removing any of the issues you posted before (the player will still have to choose from the list of attacks) AND you are adding more problems, as Saikou pointed out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 09-03-2023, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T09:48:27-07:00","id":1521988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521979#post1521979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the writers did not do that, and rules <i>as written</i> do need to be written. It\u2019s in the term. It doesn\u2019t matter how or why or what else the game designers considered, or even whether evidence of alternatives from earlier drafts was not edited out of the final draft.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I\u2019m not interested in remaining beholden to the rules as written. If I think something in the rules as written is not good for my game, I\u2019ll change it, and I encourage you to do the same. But neither of us can cite house rules to others as <i>the</i> rules of the game while contradicting the actual written rules.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure there\u2019s an older thread on this forum discussing the details of the lack of a declaration phase in M20, although it\u2019s possible I\u2019m thinking of one on rpg.net. You might want to see if you can track it down, if you\u2019re interested in that sort of thing. I lack the time for that debate now.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the declaration of intent is concerned, just the level of detail in the declaration. \u201cI will attack &lt;target&gt;, unarmed, attempting to inflict harm\u201d is enough detail. We\u2019re just leaving out whether the attack is a punch, kick, haymaker, spinning kick, death strike, or whichever of the other unarmed damaging maneuvers can be used under M20 RAW.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s enough to determine that the roll is Dex+Brawl/MA. The player makes the roll, and then describes their character\u2019s attack in a way that fits with the number of successes. A high number of successes may be a very well-placed punch, or it may be a spinning kick, or any of a large number of possible close combat moves. A single success could be a typical punch, or a fancy martial arts move that the target sees coming at the last second and moves enough to sustain merely a glancing blow. More narrative detail is added at this point.<br /> <br /> And to this point, this isn\u2019t really unusual. Mage: the Ascension existed for 20 years without having maneuvers in the core rulebook. That form of declaration was the default through three editions of the game.<br /> <br /> The only other change I\u2019m looking at is adding the option to turn extra successes into something other than bonus damage dice. So then a player might get a good roll, and decide that rather than just doing more damage, it would be cool for their character to, say, grab their target\u2019s arm and twist, inflicting injury and causing them to drop their gun - basic Strength dice of damage plus a disarm effect, But I haven\u2019t set the details on how those extra successes can buy those extra effects yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The raw is literally unworkable taken in full, that is how I conclude it must be written in error. That is why I bring up the text stating one must roll wp to change a declared action to a defensive one, something that only makes sense when there is a round of declaration. Either you need to ignore this passage, or you need to consider declaration is intended. Both would be deviations from strict RAW, but the latter option acknowledges everything that is written while the former ignores something that is written.p<br /> <br /> In any case, Combat manoeuvres have been around since 1st edition, with Flank, grapple, multiple opponents, and body slam being introduced in the first core book, they were referred to as \u2018complications\u2019 but they served the same role. Do Martial arts being introduced in 1st ed\u2019s book of shadows, 2e brought them back and added kick, bite, claw, acrobatic flip, disarm, escape, and blind foe. and revised is where they were first called combat manoeuvres, and including a load more such as clinch, close, jab pistol, blind fighting, sweep, tackle, block, parry, desperate defence, and weapon strike. And the revised akashic book added a whole load of Do related martial arts moves<br /> <br /> these manoeuvres have been a part of the system since its inception, with each edition adding more options for players to make use of, there isn\u2019t an iteration of the game run RAW that works as you state it does.<br /> <br /> And personally, I think your approach makes combat less risk reward and more power fantasy, and I think that takes away from the game, it\u2019s almost like removing botches from the system in terms of how it changes the tone of combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-03-2023, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T09:14:06-07:00","id":1522057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521984#post1521984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> so, you are saying that the combat system is a mess, which you didn't quite made your point yet (we provided examples for the use of kicks), and then your solution is to simplify it so much to the point of not even having different difficulties?<br /> <br /> How would that be better?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're conflating &quot;Difficulty&quot; the game term that sets the target number for the dice to count as success, with &quot;difficulty&quot; as in a method to represent that one option is harder to accomplish than another.<br /> <br /> This is not some new or radical concept. This was something done in the &quot;Storyteller Revised&quot; system that was the base of Trinity/Aeon/etc. 1e, Exalted, and Scion 1e: The target number to roll became a set number, and difficulty was measured in how many successes an action requires.<br /> <br /> One of the problems that's been an issue for the WoD since day one, is that there's too many variables for rolls: &quot;difficulty&quot; can come from dice-penalties, increased target numbers, or more required successes, and the books did not establish a function heuristic on which to use when. Combat, being the most mechanically intense part of the game, just highlights how little the base-line rules considered the complexity of having all three of those variables interact at the same time really is.<br /> <br /> It's better because it's easier to understand what your character can actually do, because you don't need university level mathematics to actually figuring out whether a combat option is worth using at all, or if it's situational what those situations actually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T08:05:39-07:00","id":1522098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522057#post1522057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're conflating &quot;Difficulty&quot; the game term that sets the target number for the dice to count as success, with &quot;difficulty&quot; as in a method to represent that one option is harder to accomplish than another.<br /> <br /> One of the problems that's been an issue for the WoD since day one, is that there's too many variables for rolls: &quot;difficulty&quot; can come from dice-penalties, increased target numbers, or more required successes, and the books did not establish a function heuristic on which to use when. Combat, being the most mechanically intense part of the game, just highlights how little the base-line rules considered the complexity of having all three of those variables interact at the same time really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In combat there are no required amount of successes and dice penalties are clearly stated (like the reach rule). By default, something being *harder* to do, means the Difficulty of the roll is higher than something easy. Having two actions with the same difficulty where one needs more successes than the other, means that the first should take more time and effort to be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522057#post1522057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's better because it's easier to understand what your character can actually do, because you don't need university level mathematics to actually figuring out whether a combat option is worth using at all, or if it's situational what those situations actually are.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. You still have to read and choose from the &quot;bloated&quot; list. You also don't need university level math, unless you really, REALLY, want to choose the best option possible. And that would apply for several mechanics within the system:<br /> <br /> Is it better to give yourself (magickally) bonus in dices or reduced difficulty?<br /> <br /> Well, that depends a lot. Normally, people do not care about the probabilities and go for either way. <br /> <br /> To me, you are creating problems that do not exist and providing a solution that is worse than the default rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T12:04:45-07:00","id":1522112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522098#post1522098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In combat there are no required amount of successes and dice penalties are clearly stated (like the reach rule).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you... really want me to spend an hour posting every example of this not being true?<br /> <br /> How about we just start with the most basic: Combat is based on resisted rolls. Attacks require more successes than successes rolled against them. Damage requires more successes than Soak successes. This isn't the CofD where normal combat is designed so a single success on an attack is always a hit and the rest is just figuring out what the hit actually did.<br /> <br /> You're treating &quot;required amount of successes&quot; as only apply to static numbers. They can be variables as well.<br /> <br /> Also, what's the dice penalty for having been out in extreme heat for an hour with high winds kicking up a lot of sand/dirt? If you say there isn't one, congrats, you've just proven these things aren't clearly stated because the opening of the combat chapter only talks about environmental hazards modifying difficulty, while the actual section on them says the modify dice pools and difficulties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By default, something being *harder* to do, means the Difficulty of the roll is higher than something easy. </div> </div> </div>Technically, by default, something harder to do because of &quot;external&quot; reasons increases Difficulty, but something harder to do for &quot;internal&quot; reasons results in a dice-penalty (like Wound Penalties). Though this rationale is a guideline at best since the book doesn't want different rules for characters that are blind via natural visual impairment (internal), and characters that are in pitch darkness without aid to see (external source of difficulty).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having two actions with the same difficulty where one needs more successes than the other, means that the first should take more time and effort to be done. </div> </div> </div>That's only true of Extended actions, and even then, you're presenting it out of line with the books. And Extended action at diff 6 that takes 10 successes with an interval of 5 minutes, is not supposed to take more time and effort than one with a diff of 6 that takes 5 success with an interval of a week. As the book notes, this is really about establishing dramatic tension under the assumption that something will impede the character. That is, most people with at least some basic training in the first task could do it if they had a spare hour to dedicate to it, and the reason for such a roll to exist is really for when the guards will be back in 15 minutes (and thus finishing in 1-2 rolls would be awesome, and 3 rolls would be good but pushing it, while 4 rolls would mean problems).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it's not. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You still have to read and choose from the &quot;bloated&quot; list. </div> </div> </div>What bloated list? The whole point of what travisjhall and I are talking about is getting rid of a giant list of specific maneuvers, and just having effects you buy with your successes. You don't need four different maneuvers that knock opponents prone, &quot;Knockdown&quot; is just an effect you buy with the successes you rolled (if you rolled enough). All maneuvers that only exist as descriptive difference are removed, and all maneuvers that only exist to combine multiple effects at increased costs are removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also don't need university level math, unless you really, REALLY, want to choose the best option possible. </div> </div> </div>Oh please, the sheer existence of 1s cancelling successes puts the WoD system math into 101 level Stats territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that would apply for several mechanics within the system: </div> </div> </div>Yes, the 20th edition books are continuations of the vastly outdated 30 year old ST systems that are in need of a serious overhaul in general. What's your point? Did my previous point not make it clear I feel this way about the whole system, not just combat? Did you think it was some rhetorical masterstroke to point out what I already said?<br /> <br /> Also, it's not just me given that every single system based on the original WoD system that's still being made has moved (not all in the same direction) away from these designs. Exalted 2e and onward - despite being a bloated mess in many other ways - has less variables and simpler base combat maneuvers/complications. Trinity Continuum 2e and Scion 2e both use the Storypath system where you roll your attack and then pick what effects you get based on your roll instead of having to declare specific moves first. WoD5 got rid of variable target numbers and uses successes as difficulty as well, and vastly reduced combat options.<br /> <br /> Nobody making games in this family of systems looks at this and says, &quot;yeah, that was good, we should keep that.&quot; They're all doing something else to try to do better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Normally, people do not care about the probabilities and go for either way. </div> </div> </div>Only because the probabilities in the cWoD rules are so opaque. D&amp;D is by no means a simply system, but it's very easy for people to handle the probability of picking between a option where you have a +15 bonus but the DC is 25, vs a +10 bonus, but a DC of 10; since you can just subtract your bonus from the DC, and the lower number is the one you're more likely to succeed at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, you are creating problems that do not exist and providing a solution that is worse than the default rules. </div> </div> </div>To me, you're just sticking your fingers in your ears and going, &quot;Na na na na na, I can't hear you so you must be wrong.,&quot; since you're not engaging with anything I'm actually saying.<br /> <br /> Or just go watch one of Onyx Path's many available videos of people playing a Storypath game where they get into combat so you can see how this sort of approach actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T13:03:46-07:00","id":1522116,"title":"","content":"I think a big deal is being made about very little here.<br /> <br /> the list of standard combat manoeuvres is actually quite short. And each one provides something the others do not.<br /> the dirty fighting menuevers expand the option, and each one of them contributes something new.<br /> <br /> and martial arts is the \u201cbuild your own fighter\u201d style of combat, not dissimilar to how dnd 5e fighters work.<br /> <br /> When it comes to calculation, I think this misses the wood for the trees. Much of the system gives you a feel for what is advantageous vs disadvantageous without giving you absolute certainty, any roll you make can be loaded with 1s, but more dice reduce this risk of it being a big problem, and lower diff reduce the chance it\u2019s a botch. But it can still happen, and there in lies the sense of uncertainty.<br /> <br /> failure is a major part of these game\u2019s DNA, I get the impression a reason people dismiss oWoD combat systrm is in part because they believe failure being a persistent thing is a failing of the system somehow.<br /> <br /> But I do not think this is the case at all, I believe the spectre of failure, and of botches, adds so much to the tone of the system that to do away with it or reduce it to the point of irrelevance takes away from the experience.<br /> <br /> this is why the magic system being based on Arete is a crucial design point of Mage, it is built on the idea that failure is likely, paradox builds with each roll leading up to a botch, and so the threat of a botch as difficulty climbs with each attempt to keep rolling for more successes possibly the roll that leads to your downfall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:27:10-07:00","id":1522127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522116#post1522116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big deal is being made about very little here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no requirement to participate in the thread if the goal isn't something you care about.<br /> <br /> Also, you're making a very big deal of trying to be the one that's &quot;right&quot; even when nothing you're saying is actually on point. You don't get to decide which details other people find worth the time and energy to refine in the system. If you don't care, why are you even bothering? If you do care, why can't you come up with something to say that isn't just dismissive bullshit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the list of standard combat manoeuvres is actually quite short. And each one provides something the others do not. </div> </div> </div>The list is artificially short because the book has multiple overlapping lists. The Defense maneuvers are in their own list. The &quot;status effect&quot; stuff like being stunned or prone are in one list, while flanking is in the general hand-to-hand list, and targeted attacks are their own separate thing as well.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the general hand-to-hand list is also bloated almost nothing added for the number of options. Claw, bite, punch, kick, and grapple could be reduced to two moves: strike and grapple (with bite being split between strike and grapple depending on what kind of bite you can do). Claw/bite/punch/kick are all just &quot;hit someone with a part of your body,&quot; with slightly tweaked difficulties, damage bonuses, and damage types. None of this requires four moves. It you really value differentiation here, it would be better handled with a single strike move, and a natural weapons section instead of clogging up the moves with such minor variations. Disarm and sweep can just be part of the targeted attack option; disarming is literally an example of a bonus effect of a successful targeted attack already. The idea that you can sweep someone for no damage it also fairly silly. The low risk of damage to a health adult is already covered by it being bashing damage. Tackle can easily be folded into Grapple as a third option to Clinch and Hold where you end the grapple to send a target prone on your turn, and those simply tackle rather unnecessary amount of rolling. Flanking should be with ambushed/immobilized/etc.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;quite short&quot; list is now four moves instead of ten: strike, grapple, reading opponent (though that's a trap pick as written, and you could just let people aim hand-to-hand attacks if you wanted to not have to different systems for spending an action to get bonus dice on your next one), and targeted attacks. Three if targeted moves to a different thing since it works for Ranged too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the dirty fighting menuevers expand the option, and each one of them contributes something new. </div> </div> </div>Blinding is just a targeted attack, Body Slam is just extra damage in a Clinch and the permission to turn damage lethal when it makes sense narratively (which is silly, because it means you can't upgrade a normal Clinch's damage even if it would make sense to, like using Forces to make yourself immune to fire, and grappling someone to keep them inside a burning building), Curbstomp has the same issues as Body Slam but you don't start with a grapple (if you drag someone over to a pile of broken glass, and then punch their head into the glass, wouldn't you upgrade that to lethal without needing Brawl 3?), Haymaker is actually good but it's just what the normal kick should have been, Headbutts offer a mighty +1 damage over a normal strike at ridiculous risk, Low Blow is just a targeted attack again, Pistol Whip is just using an improvised weapon but is good because it does lethal even with weapons that don't normally do lethal (which is then very confusing because that doesn't make any sense why Brawl 3 lets you upgrade the damage of Melee attacks with improvised weapons). Pistol Jab is the only one that actually does something special in a good way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> martial arts is the \u201cbuild your own fighter\u201d style of combat, not dissimilar to how dnd 5e fighters work. </div> </div> </div>Any similarities to how D&amp;D 5e fighters work doesn't really address how much the moves are bloat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to calculation, I think this misses the wood for the trees. </div> </div> </div>More dismissive BS to disguise not having a point...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much of the system gives you a feel for what is advantageous vs disadvantageous... </div> </div> </div>No, it really doesn't in a meaningful way. Yes, more dice good/less dice bad, lower diff good/higher diff bad, less successes needed good/more successes need bad. But the relative values of each? The game offers nothing to help you. Which is entirely why things like the normal Kick move sucks. Since players have no idea how to value +1 diff vs. +1 damage die, they have no idea why it's stupid to use the Kick move unless you absolutely have to. If you can get bonuses without a trade off? Sure, duh, take the bonus. But once trade offs come into play, the game is woefully insufficient in communicating advantage and disadvantage. Again, this goes back to what I already said: there's too many variables for each action for people to get their heads around without some fairly complex math.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> failure is a major part of these game\u2019s DNA, I get the impression a reason people dismiss oWoD combat systrm is in part because they believe failure being a persistent thing is a failing of the system somehow. </div> </div> </div>I dismissing the oWoD combat system because I haven't actually lost a combat as a PC in over 10 years because I've long since figure out how not to fail.<br /> <br /> Failure is built into the system in an very unfun way: by making traps in the rules that players fall for easily. Once you learn the traps and how to avoid them, combat is easy to win, if cheesy and boring. There's nothing fun about failing because the system tricked you. Failing is fun when the game rewards you in the long run for it and is clear about that. People don't have fun because they lost a fight (or potentially even a character) because they picked the wrong move off the list by picking what sounded good instead of what was mechanically right for their goals.<br /> <br /> Doing your best and failing is a very different experience than failing because the game is rigged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I do not think this is the case at all, I believe the spectre of failure, and of botches, adds so much to the tone of the system that to do away with it or reduce it to the point of irrelevance takes away from the experience. </div> </div> </div>And yet, we're talking about mages... pretty much the best splat in the entire WoD at succeeding at everything but magic itself. The ability to drop a -3 diff on pretty much any roll makes mundane failures vanishingly rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this is why the magic system being based on Arete is a crucial design point of Mage, it is built on the idea that failure is likely, paradox builds with each roll leading up to a botch, and so the threat of a botch as difficulty climbs with each attempt to keep rolling for more successes possibly the roll that leads to your downfall. </div> </div> </div>This is why Mage the Awakening completely redid all of this so it actually accomplishes what you say you want, where Ascension doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T18:22:20-07:00","id":1522130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have no requirement to participate in the thread if the goal isn't something you care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy talking about mechanics. I wasn't aware a more in depth reason was required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, you're making a very big deal of trying to be the one that's &quot;right&quot; even when nothing you're saying is actually on point. You don't get to decide which details other people find worth the time and energy to refine in the system. If you don't care, why are you even bothering? If you do care, why can't you come up with something to say that isn't just dismissive bullshit?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no interest in being right, I only wish to understand and be understood. I do not understand the necessity of these changes, and to illustrate this I am trying to explain how I use the mechanics as presented, and why I think they work very well. And that is in fact what has been requested for in the very title of the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The list is artificially short because the book has multiple overlapping lists. The Defense maneuvers are in their own list. The &quot;status effect&quot; stuff like being stunned or prone are in one list, while flanking is in the general hand-to-hand list, and targeted attacks are their own separate thing as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the problem here. There are only three defensive maneuvers, one for melee, two for brawl, one of which is active while the other is reactive. They are not all that difficult to recall, nor do they really bog the game down. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile the general hand-to-hand list is also bloated almost nothing added for the number of options. Claw, bite, punch, kick, and grapple could be reduced to two moves: strike and grapple (with bite being split between strike and grapple depending on what kind of bite you can do). Claw/bite/punch/kick are all just &quot;hit someone with a part of your body,&quot; with slightly tweaked difficulties, damage bonuses, and damage types. None of this requires four moves. It you really value differentiation here, it would be better handled with a single strike move, and a natural weapons section instead of clogging up the moves with such minor variations. Disarm and sweep can just be part of the targeted attack option; disarming is literally an example of a bonus effect of a successful targeted attack already. The idea that you can sweep someone for no damage it also fairly silly. The low risk of damage to a health adult is already covered by it being bashing damage. Tackle can easily be folded into Grapple as a third option to Clinch and Hold where you end the grapple to send a target prone on your turn, and those simply tackle rather unnecessary amount of rolling. Flanking should be with ambushed/immobilized/etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Claw and bite are specifically for Life 3 altered body mages, the options are there to give you something quick to use if you give yourself claws or teeth. It' basically punch, but with other body parts, inoffensive and not really bloat as I see it. You could probably put these options under the Life 3 section of the game, but honestly having all the combat relevant bits together makes sense for ease of location. <br /> <br /> In honesty your main complaint here seems to be in the way the information is displayed rather than in how the game actually operates, which is a different complaint to the one I thought you were making predominately. Whether each move is given as a different attack option or as a variation of a single attack, the point remains that the options are available. And for all intents and purposes, the table summarising these attack options does just that.<br /> <br /> Regarding your complaint with sweep, remember that you can use multiple actions if you want to strike immediately after getting them prone. But to be fair, being swept of your feet like that doesn't really hurt all that much, unless you have impaired reflexed you can catch yourself fairly easily, and I've experienced that first hand a few times, so I don't find it all that silly.<br /> <br /> Disarm does come with its own measure of success, that being gaining successes exceeding the opponents strength, and that the feat is more difficult for brawl, which is enough to warrant specific mention.<br /> <br /> Tackle and Grapple do two different things and have different starting requirements. To grapple you must be within reach of your opponent, while tackle requires having space to run up to them. In close quarters, only one of these options is possible. That and the way grapple resolves and Tackle resolves are also quite different, with a grapple opponent resisitng by their own strength and brawl roll, or possibly dex and acrobatics instead, with the grappler able to inflict bashing damage if they maintain their hold. tackle instead is two seperate rolls, one to hit and one to knock down, the first is a standard dex and brawl, while the second is a contested dex and athletics, with the difficulty reduced for the defending party depending on how goo the initial attack roll was. Not to mention the result is that they become knocked down rather than grappled. As such I fail to see how it makes any sense to fold these moves in to one another.<br /> <br /> Your comment on flanking is, again, a question of how information is displayed rather than what options are available, which I reiterate because that is the actual focus of the thread, less about how the information is displayed, and more about the necessity of the options provided.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your &quot;quite short&quot; list is now four moves instead of ten: strike, grapple, reading opponent (though that's a trap pick as written, and you could just let people aim hand-to-hand attacks if you wanted to not have to different systems for spending an action to get bonus dice on your next one), and targeted attacks. Three if targeted moves to a different thing since it works for Ranged too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In theory you could write it in such a way that all these moves were combined together as you describe, but they would have to have so many options attached to them to inform how and when they apply as well as what changes within the difficulty or how the opponent responds that in the end, it doesn't actually change very much. form 10 mid to short paragraphs you get 4 rather long paragraphs. and if you consider grapple is already on the long side as it is, I don't think adding to its length with extra options just to cut down on the overall move count really achieves much in the way of clear communication.<br /> <br /> For the rest of this sentence, I'm not entirely sure what you are suggesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blinding is just a targeted attack, Body Slam is just extra damage in a Clinch and the permission to turn damage lethal when it makes sense narratively (which is silly, because it means you can't upgrade a normal Clinch's damage even if it would make sense to, like using Forces to make yourself immune to fire, and grappling someone to keep them inside a burning building), Curbstomp has the same issues as Body Slam but you don't start with a grapple (if you drag someone over to a pile of broken glass, and then punch their head into the glass, wouldn't you upgrade that to lethal without needing Brawl 3?), Haymaker is actually good but it's just what the normal kick should have been, Headbutts offer a mighty +1 damage over a normal strike at ridiculous risk, Low Blow is just a targeted attack again, Pistol Whip is just using an improvised weapon but is good because it does lethal even with weapons that don't normally do lethal (which is then very confusing because that doesn't make any sense why Brawl 3 lets you upgrade the damage of Melee attacks with improvised weapons). Pistol Jab is the only one that actually does something special in a good way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All of the dirty fighting moves are moves that require more conviction than others, this is why they are on this list as it is implied that the average brawler (brawl 1-2) would simply not have the experience of wherewithal to commit to these moves. In the same way that an average level of Awareness doesn't let you be sensitive enough to sense auras.<br /> <br /> Regarding Body Slam, I really don't think that implication is accurate. None of the maneuvers take in to account environmental damage or use of magic, and I think it is somewhat disingenous to argue that because damage is upgraded in this instance, that one can then conclude the intent is that in no other context and damage be upgraded. The idea is that with Brawl 3, you can now do these things which upgrade the damage without needing glass, magic, fire, or whatever other external factors, you can do it with brawl alone. Headbutts are for when you are otherwise immobilised, similar to kicks, less strategic and more when you have little else. You can, for example, headbutt someone who has your arms immobalised in a grapple. The option is there for one to use when the need comes up.<br /> <br /> Lowblow is a targeted attack, but it adds information the stamina roll to avoid being stunned, something unique to this move. Usually stunning is something that you don't roll to defend against, it's just what happens if you receive more damage than you have stamina. And this is an exception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any similarities to how D&amp;D 5e fighters work doesn't really address how much the moves are bloat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was more an attempt to illustrate that these were not extra options that one had to sift through while choosing what to do this turn, but build options for your martial artist. The moves are there for you to create your own signature fighting style within the games system. Completely ignorable if you don't wish to delve in to martial arts type builds. To me this seems no more offensive than a spell list. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More dismissive BS to disguise not having a point...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... dismissive is the entire tone of your response so... pot calling the kettle black?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it really doesn't in a meaningful way. Yes, more dice good/less dice bad, lower diff good/higher diff bad, less successes needed good/more successes need bad. But the relative values of each? The game offers nothing to help you. Which is entirely why things like the normal Kick move sucks. Since players have no idea how to value +1 diff vs. +1 damage die, they have no idea why it's stupid to use the Kick move unless you absolutely have to. If you can get bonuses without a trade off? Sure, duh, take the bonus. But once trade offs come into play, the game is woefully insufficient in communicating advantage and disadvantage. Again, this goes back to what I already said: there's too many variables for each action for people to get their heads around without some fairly complex math.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, that is how I view the Kick move, it's a move you use because you are otherwise demobalised or your arms are unable to work. The move is there so that if a player needs to kick, there is a quick way to see how to resolve it. I don't these moves need to be more than that. But in all honesty, if you can reduce the difficulty on your kick magically, then it does become the better option, and with willpower included, it's simply more damage. So what you put in to the attack can indeed make it viable as a strategy depending on the situation.<br /> <br /> Regarding the idea that there are too many variables. I don't really see that as an inherently bad thing. Much of the storyteller system is designed around the idea of making the story and using the mechanics to define how that story beat resolves. You want to try and hit him? Here is how hitting people is resolved. You want to try grappling him? Here is how grappling people is resolved. Wanting to only ever play the &quot;best option&quot; is what I mean when I say one is missing the woods for the trees, a comment you dismissed as merely dismissive. I mean that perfect calculation of odds is not what this combat system is for, and to be angry at it for not being that is sort of like being angry at a calculator for not being a computer. It's simply not designed nor intended for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dismissing the oWoD combat system because I haven't actually lost a combat as a PC in over 10 years because I've long since figure out how not to fail.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Without knowing what your winning strategy is, I can only assume you have rather kind STs managing your combat encounters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failure is built into the system in an very unfun way: by making traps in the rules that players fall for easily. Once you learn the traps and how to avoid them, combat is easy to win, if cheesy and boring. There's nothing fun about failing because the system tricked you. Failing is fun when the game rewards you in the long run for it and is clear about that. People don't have fun because they lost a fight (or potentially even a character) because they picked the wrong move off the list by picking what sounded good instead of what was mechanically right for their goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All I can say is that I don't share this experience. The combats I have run and remember as players tend to be more focused on resolving the issue than about getting the most damage in. Oftern time my players find that running away is the best option, other times it's about distracting the threat so that others have enough time to finish what they are doing. I've even had &quot;combat&quot; which wasn't even about fighting, all the players were rushing in to deal with a scenario at once. If you're interested I can tell you this scenario, but I am getting the impression that you have lost all patience with me quite some time ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doing your best and failing is a very different experience than failing because the game is rigged.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't understand what you mean when you say it is rigged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, we're talking about mages... pretty much the best splat in the entire WoD at succeeding at everything but magic itself. The ability to drop a -3 diff on pretty much any roll makes mundane failures vanishingly rare.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If this is an Entropy effect you are referring to, then I would say you need to keep in mind that Entropy magic has a way of coming back to hit the mage later down the line. But I feel that is a different discussion. I only bring it up to state that such things need not be solved situations if properly considered by the ST<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522127#post1522127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why Mage the Awakening completely redid all of this so it actually accomplishes what you say you want, where Ascension doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> ehhh.... I found much of the chronicles system lacking in that regard actually. The opt in nature of botches being a particular sore point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T23:05:27-07:00","id":1522138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522130#post1522130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy talking about mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you keep avoiding the actual mechanics involved in all of this for other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wasn't aware a more in depth reason was required. </div> </div> </div>The OP has specified as specific design goal you and Lord Revan kept arguing against for no perceivable reason other than it not being the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no interest in being right, I only wish to understand and be understood. </div> </div> </div>I don't believe you, because you don't demonstrate any actual attempt to understand what the changes accomplish. You also aren't actually making a case to be understood on the flip side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not understand the necessity of these changes, </div> </div> </div>None of this is a matter of necessity. These are games. Some of us want rules that work differently. That's all the &quot;necessity&quot; required.<br /> <br /> The desire/motivation is a system where the decision on what your attack accomplished comes after you see how well the roll did, rather than having to declare all the specifics of your attack before you roll anything.<br /> <br /> This is to give players more descriptive freedom because you don't have mechanics attacked to specifics (punches, kicks, haymakers, etc.), so a light hit can be described as anything from a basic jab to a big attack that grazed and so on, and turns one complex decision point into two simpler decision points with more guidance from the system and dice on what to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand the problem here. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say there was a distinct problem with the book. I was pointing out a problem with your argument. You call the list short, so I illustrated how artificial that distinction is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It' basically punch, but with other body parts, inoffensive and not really bloat as I see it. </div> </div> </div>This is pretty telling to how little you care about &quot;understanding.&quot; You might as well have just posted, &quot;Yeah, this is obviously bloat, but I don't care because the only thing to understand is that the RAW for M20 are the best.&quot;<br /> <br /> So much of this is just, &quot;We need five moves that are 99% the same in function because that 1% is vital for reasons I can't explain, but without it the game would be ruined.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In honesty your main complaint here seems to be in the way the information is displayed rather than in how the game actually operates, which is a different complaint to the one I thought you were making predominately. </div> </div> </div>No, my main complaint is the actual rules. However you an Revan are using the organization of the rules as part of your arguments, so I'm addressing that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding your complaint with sweep, remember that you can use multiple actions if you want to strike immediately after getting them prone. </div> </div> </div>That has nothing to do with my comment on how sweeps shouldn't do zero damage and just automatically knock people prone. People end up with strains and minor breaks from falls less serious than a sweep all the time. An unexpected sweep is especially dangerous to hitting the head on hard surfaces. The idea that you can catch yourself, or not, is why it should be an attack with a risk of damage. As it is, there's no room for a frail Stamina 1 person to break their hip when you sweep them. So if you don't find that the rules let you go around sweeping old people and never injure them in the process... I'm not sure what you think you have to add to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such I fail to see how it makes any sense to fold these moves in to one another. </div> </div> </div>I fail to see what reciting the RAW in more detail does to defend the RAW, or why this sort of weaksauce is supposed to make my less dismissive of your poor argumentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your comment on flanking is, again, a question of how information is displayed rather than what options are available, which I reiterate because that is the actual focus of the thread, less about how the information is displayed, and more about the necessity of the options provided. </div> </div> </div>Well, since we're reiterating:<br /> <br /> <b>I'M NOT THE ONE THAT MADE THE NUMBER OF GENERAL MANEUVERS PART OF HIS ARGUMENT.</b><br /> <br /> Yes, I have been talking a lot about bloat, but bloat is when the options are redundant and superfluous, not just that there are a bunch of them. If there are 10 moves an each actually does something valuable, that's fine. If there's 10 moves and you can compress them to four without losing anything valuable, there's bloat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In theory you could write it in such a way that all these moves were combined together as you describe, but they would have to have so many options attached to them to inform how and when they apply as well as what changes within the difficulty or how the opponent responds that in the end, it doesn't actually change very much. form 10 mid to short paragraphs you get 4 rather long paragraphs. and if you consider grapple is already on the long side as it is, I don't think adding to its length with extra options just to cut down on the overall move count really achieves much in the way of clear communication. </div> </div> </div>Prove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the rest of this sentence, I'm not entirely sure what you are suggesting. </div> </div> </div>I said you could summarize the 10 general hand-to-hand rules into 4, but included targeted attacks to cover some of them. Since targeted attacks aren't specific to hand-to-hand combat, you could call the list 3 instead with the understanding that targeted is still there for more options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of the dirty fighting moves are moves that require more conviction than others,... </div> </div> </div>Why does &quot;conviction&quot; let you punch people harder (and why wouldn't that just be spending WP on your attack)? Besides the fact that the book doesn't say that. The book says, &quot;The following collection of brutal blows demands at least three dots in the Brawl Ability, plus a background that includes such dirty tricks (gang membership, violent neighborhood, rape-prevention classes, and so on).&quot; No mention of conviction or a particularly unique mindset that only a select few can achieve.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding Body Slam, I really don't think that implication is accurate. </div> </div> </div>Are you reading the book? It says, &quot;The impact typically inflicts bashing damage; if the surface happens to be sharp, spiked, or incredibly hot, however, such injuries might be lethal instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Body Slam lets you upgrade damage to lethal if the situation provides something to slam them into that would be more dangerous than usual. Grapple doesn't have that stipulation. That's basically the only thing Body Slam does beyond +2 &quot;conviction&quot; damage.<br /> <br /> This is what we refer to as an Air Breathing Mermaid problem. Until Body Slam comes into the picture, it seems perfectly natural to let Clinches do lethal damage if there's something in the environment you can use your grapple control to press the target into. When Body Slam is introduced, suddenly you need Body Slam to get that advantage per the RAW, as Body Slam has that caveat, but Grapple doesn't. Letting Clinches to lethal damage by taking advantage of environmental factors suddenly becomes a house rule instead of common sense thanks to Body Slam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...no other context and damage be upgraded. </div> </div> </div>Not &quot;no other,&quot; but only specified rules since you've created the RAW that it requires exceptions to the general rule of Clinches doing bashing. You can bite for lethal in Clinches if you have a lethal bite because that exception is already explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea is that with Brawl 3, you can now do these things which upgrade the damage without needing glass, magic, fire, or whatever other external factors, you can do it with brawl alone. </div> </div> </div>Since I already quoted that you're explicitly wrong about Body Slam, onto Curbstomp: &quot;An ugly way of rearranging someone\u2019s face involves propping said face against a curb or other hard surface...&quot; Note, again, that the move explicitly requires appropriate external surfaces. You can't, under the RAW, use Curbstomp on someone when fighting in a pile of loose dirt. You need the leverage of a sufficiently hard surface to get the extra damage and upgrade to lethal.<br /> \u200b<br /> It helps to know the RAW if you're going to defend them. If you're defending your house rules... that's a very different story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Headbutts are for when you are otherwise immobilised, similar to kicks, less strategic and more when you have little else. </div> </div> </div>No, that's when those moves are useful in the system when you understand the mechanics. What the book says is that headbutts are for surprise heavy hit at some risk to your own head that gets you +1 damage for your effects.<br /> <br /> The fact that it's only useful if you don't have any other options is a side effect of knowing how the rules work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can, for example, headbutt someone who has your arms immobalised in a grapple. </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. If you're immobilized by a Grapple you can't attack the person grappling you. You can only roll to break free, or reverse, or as implied in other places take non-physical actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was more an attempt to illustrate that these were not extra options that one had to sift through while choosing what to do this turn, but build options for your martial artist. </div> </div> </div>Except you &quot;build your martial artist&quot; by adding more and more options to pick from each combat round. And this doesn't address things like there being moves in the MA list that are exactly the same except for one being for any martial artist, and the other only being for hard stylists. You're not telling me what Snap Kick adds to the game by being there, as it's completely redundant. It doesn't help you &quot;build your own style&quot; because you can already do that with Elbow/Knee Strike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me this seems no more offensive than a spell list. </div> </div> </div>Vancian spell lists are trash game design and only justifiable in games that want to emulate D&amp;D (or emulate games emulating D&amp;D like making a Final Fantasy I RPG would be). WotC only keeps them because the fans will rebel if they change anything consider to fundamental to the D&amp;D experience.<br /> <br /> And, of course, this is completely pointless argumentation. &quot;You can ignore this if you don't want to play a martial artist, just like you can ignore this if you don't want to play a D&amp;D spellcaster,&quot; doesn't defend these mechanics at all for the people that want to use these things and finds them negative aspects of the games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In all honesty, that is how I view the Kick move,... </div> </div> </div>Where does <b>the book</b> say this? The book doesn't. You're saying this because you know the Kick move is bad. But you're bending over backwards to defend it instead of acknowledging it doesn't have to be there. A &quot;strike&quot; move that covers any unarmed attack lets you kick when your arms aren't available. And there's no inherently increase in the difficulty of a kick if you can't move your arms, so that penalty should be coming from the source of your lack of arm movement (if any). If you have two broken arms, you're kicks are going to suck from the pain (we have Wound Penalties just for this purpose!), rather than having a shitty Kick specific move just for when you can't punch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really see that as an inherently bad thing. </div> </div> </div>It makes the odds of rolls too opaque for players to adequately assess their chances, and make informed decisions about what their character would do. You can't say, &quot;My character is a flashy go for broke kinda fighter, and will take high-risk high-reward strategies over low risk low reward strategies,&quot; if you can't easily assess levels or risk and levels of reward (and especially if a move is low risk/high reward, or high risk/low reward to add to complications since low risk/high reward tactics will just dominate combat and make it boring, and high risk/low reward will never get used unless contrived into the narrative).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much of the storyteller system is designed around the idea of making the story and using the mechanics to define how that story beat resolves. You want to try and hit him? Here is how hitting people is resolved. You want to try grappling him? Here is how grappling people is resolved. </div> </div> </div>Why does the game need three different methods of bonus/penalties to accomplish this? What does having so many add?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wanting to only ever play the &quot;best option&quot; is what I mean when I say one is missing the woods for the trees, a comment you dismissed as merely dismissive. </div> </div> </div>It's dismissive and dismissed because it's a strawman. I never said anything of the sort. I don't enjoy cWoD combat because I've mastered it, and it's not fun unless I purposefully handicap myself. I don't want that. That's the state I find myself in though. You say you don't like the CofD opt-in dramatic failure mechanics? Well that's what doing anything but optimized combat in the cWoD is for me: purposefully picking shitty moves I know are shitty for the sake of the story. But I don't get XP for it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile I have other systems that don't get boring once you actually understand the mechanics to use, so I think it's better to house rule the cWoD games to better combat systems if not switch over to other systems fully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean that perfect calculation of odds is not what this combat system is for, and to be angry at it for not being that is sort of like being angry at a calculator for not being a computer. It's simply not designed nor intended for that. </div> </div> </div>Cite a single sentence where I got angry over not being able to perform &quot;perfect calculations,&quot; or get a fucking real good apology ready for your bad faith crap.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise, you're just further admitting the whole &quot;I just want to understand and be understood,&quot; bit is a lie. There's an obvious middle ground between &quot;I need perfect calculations to have fun,&quot; and, &quot;The game should require three spreadsheets and university level stats to figure out if a punch or a kick if the approximate better option.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without knowing what your winning strategy is, I can only assume you have rather kind STs managing your combat encounters. </div> </div> </div>Wow, ad hominem at my STs, real classy.<br /> <br /> Yeah, my STs were &quot;kind&quot; not to attack my PCs with a tank battalion and jet fighter air support.or other such, &quot;I'm the ST, I can always win because I can fiat in bigger and badder enemies than you&quot; stuff. <br /> <br /> My &quot;strategy&quot; is pretty simple: fight pragmatically and focus on the practical (stealth, range, and guns to start whenever possible). Like people that fight in life or death situations do all as a matter of survival. Flashy shit gets you killed in fights to the death. Boring wins because boring is what works the best; that's why people want unrealistic combat in action moves where impractical shit is allowed to work better than standard boring combat moves. Mechanically? Prioritize Dex, difficulty bonuses/avoiding difficulty penalties, other dice adders, other damage adders, increasing damage type. I've one-shot vampires with guns without magic, people get way to cocky abut soaking bashing/lethal and thinking Agg is king because of Garou and Gangrel with claws. This isn't the CofD where there are slats that don't take wound penalties from lesser damage types, or creatures that can heal all bashing/lethal damage in a turn.. Massive bashing or lethal damage attacks are generally better than small agg damage attacks (or agg damage attacks that risk easy counter attacks). I once had a mage that averaged 12 damage levels (not dice) with his Trinket (in M20 terms) rifle. Not many thing can manage soak pools big enough to do anything about that.<br /> <br /> Countersnipers are a problem of course, but again, unless the ST is just tossing in one to kill you instead of making this an actual fight to roll out, you use you magic to keep yourself safe from that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The combats I have run and remember as players tend to be more focused on resolving the issue than about getting the most damage in. Oftern time my players find that running away is the best option, other times it's about distracting the threat so that others have enough time to finish what they are doing. I've even had &quot;combat&quot; which wasn't even about fighting, all the players were rushing in to deal with a scenario at once. If you're interested I can tell you this scenario, but I am getting the impression that you have lost all patience with me quite some time ago. </div> </div> </div>It would help my patience if you cut out the damned assumptions. You read &quot;never lost a fight&quot; and think I mean, &quot;I always did the most damage.&quot; No. Retreat is a win if my character is under attack and isn't defending an important thing they can't carry off with them. Winning means &quot;accomplished my objectives.&quot; Whatever those were. Yeah, I've been in some more action heavy games, and that meant killing NPCs, but that also means things like the time one of my mages ended a fight that looking like it was going to be a big boss battle sort of thing in the first turn by encasing the icky monster in granite in one (vulgar) roll with Matter 3/Prime 2. You might notice how little value I put on damage itself in my priority list above for winning in combat. Because it's the most limited in what it can accomplish. Broad competency lets you do lots of things to win. Avoiding fights you don't need to get in helps your win record a lot too, because there's always the chance the dice screw you, so don't get in fights unless you have to.<br /> <br /> If your real want to understand, listen to what I say. Don't assume thing I'm not saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't understand what you mean when you say it is rigged. </div> </div> </div>The books tell you to focus on story and narrative, and to use the rules to be a neutral arbiter of your attempts. But the rules aren't neutral. They're full of traps and tricks that make some characters and some choices unexpectedly bad, and others unfairly good. I can win so handily because I've studied the system in enough detail that I can reliably pick the unfairly good option on demand. The system is rigged against players without significant mastery of its intricacies in directly conflict with it's desire to be a more story driven game, because picking the good for the story options are in opposition to picking the good for the mechanics options, instead of being in alignment with each other. If players follow the advice of the book to focus on the narrative and be loose with the mechanics, they fall into the traps. That's what I mean by it being rigged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I only bring it up to state that such things need not be solved situations if properly considered by the ST </div> </div> </div>You're just shifting the goal posts. You were going on about how &quot;failing&quot; is part of the &quot;DNA&quot; of the system, and how we're supposed to fail all the time and that's supposed to be fun... when mages are really good at succeeding. This isn't about ruining the ST's plans by getting a great Investigation roll or something, it's just... it's very silly to think mages fail and mundane rolls frequently if they're putting any effort into it.<br /> <br /> Where is this failure so essential to the system, when mages are so easily capable of making themselves highly competent at mundane tasks? Don't change the subject to things like whether or not the problem is &quot;solved.&quot; If the problem can be solved with one good mundane roll, it wasn't much of a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ehhh.... I found much of the chronicles system lacking in that regard actually. The opt in nature of botches being a particular sore point. </div> </div> </div>I'll take Reach over Vulgarity as a way to push mages into hubris and dangerous magic any day. Ascension's risk/rewards favor subtle so much that players don't even take low risk vulgar chances. Awakening 2e's Reach system actually tempts you with enough power that a few Paadox dice don't seem like a big risk at all (and it's not at first, which is what makes such power tempting instead of acts of desperation like so many Ascension players treat magic with high Paradox risks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T23:19:58-07:00","id":1522141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522138#post1522138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe you,</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I see little benefit to you in maintaining this communication.<br /> <br /> If you have decided I am arguing in bad faith, then nothing I say will be of any value to you.<br /> That doesn\u2019t really leave me with anywhere to go.<br /> <br /> from my effort, I have tried to address your concerns by explaining how I approach this problem, and while your counters contain valid points that I would have addressed, the tone of contempt is impossible to ignore here.<br /> <br /> I get the distinct impression you do not want me to retort, you simply want me to be wrong and go away.<br /> <br /> I assure you that I am responding to your points in thr best manner that I can. I am sorry to have insulted you by presumption, but I assure you there is no malice involved. These presumptions are the honest impression I have gotten from the retorts you provide me, not a means to dismiss. I very much welcome being corrected on where my impressions fall short.<br /> <br /> I do believe I understand your position. You believe that the combat system fails because:<br /> <br /> - the options do not provide a meaningful set of choices<br /> - this is because the choices presented do not alter the outcome in any meaningful way beyond base attacks or not attacking at all<br /> - as a result, every option is just bloat<br /> <br /> do feel welcome to amend this if a crucial point is missed or requires further focus.<br /> <br /> I hoped I was able to address why this is not how I viewed the system, and why I believed that the system does indeed enable engaging combat in part because of the choices presented, but it does seem quite clear I have failed to explain myself adequately. And now you are more intent in trying to catch me out and prove me wrong than to actually understand my position.<br /> <br /> It is disheartening to see this though, I would have hopped you\u2019d provide me the same measures of respect you expect I give you. I understand you are to hurt by what you see as assumptions to avoid falling in to assumptions yourself, and I do apologise for causing that hurt.<br /> <br /> if you are done with me, then I can abide. But if you would genuinely desire my retort, then I can provide it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-06-2023, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T03:14:52-07:00","id":1522149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522138#post1522138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe you,</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I see little benefit to you in maintaining this communication.<br /> <br /> If you have decided I am arguing in bad faith, then nothing I say will be of any value to you.<br /> That doesn\u2019t really leave me with anywhere to go.<br /> <br /> For my part, I have tried to address your concerns by explaining how I approach this problem, and while your counters contain valid points that I would have addressed, the tone of contempt is impossible to ignore here.<br /> <br /> I get the distinct impression you do not want me to retort, you simply want me to be wrong and go away.<br /> <br /> I assure you that I am responding to your points in thr best manner that I can. I am sorry to have insulted you by presumption, but I assure you there is no malice involved. These presumptions are the honest impression I have gotten from the retorts you provide me, not a means to dismiss. I very much welcome being corrected on where my impressions fall short.<br /> <br /> I do believe I understand your position. You believe that the combat system fails because:<br /> <br /> - the options do not provide a meaningful set of choices<br /> - this is because the choices presented do not alter the outcome in any meaningful way beyond base attacks or not attacking at all<br /> - as a result, every option is just bloat<br /> <br /> do feel welcome to amend this if a crucial point is missed or requires further focus.<br /> <br /> I hoped I was able to address why this is not how I viewed the system, and why I believed that the system does indeed enable engaging combat in part because of the choices presented, but it does seem quite clear I have failed to explain myself adequately. And now you are more intent in trying to catch me out and prove me wrong than to actually understand my position.<br /> <br /> It is disheartening to see this though, I would have hopped you\u2019d provide me the same measures of respect you expect I give you. I understand you are to hurt by what you see as assumptions to avoid falling in to assumptions yourself, and I do apologise for causing that hurt.<br /> <br /> If you are done with me, then I can abide. But if you would genuinely desire my retort, then I can provide it.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T05:33:51-07:00","id":1522151,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Ok, this discussion has diverted from the op and the tone of the posts are just too agressive. I believe we might be in a &quot;agree to disagree&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> Dismissing Saikou arguments as &quot;bullshit&quot; is not only rude, but untrue. Let's try to summarize a bit:<br /> <br /> -You don't like how the system works (difficulties, needed successes and how it's not trivial to calculate the odds) , and not only for combat:<br /> <br /> Ok, this means you change the entire system or you just change combat maneuvers?<br /> <br /> - Your complain about the list being bloated is not about it being big, but it having some maneuvers that you consider useless or inferior, or at least unecessary because it is covered by another one.<br /> <br /> I don't think the list is big, and I agree that *some* maneuvers look unnecessary. However I feel that this is no reason at all <b> for a ST to completely remove them from the game and the option that a player could choose</b>. While you think headbutt is weak, a player might <b>enjoy</b> doing that because it's a bad ass move you see in movies. <br /> <br /> -You proposed to completely change the combat system in a way that there are no difference in difficulty from attacks (is that right?) and you can choose the &quot;fluff&quot; of the attack after the roll:<br /> <br /> That I completely disagree. In my games, I like to focus on what is really happening in-game. I really think that &quot;I attack&quot;, roll, &quot;you give X damage&quot; and it doesn't matter if it was a high kick, a punch, a knee to the stomach, really kills the life of the game and starts looking like a video-game. I like to deal with combat in details, and the reactions of the NPCs will depend on exactly what the PCs do.<br /> <br /> Also, I might not understand <b>exactly</b> how your house rule works, so if you could provide an example of combat it would be better.<br /> <br /> <br /> What Saikou and I are saying, is that we do not mind the maneuvers flaws (the fact that some <b>might</b> be worse than others in most situations) to the point of changing it, since you can just <b>not use that specific maneuver</b> if you are worried about efficiency.<br /> <br /> Now, you as a ST have a player that wants to use the spinning kick. Do you forbid him from doing it? He has to use the regular kick? Or there is no kick, only generic &quot;hits&quot;? What if the character is a martial artist and he wants to use complicated movie-like attacks?<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: You said you didn't lose combat in years, but then you use examples of using sniper rifles from afar in stealth, lol. We are talking about hand to hand combat here, and I bet you didn't win all of them in years.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T00:35:54-07:00","id":1522203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I attack&quot;, roll, &quot;you give X damage&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we are all perfectly aware that this is not the alternative that has been examined. A detailed description of the action follows the roll, along with additional decisions concerning how successes are allocated to effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to deal with combat in details, and the reactions of the NPCs will depend on exactly what the PCs do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am perfectly capable of having NPCs react based on the detailed descriptions of the action that follows the roll.<br /> <br /> While I\u2019m at it, that goes for botches too. They\u2019ve been mentioned as another think that is supposedly downgraded if we don\u2019t choose a maneuver before the roll. Most maneuvers provide no specific guidance on how to handle botches (Disarm being the only exception I can think of) and I have enough information without a maneuver specified to be able to describe a suitably nasty botch when that is appropriate. (Or my players can. I trust my players to make good-faith attempts to impose consequences for their own characters\u2019 actions on the characters most of the time, and to accept correction if I tell them there need to be harsher consequences in a particular case. Also, we\u2019re all familiar with \u201cYes, and\u201d and \u201cYes, but\u201d techniques, to allow us to build on what others have put forward, too, so I can often upgrade a botch suggestion with \u201cYes, and\u201d.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I might not understand <b>exactly</b> how your house rule works, so if you could provide an example of combat it would be better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revan, you\u2019ve been provided enough information already to be able to demonstrate a better understanding of the proposal than this. Nobody is going to bother writing more detailed examples for you if you can\u2019t show good-faith engagement with what has already been discussed. Everyone\u2019s time is limited, and you aren\u2019t showing us that there\u2019s any value in writing more stuff for you.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve talked about this with my players. They knew pretty much instantly what was being proposed, and were able to relate it to their own experiences and other systems that handle combat a bit differently. They are the ones who need to be onboard with this, not Revan or Saikou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-07-2023, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T05:50:48-07:00","id":1522210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522149#post1522149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I see little benefit to you in maintaining this communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect your post a lot. I'm not completely moved by it, because there's some repetition of things I've attempted to highlight as very frustrating to me (and I'd hope I haven't come off as subtle about these things). So I'd say I'm &quot;on the fence&quot; on your motivations here right now. It would be cool to get off the fence on the better side of it, but I'm still wary. I might not like how your arguing all this, but you're stepping up a lot on an interpersonal level and I have to give you props for that.<br /> <br /> I'm going to do my best to chill down here, but I'm going to be blunt on a few things because I'm generally blunt about stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For my part, I have tried to address your concerns by explaining how I approach this problem, and while your counters contain valid points that I would have addressed, the tone of contempt is impossible to ignore here. </div> </div> </div>So, while I appreciate this, this is a series of back-and-forths that includes you saying, &quot;I\u2019m saying I don\u2019t recognise the validity of the complaint.&quot; To me, this just makes all the points you're praising as valid and worth discussing as... just some sort of rhetorical practice or something, because you don't acknowledge the base premise as valid. If you don't believe the base premise is valid, where's my faith that you want to understand it supposed to come from?<br /> <br /> &quot;You're clearly wrong, but you're at least making some good points and I want to explore them,&quot; is not a conversation I'm interested in. If the goal is mutual understanding, I can't have a chill debate about mechanical tidbits under the shadow of my position (esp. on a matter of taste and preference, no some objective truth) isn't valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the distinct impression you do not want me to retort, you simply want me to be wrong and go away. </div> </div> </div>What I would like, for the sake of a potential positive continuation here, is a better balance regarding the focus on your retorts. As my big post spent a lot of time on, you've made a bunch of points that are really tangential to the core issue, and that's making me feel like it's because that &quot;more favorable ground&quot; for you to debate on. I can understand that you don't mean it that way, and you might be getting carried away with tangents (I'm kinda suspecting travisjhall would wish I'd edit down how much I'm responding to like he has been, but I'm a sucker for deep dives).<br /> <br /> I also really don't understand what you want to be understood about. If you were writing an essay about this instead of having a conversation, what would your thesis statement be? How does everything you've been saying about the rules relate back to that core point? Because for me, it feels like you're taking the position of a defense lawyer: that all you have to do is establish reasonable doubt that a significant change to the rules would be valuable,and you've made your point; which is an adversarial sort of approach. So when I talk about focus, I'm saying to maybe not retort on everything, because some of the more edge case retorts are a point of social friction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - the options do not provide a meaningful set of choices<br /> - this is because the choices presented do not alter the outcome in any meaningful way beyond base attacks or not attacking at all<br /> - as a result, every option is just bloat\u200b </div> </div> </div>OK, going to be honest... you almost completely lost my willingness to respond with this.<br /> <br /> Whether a more subjective or objective topic, I tend to feel very strongly about the use of absolutes. I realllllllly don't like when people attribute absolutes to me that I didn't directly express. I never said &quot;every&quot; (every is an absolute) option is just bloat. My position here is definitely more nuanced, and I don't think this is going to sound new:<br /> <br /> &quot;The game provides too many options, which obscures the meaningful choices that are present.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a reason I didn't reduce the generic hand-to-hand list to &quot;strike&quot; and &quot;targeted strikes.&quot; I use words like messy, bloated, rigged, trapped, opaque, and so on because they're things that can be fixed without necessarily redoing the whole thing. A messy room doesn't have to stop being a room to become a clean room.<br /> <br /> You might find what travis and I are suggesting to radical of an overhaul, but we're not saying that the concept of what the rules are trying to do is fundamentally broken. Rather that the method of going from concept to execution needs to be reconsidered.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is because the game focuses on granular details (punches vs. kicks. vs. elbows,, etc,) that mix specific action descriptors with specific mechanics instead of focusing on narrative intent and action impact.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;As a result, the way to address this is to decouple descriptive aspects from mechanical aspects so players focus on narrative intent first, and description based on action impact determined after the dice are rolled.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand you are to hurt by what you see as assumptions to avoid falling in to assumptions yourself, and I do apologise for causing that hurt. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for expressing this. I'm not sure I'm in a place yet to type something I feel is equal to this to you, but I do hope if we can exchange ideas further in respect of your earnestness here, I'll find proper words for it.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a><br /> <br /> I'm going to be brief, because I'm trying to not mood-whiplash too hard here, but what the heck? Sure if that was right after my post I get it. But Saikou most certainly didn't deserve such an excellent attempt to reset a heated conversation followed by that. Read the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T06:36:13-07:00","id":1522217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522203#post1522203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve talked about this with my players. They knew pretty much instantly what was being proposed, and were able to relate it to their own experiences and other systems that handle combat a bit differently. They are the ones who need to be onboard with this, not Revan or Saikou.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I can say is good luck to you then, and apologise that I was unable to provide anything of value to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T07:53:26-07:00","id":1522219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521988#post1521988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, Combat manoeuvres have been around since 1st edition, with Flank, grapple, multiple opponents, and body slam being introduced in the first core book, they were referred to as \u2018complications\u2019 but they served the same role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flank and multiple opponents are not remotely similar to the bulk of M20\u2019s maneuver system, aside from how Flank literally become possibly the only maneuver that combines with other maneuvers and really is a circumstantial bonus that would sit better alongside multiple opponents and similar rules which are not maneuvers. Grapple and body slam .<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that there weren\u2019t some combat modifiers back then, but there was no distinction between a punch and a kick and an elbow strike and a spinning kick and so on in the 1e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> Revised had a short list of Surprise Maneuvers in the core book, but they don\u2019t perform a similar role to M20\u2019s long list of maneuvers either.<br /> <br /> And nobody has suggested getting rid of all the circumstantial modifiers, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1521988#post1521988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Martial arts being introduced in 1st ed\u2019s book of shadows, 2e brought them back and added kick, bite, claw, acrobatic flip, disarm, escape, and blind foe. and revised is where they were first called combat manoeuvres, and including a load more such as clinch, close, jab pistol, blind fighting, sweep, tackle, block, parry, desperate defence, and weapon strike. And the revised akashic book added a whole load of Do related martial arts moves</div> </div> </div> </div>It is really important to understand here that for any RPG, there are groups who play without expansions. The basic rules have to work in their own, because people will use them on their own. And they - we, really, because I\u2019m one of the people who has done it - did play Mage successfully that way, way back in the 1990s. People often really did declare their unarmed combat attacks without specifying whether it was a punch or a kick, and the system didn\u2019t implode and still worked well enough to eventually give us a 20th Anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T19:12:54-07:00","id":1522250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522203#post1522203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve talked about this with my players. They knew pretty much instantly what was being proposed, and were able to relate it to their own experiences and other systems that handle combat a bit differently. They are the ones who need to be onboard with this, not Revan or Saikou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that answer killed the thread for me too. It's the second time <b>you</b> create a thread and when people disagree and asks for more info you say that it is not our place for us to ask and for you to provide. Well, then why the fuck ask that here?<br /> <br /> All I want to say right now is that the mere existence of the maneuvers can't hurt, since people can juat ignore them. And if I were in a game and the ST said that I couldn't use a maneuver because they are removed in his table, or that combat is simplified to the degree of not even having different difficulties anymore, I would leave immediately. <br /> <br /> If your players are ok with what you're doing, good for you. Next time ask them instead of opening a thread and bashing on who disagrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T21:43:49-07:00","id":1522292,"title":"","content":"Since the difficulty of evaluating whether a maneuver is worth using in a given circumstance has been mentioned in this thread, for everyone\u2019s convenience, here\u2019s an Anydice program to run the numbers for you: <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/31a9c\" target=\"_blank\">https://anydice.com/program/31a9c</a><br /> <br /> It only does one comparison at a time (varying with the number of dice in the relevant attack pool and Strength) because looping over scenarios got to be too long to run on the Anydice server. There is it set up for comparing Punch and Kick, but it\u2019s easy enough to modify the last few lines for other damaging maneuvers. The \u201cwod\u201d functions generally should be useful for calculations over a broad range of scenarios. (0 successes is an ordinary failure, -1 successes is a botch,)<br /> <br /> It\u2019s set to one of the turning points - 8 dice, 3 strength - where using Kick, which players would normally assume increases damage, actually reduces mean damage. Just change the obvious variables near the bottom to try it for different scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T01:35:09-07:00","id":1522296,"title":"","content":"That is looking at kick in isolation. But one can also consider factors like:<br /> - adding willpower<br /> - kicking someone immobilised or knocked down<br /> - using magic to enhance the kick<br /> - kicking someone as part of a flank<br /> - environmental factors<br /> - multiple actions to kick (which could allow one kick per die in pool, especially good when opponent cannot dodge)<br /> <br /> etc<br /> <br /> considering how close it is as a raw option, any reduction in difficulty or auto success may indeed tip it in the other way.<br /> <br /> but even then, averages do not tell the whole story of risk/reward. While it is less likely to hit, all hits from a kick are more likely to damage than all hits from a punch, and that is the main element of risk reward. Going safe vs getting that extra hit.<br /> <br /> plus, it can feel quite amazing to benefit from something which was otherwise unlikely to work, especially when it makes all the difference in the moment.<br /> <br /> The summary here is averages do not tell us which option is the best option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-09-2023, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T13:04:33-07:00","id":1522307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522296#post1522296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">considering how close it is as a raw option, any reduction in difficulty or auto success may indeed tip it in the other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is... everything you mentioned applies equally to a punch as a kick unless you specifically make it kick only (aka magically enhance your kicks instead of Brawl/etc. in general).<br /> <br /> Even the desperation &quot;max attacks&quot; is better for a punch than a kick, because you land 1 more hit out of 10, which is going to matter when all of your attacks have 10% of botching and ending your flurry (or whatever other consequence).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but even then, averages do not tell the whole story of risk/reward. While it is less likely to hit, all hits from a kick are more likely to damage than all hits from a punch, and that is the main element of risk reward. Going safe vs getting that extra hit. </div> </div> </div>The thing, the averages include the average damage. Lower diff to hit also translates into more roll-over damage. You hit more, and you hit with more damage, because you get damage from your extra attack successes. The few situations where you might be better for the damage are tiny fractions of a success different. Just never picking Kick over Punch will require hundreds of roll in that tiny range of situations where the damage bonus outweighs the diff increase to see a difference outside the normal variance of your punches.<br /> <br /> You can say &quot;averages don't tell the whole story,&quot; but for Punch vs. Kick they do, because that's the only difference between them: how diff and damage mods impact the overall averages.<br /> <br /> What averages don't tell you are things like why you should always take a medium target Punch over a Kick if you want to take a +1 diff for +1 damage, because you get that and whatever bonus the ST gives you for the targeted attack. The averages can't tell you the whole story of a Punch vs a targeted Punch, because targeting adds something beyond raw numbers that Kick doesn't.<br /> <br /> This is exactly why I don't like how the cWoD handles this stuff. A Punch vs. a targeted Punch is a real choice. Being a PC with four kinds of kicks that are just adjusting diff and damage isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> plus, it can feel quite amazing to benefit from something which was otherwise unlikely to work, especially when it makes all the difference in the moment. </div> </div> </div>There are so many ways to take risks in cWoD combat that could fail horribly or succeed amazingly without maneuvers. While it was Revised with different multiple action rules, I decided my character, who was in a friendly duel not serious combat, went for a full max attacks and zero defense thinking he was going to lose anyway... and then didn't get hit by the attack that should of ended the fight and got three hits in for free. It was exceedingly memorable, but that didn't need specific maneuvers to achieve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The summary here is averages do not tell us which option is the best option. </div> </div> </div>But what don't they tell us if the difference between two options is only to affect the averages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T14:33:32-07:00","id":1522309,"title":"","content":"Imagine this scenario:<br /> <br /> you have strength 3 brawl 3<br /> <br /> yourboponent has been knocked down by someone else, so they are imobalised, they have used up their dice and so cannot dodge.<br /> <br /> now, you could roll one attack with your full pool, or you could roll 6 attacks with a pool of 1 each<br /> <br /> let\u2019s say you roll. 3, 4, 5, 6, 4 8<br /> <br /> the diff to punch is 4, and to kick is 5, due to them being knocked down.<br /> <br /> as one attack, this roll would net you 5 successes for a punch, which mean 4+3 damage dice, a total of 7, and 3 for a kick, giving you 2+3+1 = 6 damage dice<br /> <br /> however, if these were six separate attacks, then you would get a damage roll for each one separately.<br /> <br /> for the punch that is:<br /> 3x5 = 15<br /> for the kick that is:<br /> (3+1)x4 = 16<br /> <br /> reducing the difficulty by a further -2 prior tovthis roll would instead let you receive max potential. For the punch this is 18 damage, while the max potential for the kick is 24 damage. While the risk of botching is exactly the same for both.<br /> <br /> Thing thing about rolling only one die is that a difference of difficulty of 1 only matters 10% of the time. If you get 8,8,8,2,3,2, then it\u2019s 9 for the punch and 12 for the kick, a 33% increase in damage output.<br /> <br /> in this scenario of diff 4 vs 5, each roll has a 60% chance of being better for kicking, a 10% chance of being better for punching, and a 30% chance of being the same for either choice.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T17:09:53-07:00","id":1522317,"title":"","content":"OK:<br /> <br /> 1) You're ignoring the impact of botching before you get all those attack in when you reduce your dice-pool so much.<br /> <br /> 2) The target still gets to soak, which is multiplied by the number of attacks as well.<br /> <br /> 3) You haven't addressed why not to throw targeted punches instead of kicks.<br /> <br /> And think about it, you're trying to make a case for maneuvers by whipping out a highly contrived circumstance that is still of a tiny mechanical benefit. You're not making the case that having Kick and Punch is really valuable if in the rarest and best possible circumstance, you need a 1-2 more HL of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T18:58:20-07:00","id":1522321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522296#post1522296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is looking at kick in isolation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is providing a flexible tool that you can use to do whatever comparison you care to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522296#post1522296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but even then, averages do not tell the whole story of risk/reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>AnyDice does not simply provide averages. It will provide the probabilities of each possible result of the roll, or the probability of rolling at least a certain number of successes or amount of damage, and other data of that type.<br /> <br /> But really, beyond the flexibility of the tool I provided, it really is not a good argument in favour of maneuvers to tell us that the practical effect of them is difficult to evaluate due to the complexity of the system. This is not a feature that helps my players get good use at out of the mechanic at the table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T19:04:29-07:00","id":1522322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522317#post1522317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK:<br /> <br /> 1) You're ignoring the impact of botching before you get all those attack in when you reduce your dice-pool so much.<br /> <br /> 2) The target still gets to soak, which is multiplied by the number of attacks as well.<br /> <br /> 3) You haven't addressed why not to throw targeted punches instead of kicks.<br /> <br /> And think about it, you're trying to make a case for maneuvers by whipping out a highly contrived circumstance that is still of a tiny mechanical benefit. You're not making the case that having Kick and Punch is really valuable if in the rarest and best possible circumstance, you need a 1-2 more HL of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impact of botching is incredibly ST dependent, and so would be far too hypothetical to be useful to discuss.<br /> <br /> regarding soak\u2026I actually can\u2019t find a single source that states this is how it works, and may indeed be a house rule on your part. As far as I can tell, the player accumulates their damage dice in phase 2, and then they are all rolled together in phase 3 against a single soak roll. You might do separate soak rolls for lethal vs bashing, but otherwise nothing RAW suggests multiple attacks from one player allows multiple soak attempts. That's something covered more by defensive actions. If you find evidence to the contrary by all means share it, otherwise I will have to chalk this up a house rule, and therefore another hypothetical.<br /> <br /> why kicks instead of targeted punches when the enemy is knocked down? For one thing it means you yourself don\u2019t have to bend down yourself. Remaining standing can be advantageous if you suddenly find you need to dodge, something you may not be able to do at the standard difficulty while crouching. Though again, these circumstances to become ever more layers of hypothetical.<br /> <br /> actually on that point, many scenarios may be open that a punch may be subject to increased difficulty but a kick would not, such as if the player is carrying anything, if their hands are damaged or in pain, or if they are trying to hit something beyond the reach of their arms but within reach of their feet.<br /> <br /> and I don\u2019t know what you think is controved about using the games rules. If someone has knocked down an opponent, you get a -2 to his them. If someone has blinded them, that\u2019s another -2.<br /> <br /> it isn\u2019t difficult to set up situations with your mage friends to knock down and/or blind the target ahead of bringing down the beating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-09-2023, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T19:06:21-07:00","id":1522323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522321#post1522321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is providing a flexible tool that you can use to do whatever comparison you care to.<br /> <br /> <br /> AnyDice does not simply provide averages. It will provide the probabilities of each possible result of the roll, or the probability of rolling at least a certain number of successes or amount of damage, and other data of that type.<br /> <br /> But really, beyond the flexibility of the tool I provided, it really is not a good argument in favour of maneuvers to tell us that the practical effect of them is difficult to evaluate due to the complexity of the system. This is not a feature that helps my players get good use at out of the mechanic at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps address the other parts of my argument rather than cherry pick the bits you feel you can dismiss with little discussion and used that to say I don\u2019t have an argument at all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T21:12:59-07:00","id":1522325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522323#post1522323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then perhaps address the other parts of my argument</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I just provided a useful tool to make it easier to do something that has been mentioned as hard to do. I see nothing else in your post that argues against that, and so nothing else I should care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T01:14:43-07:00","id":1522334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522325#post1522325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I just provided a useful tool to make it easier to do something that has been mentioned as hard to do. I see nothing else in your post that argues against that, and so nothing else I should care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I shall reflect that back","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T02:51:58-07:00","id":1522336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522322#post1522322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impact of botching is incredibly ST dependent, and so would be far too hypothetical to be useful to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you were just argument how &quot;averages can't tell us everything.&quot; This is the kind of stuff that averages can't actually tell us. You're being extremely inconsistent, arguing technicalities for one thing, and the vagaries of circumstance for another.<br /> <br /> Considering there's a 41% chance you're going to botch at least one out of five 1 die attacks regardless of the Difficulty, it's still something you can't just handwave away because you don't know what the ST will rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> regarding soak\u2026I actually can\u2019t find a single source that states this is how it works, and may indeed be a house rule on your part. </div> </div> </div>Well, we can tack this up to M20 trying to be different with order of operations in combat for whatever reason. But considering every previous edition of the game has you roll soak for each attack, and every other 20th game does that too (including C20 and Wr20, which uses the multiple Phases approach instead of the reverse declaration approach),<br /> <br /> But if you insist on taking M20 in isolation and ignore all previous editions of Mage and all of the other 20th core books: &quot;If and when an attack hits the target, it\u2019s time to figure out how badly that target gets hurt.&quot; That's how Phase 3 starts, and continues without any deviation. It takes about an attack hitting, rolling the damage for the attack, if that kind of damage is soakable, and then rolling to soak. There's nothing in Phase 1 or 2 that implies damage accumulates per attack.<br /> \u200b<br /> Beyond that it's illogical and inconsistent with the rest of the text for five attacks from five different individuals to each get soaked individually, but five attacks from one character on another to be totaled before soak. Why on Earth should it matter what the source of each attack is (and there's already rules for the difficulties of facing multiple opponents which doesn't talk about this being a factor)? It makes way more sense that each attack is resolved individually so you don't get very weird outcomes.<br /> <br /> Also please don't say I'm house ruling something you acknowledge isn't explicitly stated technically in the text. If you acknowledge this is a matter of interpretation, than either of us could be right within a technical parsing of the text without the other implementing a house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...therefore another hypothetical. </div> </div> </div>If hypothetical situations aren't going to count, what, exactly, is left of your own example? Your entire example is just a hypothetical situation. You keep on tacking more hypothetical things on as counterpoints instead of citing the text, or making an extrapolation based to statistics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one thing it means you yourself don\u2019t have to bend down yourself. Remaining standing can be advantageous if you suddenly find you need to dodge, something you may not be able to do at the standard difficulty while crouching. Though again, these circumstances to become ever more layers of hypothetical. </div> </div> </div>More importantly, there's nothing in the RAW that says you suffer any mechanical penalties to punching someone that's prone in front of you. You're not talking about a hypothetical where there's an ambiguous rule without set outcomes, you're talking about either a house rule or at least a use of ST fiat powers to apply a penalty that does not exist in the text. Besides the contradiction between the text and the combat charts, the only default source of difficult penalties to Dodging that would be relevant to the situation as that you need room to Dodge. But any penalty to Dodge from tight space would apply if you're kicking someone while less mobile because you're dog-piling the target with your buddies, or if you're leaning over to punch the poor sap. It would be all the bodies in the way that you need to maneuver around that would be the source of increased difficulty, not the crouching-to-punch part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> actually on that point, many scenarios may be open that a punch may be subject to increased difficulty but a kick would not, such as if the player is carrying anything, if their hands are damaged or in pain, or if they are trying to hit something beyond the reach of their arms but within reach of their feet. </div> </div> </div>More &quot;hypothetical&quot; concepts, and all of this could be applies to kicks as well: tight pants could penalize your kicks, legs are just as (if not more so for being larger targets) capable of being injured, and since legs are larger on average, they might not be able to reach a target around/through lots of obstacles while a hand easily could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and I don\u2019t know what you think is controved about using the games rules. </div> </div> </div>The manner in which you're using them. You're starting with the conclusion of, &quot;the Kick maneuver is useful,&quot; and back-filling in hypothetical scenarios to try to make Kicks useful, while avoiding the fundamental question:<br /> <br /> What does having a Kick maneuver add to the game instead of just having a general &quot;strike&quot; maneuver that doesn't care which limb you use?<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care about a WoD where apparently people always remember to restrain arms, but not the legs, the exists just so people can claim it's important to have basic punches and kicks as things that need different mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone has knocked down an opponent, you get a -2 to his them. If someone has blinded them, that\u2019s another -2. </div> </div> </div>And... Punch or a targeted Punch, gets more out of that -4 difficulty break than a Kick does without any hypothetical stuff tacked on to contrive the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it isn\u2019t difficult to set up situations with your mage friends to knock down and/or blind the target ahead of bringing down the beating. </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to imagine a situation where there's any point to continuing to roll out combat against a restrained and blinded target that the players feel like beating to a bloody pulp well after it's clear they've won the fight.<br /> <br /> I think the vast majority of Mage players are vastly more interested in what happens after you've beaten this person to whatever level of harm is intended, than rolling a bunch of dice to see how many individual attacks it takes to do so. If this is still in the middle of a fight with more opponents to deal with, two characters taking non-damage dealing options to make it easier for one person to land a few big hits isn't really effective (both in terms of lost damage from them not dealing any, and all of the other combatants having a soft target in the ally that's holding the target prone). It is better in WoD combat to focus on one target at a time if you can, because numerical advantage is devastating, but you don't want that turned around on you either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T05:28:03-07:00","id":1522341,"title":"","content":"Just a general note before I get in to this. I am finding your adversarial style of argument to be incredibly draining. This feels less like an attempt to understand one another and more like you are trying to use anything possible to dismiss what I say or twist it to make me out to be a bad actor. As someone who has stated previously in our discourse that they cannot stand even the slightest bit of misrepresentation against them, I find this to be a rather unreasonable position to take, expecting respect on your stance but offering none for whom you discourse with.<br /> <br /> I have been rather patient until now, but I am starting to question what value there is in continuing this discourse, especially as nothing I say seems to mean anything to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you were just argument how &quot;averages can't tell us everything.&quot; This is the kind of stuff that averages can't actually tell us. You're being extremely inconsistent, arguing technicalities for one thing, and the vagaries of circumstance for another.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I have already highlighted a point at which averages do not portray the entire story, to then tell me not considering all possible permutations of the ST's whims as invalidating this is something of a leap of logic.<br /> <br /> But fine, you consider me inconsistent, and I don't believe there is anything I can do to convince you otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Considering there's a 41% chance you're going to botch at least one out of five 1 die attacks regardless of the Difficulty, it's still something you can't just handwave away because you don't know what the ST will rule.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The results of a botch are up to the ST, and as such it becomes difficult to factor in. But regardless of punch or kick, the percentage chance of a botch happening on a single die roll is exactly the same. That is the point I am trying to get at. It hope I have made this clear at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Well, we can tack this up to M20 trying to be different with order of operations in combat for whatever reason. But considering every previous edition of the game has you roll soak for each attack, and every other 20th game does that too (including C20 and Wr20, which uses the multiple Phases approach instead of the reverse declaration approach),<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually cross-referencing with V20, often considered the most complete of the standard WoD rulesets, and indeed such rules were not stated there. It would have been nice had you actually provided a page reference so we could get to the bottom of this rather than throw me vague &quot;It's in the others&quot; references, forcing me to do all the source tracking on our behalf, but then since you consider me an opponent rather than a collaborator, perhaps you don't feel any incentive to work with me on this.<br /> <br /> In any case, looking through W20, I cannot find a single mention that multiple attacks leads to multiple soak rolls. In fact for damage it says the following: &quot;To figure out how much damage has been inflicted, the attacking player rolls her dice pool against difficulty 6, Each success deals out one health level of damage&quot; W20 Core pg290.<br /> For soak it says this &quot;To soak damage, roll your character's satamina against a difficulty determined by the damage.&quot; W20 Core Pg290<br /> <br /> So apart from requiring a different soak roll depending on the level of damage received. It does seem like the RAW is that damage from one's attacks are pooled together and rolled all at once during the resolution phase of the combat, not separately.<br /> <br /> C20 seems to state nothing which contradicts with this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once all the characters have determined if their attacks hit or missed, the next step is to see how much damage the characters inflicted or suffered...Rolling damage is relatively simple. Every weapon, from a fist to an assault rifle, has a base damage. The attacker rolls this base damage + one additional die for every success after the first on the character's attack roll... C20 pg281 (if you want to read the full paragraph for yourself)<br /> <br /> Compounding this is the combat summary for stage four: Resuloution and Damage<br /> &quot;Determine total damage effect (based on the weapon type or maneuver), adding any extra dice gained from successes on the attack roll. Targets may attempt ot soak damage, if possible. Kithain, like mortals, cannot soak lethal damage unless they are wearing armor, except when this lethal damage is chimerical. Kithain can soak chimerical lethal damage just like bashing damage. Each success on the character's soak roll reduces their damage taken by one health level&quot; C20 Core pg283<br /> <br /> At no point does it state that damage from multiple attacks are rolled seperately, just that we determine the total damage effect, and roll that, with a single soak attempt against the result.<br /> <br /> But I do encourage you to have a look for yourself and source where there is something showing evidence to the contrary, because for the life of me I cannot find it, leading me to conclude this is actually an assumption made by players/STs rather than a bonified RAW thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> But if you insist on taking M20 in isolation and ignore all previous editions of Mage and all of the other 20th core books: &quot;If and when an attack hits the target, it\u2019s time to figure out how badly that target gets hurt.&quot; That's how Phase 3 starts, and continues without any deviation. It takes about an attack hitting, rolling the damage for the attack, if that kind of damage is soakable, and then rolling to soak. There's nothing in Phase 1 or 2 that implies damage accumulates per attack.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do all of phase 2 before you move on to phase 3, that is actually quite a crucial design element of WoD combat. Rolling damage immediately after rolling attack actually messes up the flow of combat quite significantly. I can get in to why this is if you are interested, but I bring this up mainly because it is an often used house rule people mistake as a RAW rule that you roll damage immediately after the attack, which is not the case.<br /> <br /> As a result, the idea that you must roll damage separately for each his you make seems to be based around the assumption that these things remain separate, and I haven't found a single explicit statement through any of the books to support this.<br /> <br /> That is why I conclude that this is not how combat actually functions going RAW, regardless of which edition or system you use.<br /> <br /> But again, if you have a passage that demonstrates otherwise, I would really like to be made aware of it. Preferably one that doesn't require too much interpretation to see the intent of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> Beyond that it's illogical and inconsistent with the rest of the text for five attacks from five different individuals to each get soaked individually, but five attacks from one character on another to be totaled before soak. Why on Earth should it matter what the source of each attack is (and there's already rules for the difficulties of facing multiple opponents which doesn't talk about this being a factor)? It makes way more sense that each attack is resolved individually so you don't get very weird outcomes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a compelling point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Also please don't say I'm house ruling something you acknowledge isn't explicitly stated technically in the text. If you acknowledge this is a matter of interpretation, than either of us could be right within a technical parsing of the text without the other implementing a house rule.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely, either way would therefor be a house rule<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> If hypothetical situations aren't going to count, what, exactly, is left of your own example? Your entire example is just a hypothetical situation. You keep on tacking more hypothetical things on as counterpoints instead of citing the text, or making an extrapolation based to statistics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is more about the degree of hypothetical. If I was to say &quot;what if an enemy was grabbing your arms&quot; then you could dismiss that as not really being a factor since you could equally says &quot;what if an enemy was grabbing your legs&quot;.<br /> <br /> I made a clear scenario to explain how I understand an aspect of the mathematics. We could continue with countless iterations of these examples, but I believe the point is being missed, the point being that there are situations in which it is better to kick than to punch. The point that punching is on average better with all things considered as standard does ignore this point as context defines the landscape upon which the choices are made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> More importantly, there's nothing in the RAW that says you suffer any mechanical penalties to punching someone that's prone in front of you. You're not talking about a hypothetical where there's an ambiguous rule without set outcomes, you're talking about either a house rule or at least a use of ST fiat powers to apply a penalty that does not exist in the text. Besides the contradiction between the text and the combat charts, the only default source of difficult penalties to Dodging that would be relevant to the situation as that you need room to Dodge. But any penalty to Dodge from tight space would apply if you're kicking someone while less mobile because you're dog-piling the target with your buddies, or if you're leaning over to punch the poor sap. It would be all the bodies in the way that you need to maneuver around that would be the source of increased difficulty, not the crouching-to-punch part.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Under certain circumstances, say, in a high winds or driving rain - a task might be more challenging than usual. In such cases, the Storyteller might raise the difficulty one to three steps above tits usual level (+1 to +3)&quot; M20 Core Pg 387.<br /> <br /> ST can decide to apply these difficulty modifiers as makes sense given the context of the story. This is not a house rule, this is literally how the game work.<br /> <br /> If you wish to make all penalties run so that when the player asks &quot;can I kick them instead&quot; you say &quot;nope, kicking is just a worse punch&quot;, then that is entirely your design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> More &quot;hypothetical&quot; concepts, and all of this could be applies to kicks as well: tight pants could penalize your kicks, legs are just as (if not more so for being larger targets) capable of being injured, and since legs are larger on average, they might not be able to reach a target around/through lots of obstacles while a hand easily could.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason I didn't wish to go in to excessive hypotheticals regarding botches, I suspected you would simply say &quot;hypotheticals exist that make kicking worse therefore hypotheticals that making kicking better are invalid&quot;<br /> <br /> This isn't my argument. My argument is that there are contexts in which one maneuver is better than the other, and the implications of using one over the other can create differences in the way the combat flows generally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> The manner in which you're using them. You're starting with the conclusion of, &quot;the Kick maneuver is useful,&quot; and back-filling in hypothetical scenarios to try to make Kicks useful, while avoiding the fundamental question:<br /> <br /> What does having a Kick maneuver add to the game instead of just having a general &quot;strike&quot; maneuver that doesn't care which limb you use?<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care about a WoD where apparently people always remember to restrain arms, but not the legs, the exists just so people can claim it's important to have basic punches and kicks as things that need different mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And... Punch or a targeted Punch, gets more out of that -4 difficulty break than a Kick does without any hypothetical stuff tacked on to contrive the situation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While punch is more likely to succeed, the same &quot;all success roll&quot; on a punch and a kick will let the kick do more damage. It might be less likely to get to that point, but if it does, it is very nice, so if the diff is low enough, you might as well go for it. You can even target them with the kick if so desired. Allowing to, for example, still target the leg and thus get the benefit of the leg damage effect (such as immobilisation), but also get the +2 damage, as oppose to, say, targeting their hand (which might instead next them a reduction in die for their punches)<br /> <br /> Oh actually, that's another point, specific injury is also mentioned pg 387, going beyond wound penalties, you can lose dice on your dice pool if a specific part of you is injured, so if one's hands are injured to the point of losing 2 dice, then kicking might seem like a good alternative. Again, this is all circumstantial, but circumstance is what drives these decisions<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> It's difficult to imagine a situation where there's any point to continuing to roll out combat against a restrained and blinded target that the players feel like beating to a bloody pulp well after it's clear they've won the fight.<br /> <br /> I think the vast majority of Mage players are vastly more interested in what happens after you've beaten this person to whatever level of harm is intended, than rolling a bunch of dice to see how many individual attacks it takes to do so. If this is still in the middle of a fight with more opponents to deal with, two characters taking non-damage dealing options to make it easier for one person to land a few big hits isn't really effective (both in terms of lost damage from them not dealing any, and all of the other combatants having a soft target in the ally that's holding the target prone). It is better in WoD combat to focus on one target at a time if you can, because numerical advantage is devastating, but you don't want that turned around on you either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point, I really want to know one thing<br /> <br /> What are you trying to get out of this discussion now?<br /> <br /> is your goal to get me to concede and decide never to use combat maneuvers? Or is your goal to understand why I believe they are of use?<br /> <br /> If it is the former then fine. I concede. My way of playing where I might create scenarios where a player could decide kicking is the more appealing choice, or deciding that even if it is more likely to fail, it still offers them what they wish to get out of combat, is the inherently wrong way to play.<br /> <br /> If it is the latter, then please could you tell me what do you think my stance is here? What is it I believe about the way combat works and why do I advocate for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-10-2023, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T13:19:43-07:00","id":1522354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522341#post1522341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am finding your adversarial style of argument to be incredibly draining.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have repeatedly ignored a direct question I've asked three times now. That is not showing me respect while you get none back from me. Misrepresenting my request to avoid a specific form of misrepresentation as being particularly frustrating to me (turning my nuanced conditional statements into absolutes) into some broad directive that I cannot tolerate any misrepresentation is doing exactly what I requested you not to do; another act of disrespect from you. If you want to make this about us, instead of keeping it on the actual topic, no, there is no point to continuing.<br /> <br /> Why is it so much to ask that you answer a fundamental question about your position so I can actually understand it? Instead of addressing that question, you bring the debate back to contestable rules. How am I supposed to understand a position you will no clarify on a direct question about it? If all I get are rules arguments, then that's all I can respond with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe I have already highlighted a point at which averages do not portray the entire story, to then tell me not considering all possible permutations of the ST's whims as invalidating this is something of a leap of logic. </div> </div> </div>You didn't highlight a point at which averages don't tell the whole story. I made the case on this, and you didn't actually contest it with any retort. You replied with a scenario that happens to have numbers that could shift the balance in a Kick's favor... by using averages as the core point of your example. When actually presented with points in the system where averages don't tell the whole story - which are points that should bolster your point to take into account, not diminish it - you retreat from those. I do not understand why botches, targeted attacks, and other such aspects of the system aren't things you would embrace if you're arguing against just looking at the averages. I also do not understand why you then go to ST fiat of increased difficulty in a retort while rejecting the ST fiat of the results of a botch as valid consideration.<br /> <br /> Your retorts are inconsistent with each other. I cannot understand a coherent point from inconsistent responses alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was actually cross-referencing with V20, often considered the most complete of the standard WoD rulesets, and indeed such rules were not stated there. </div> </div> </div>V20, pg. 247: &quot;After an attack hits and inflicts damage, the defender may make a soak roll to resist.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> Note the singular. &quot;An attack&quot; hits and the target soaks that attack's damage. If the books wanted you to roll up all your attacks and add the damage together, this phrasing would be illogical. This is a consistent feature of the books: damage and soak relate to a single attack, not multiple attacks.<br /> <br /> There is nothing that says to add up the damage from each attack, and then the target has to soak that total damage, and lines that are phrased that single attacks are matched to single soak rolls. Yes, the texts could be much clear about this (and used to be when they had more combat examples in them), but unless you can cite something that says to add damage from multiple attacks together, I don't see how you side with that interpretation based on just a lack of specificity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Precisely, either way would therefor be a house rule </div> </div> </div>Then why are you arguing your house rule is the RAW?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is more about the degree of hypothetical. </div> </div> </div>Something either is a hypothetical, or it isn't. There's also no objective metric of degree of hypothetical. If we're talking about statistics, we can talk about things like standard deviation/variance, or which method of calculating if something is an outlier to set boundaries of what's too unusual to consider. If you want to say, &quot;lets ignore botches on 6 dice to Punch vs. 6 dice to Kick, as in both cases the odds are under 5%,&quot; I could see the validity of treating it as an outlier for an example and ignoring a botch result.<br /> <br /> Just going on a personal feeling of subjective &quot;hypothetical-ness&quot; isn't something that is simple to find common ground on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I was to say &quot;what if an enemy was grabbing your arms&quot; then you could dismiss that as not really being a factor since you could equally says &quot;what if an enemy was grabbing your legs&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Which is... exactly what happened? You selectively added things in favor of Kicks, that are no more or less likely to come up that things that favor Punches, and so I pointed that out.<br /> <br /> This is what I meant when I requested more focus in your retorts: if you know this was coming, and you knew there was no positive resolution of it, why even bring it up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....the point being that there are situations in which it is better to kick than to punch. </div> </div> </div>A point I made in post 7 of this thread. This is why I hate my comments being reduced to absolutes: I acknowledged that these situations can exist from pretty much the beginning of the thread, but you're treating me as if I need to be told something so basic when it's your simplification of my position that's the cause of misunderstanding between us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ST can decide to apply these difficulty modifiers as makes sense given the context of the story. This is not a house rule, this is literally how the game work. </div> </div> </div>Again, you're reducing my statements. You quoted me saying, &quot;...you're talking about either a house rule <b>or at least a use of ST fiat powers </b>to apply a penalty that does not exist in the text.&quot; emphasis mine. And responded with the general rules that the ST has fiat powers to apply penalties if they see fit.<br /> <br /> If the previous example might have been excusable because my statement got lost in the rush of time and responses, chiding me for not acknowledging something that you quote me acknowledging is not so easily excused. You want to feel like a collaborator? Don't quote me the rules as if you're correcting me when you're just citing the passage that backs up what I actually said.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wish to make all penalties run so that when the player asks &quot;can I kick them instead&quot; you say &quot;nope, kicking is just a worse punch&quot;, then that is entirely your design. </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, implied I am advocating for this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't my argument. My argument is that there are contexts in which one maneuver is better than the other, and the implications of using one over the other can create differences in the way the combat flows generally. </div> </div> </div>Then why can't you make it without hypothetical scenarios that are biased in the favor of Kicks?<br /> <br /> Why do you refuse to answer the question I highlighted as &quot;fundamental&quot; in that passage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are you trying to get out of this discussion now? </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to see if you'll answer a question that gets back to whatever your core position and purpose here actually is.<br /> <br /> What about you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is your goal to get me to concede and decide never to use combat maneuvers? Or is your goal to understand why I believe they are of use? </div> </div> </div>Neither.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is the latter, then please could you tell me what do you think my stance is here? What is it I believe about the way combat works and why do I advocate for it? </div> </div> </div>I've already said I have no idea what your stance is, or what you believe about all this. It's a primary reason why I struggle with you saying you want to reach mutual understanding.<br /> <br /> You have reduced my position, repeatedly, to a parody of what I actually said, and refuse to answer a question I've asked repeatedly. Yet you insist I'm the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T15:36:23-07:00","id":1522364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522354#post1522354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have repeatedly ignored a direct question I've asked three times now.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, it may have gotten lost in the great mounds of texts previously written. So I ask you now, to make things simple, what is your direct question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T15:56:07-07:00","id":1522365,"title":"","content":"What does having maneuvers, such as Kick, that only modify difficulty and damage, add to the game? In the context of their being general options like targeted attacks already existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T16:10:23-07:00","id":1522366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522365#post1522365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does having maneuvers, such as Kick, that only modify difficulty and damage, add to the game? In the context of their being general options like targeted attacks already existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It conjures to mind scenarios in which one will need to rely on kicking, such as when their arms of no or limited use. Something that the player can impress upon an NPC as well if desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T16:49:49-07:00","id":1522368,"title":"","content":"But why the need for a mechanical distinction? A general &quot;strike&quot; maneuver can be written to conjure kicks as well as punches, while targeted shots also work to remind players that bodies have individual areas to exploit. How does tying specific mechanics to specific descriptions of attacks add the impetus to think about using kicks in combat as a whole?<br /> <br /> Or to come at if from another angle, why does a player that wants their PC to kick someone have to eat a +1 difficulty or invest in specific MA/Do moves just to throw a kick if they're already thinking about describing things with more than just punches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T17:06:29-07:00","id":1522370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522368#post1522368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why the need for a mechanical distinction? A general &quot;strike&quot; maneuver can be written to conjure kicks as well as punches, while targeted shots also work to remind players that bodies have individual areas to exploit. How does tying specific mechanics to specific descriptions of attacks add the impetus to think about using kicks in combat as a whole?<br /> <br /> Or to come at if from another angle, why does a player that wants their PC to kick someone have to eat a +1 difficulty or invest in specific MA/Do moves just to throw a kick if they're already thinking about describing things with more than just punches?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a kick and punch were exactly the same, it would be no different to, say, if an enemy grabbed their arms, preventing their punches but still enabling a kick.<br /> <br /> because there is a difference, it makes this scenario more distinct. Their kick has a higher chance to fail, but still offers an avenue to inflicting damage, and because of the extra damage die provided, it does provide a bit more hope for a way out even with your arms disabled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-10-2023, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T17:48:31-07:00","id":1522371,"title":"","content":"You say there would be no distinction between being grabbed by the arms... but that distinction isn't in the grappling rules anyway. You're grappled, you can't kick or punch, so that's not telling me why Kick adds to the game over just having a &quot;strike' move.<br /> <br /> Why does attacking with your feet if your arms are disabled need a +1 diff and a +1 damage? If your legs are tied up you get to punch at normal diff and damage. If you arms are injured, you'll have wound penalties that will make your kicking harder.<br /> <br /> But we're circling back to old unproductive things.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say that the concept of significant choices in combat to make things more distinct and memorable is bad As I said from the beginning, I think the execution in the rules isn't good. This is why I said &quot;Neither&quot; before. I understand why people want maneuvers. I don't understand why you're clinging so strongly to the idea that their might be other methods of doing combat moves. And you're not address that part of this. When we get close, we circle back to old stuff that didn't get us anywhere. It feels like you're hung up on defending the concept, that you're reflexively defending the execution, when my issue is with the execution and not the concept..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T23:47:53-07:00","id":1522381,"title":"","content":"I really don\u2019t know what you want from me. I have answered your question in the plainest possible terms. I have answered it again and again and again, and no matter how many times I address it, you keep dismissing it and tell me I have refused to answer. <br /> <br /> Tell me exactly what type of answer you want, tel lme what you are hoping to get out of me.<br /> <br /> <br /> regarding grappling. Do we really need it written down that if someone holds your arms down that you can still use your feet to kick? If you say yes, then this is what motivates me to say when you say things like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2018You're grappled, you can't kick or punch, so that's not telling me why Kick adds to the game over just having a &quot;strike' move.\u2019 </div> </div> </div>it suggests you are advocating for this:<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you wish to make all penalties run so that when the player asks &quot;can I kick them instead&quot; you say &quot;nope, kicking is just a worse punch\u201d\u201d.<br /> <br /> Similarly, wound penalties via health are merely 1 way to consider wounds, you can have targeted wounds that only affect one part of your body and thus only actions that use that part. The system is flexible enough to allow for this, and it makes sense that if someone broke your fingers, your punches would suffer but your kicks would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand why you're clinging so strongly to the idea that their might be other methods of doing combat moves. And you're not address that part of this. </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand what you are asking here. Is it that you don\u2019t understand why I think it makes sense that a punch and a kick are separate manoeuvres?<br /> <br /> i believe I have addressed this repeatedly, it\u2019s because they are in fact different things, there will be scenarios when one can not punch but they can kick, and they are in a more dire dotuation because of it. That\u2019s part of drama, not having your best options therefore you need to decide on whether or not to rely on messier options. And that is what this manoeuvre allows.<br /> <br /> you call these hypotheticals that make kicking more favourable, and indeed they are, but such scenarios are not outside the field of possibility.<br /> <br /> kicking is an act of desperation, having it be more difficult yet more painful reflects that. It is not a choice you make because it is optimal, but because it is the best option you have in the moment. And that is why I think it has merit. Bad options that you find you have to resort to incentivise us to design encounters that highlight such manoeuvres, and make combat feel more alive than simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d<br /> <br /> please, I implore you, before you ask me the same question for the umpteenth time, consider what it is I am answering you, actually try to understand what it is I\u2019m saying, where I am coming from. Because otherwise my position will continue to elude you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T00:10:45-07:00","id":1522382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522381#post1522381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad options that you find you have to resort to incentivise us to design encounters that highlight such manoeuvres, and make combat feel more alive than simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>When I started this thread, I was very specific about what I asked. I did not ask you, or anybody else, to tell me what I should do in my game. Instead, I asked what you have done in your games, and what effect that had had in your games. There is a reason I asked this. It\u2019s because each of us can really only speak to our own experiences.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, are you telling us that without Punch and Kick being distinct maneuvers, and other also-similar actions also being distinct maneuvers, the combats that you run as an ST, or play as a player, would be simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d? Remember, <i>speaking to your own experiences</i>; I am not asking you to guess concerning our experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T00:19:21-07:00","id":1522383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522382#post1522382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I started this thread, I was very specific about what I asked. I did not ask you, or anybody else, to tell me what I should do in my game. Instead, I asked what you have done in your games, and what effect that had had in your games. There is a reason I asked this. It\u2019s because each of us can really only speak to our own experiences.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, are you telling us that without Punch and Kick being distinct maneuvers, and other also-similar actions also being distinct maneuvers, the combats that you run as an ST, or play as a player, would be simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d? Remember, <i>speaking to your own experiences</i>; I am not asking you to guess concerning our experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, yes. If they are the same manoeuvre and there is not obstacle that necessitated consideration of other manoeuvres, then combat will will boil down to \u201cI hit him\u201d over and over again, and this gets old quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T00:19:57-07:00","id":1522384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don\u2019t know what you want from me. I have answered your question in the plainest possible terms. I have answered it again and again and again, and no matter how many times I address it, you keep dismissing it and tell me I have refused to answer. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's not what he just did. What he just did was to state why he doesn't <i>agree with </i>your answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T01:18:51-07:00","id":1522386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522384#post1522384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that's not what he just did. What he just did was to state why he doesn't <i>agree with </i>your answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>if they disagree then they disagree. That isn\u2019t an issue for me. My problem is when they routinely tell me I haven\u2019t addressed something I am sure I have addressed multiple times in multiple ways and using that as the basis to dismiss my position as reflexive defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T01:18:59-07:00","id":1522387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522383#post1522383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, yes. If they are the same manoeuvre and there is not obstacle that necessitated consideration of other manoeuvres, then combat will will boil down to \u201cI hit him\u201d over and over again, and this gets old quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Now I am going to speak to my experiences.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been roleplaying for over 30 years now. I\u2019ve used a wide variety of systems - some of the Storyteller/Storytelling lineage, many not - including Mage: the Ascension, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Changeling: the Lost, D&amp;D (at least 8 distinct editions), Masks: A New Generation, Seventh Sea, Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Don\u2019t Rest Your Head, Everway, Amber DRPG, Firefly, Ars Magica, Monster of the Week, Night Witches, Sign, multiple scenario-specific custom systems designed by me for convention play and/or LARP, a much larger variety of other scenario-specific custom systems designed by others for convention play and/or LARP, and so many others that I have no doubt I would hit triple figures if I counted up everything I\u2019ve played.<br /> <br /> A great many of those games have not involved the very specific distinction between maneuvers that M20 has, including the way I\u2019ve played and run Mage in the past.<br /> <br /> I have been able to avoid combat becoming simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d\u200b as a general rule (the exceptions being when we wished to simply burn through the rolls quickly to get onto something more meaningful - that\u2019s a valid choice sometimes). Even when playing Monster of the Week recently, a game that has literally one move for inflicting harm on another living being (called Kick Some Ass) with the same people I will soon be running M20 for, our combat was tense, colourful, and held meaningful decisions.<br /> <br /> My experience is that I do not need Punch, Kick, Elbow Strike, Spinning Kick and so on as distinct mechanics in the system to have more complex and interesting combat than \u201cI hit him\u201d over and over again.<br /> <br /> I accept your description of your experiences as fundamentally true. Will you do the same for mine?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T01:28:18-07:00","id":1522388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522387#post1522387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Now I am going to speak to my experiences.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been roleplaying for over 30 years now. I\u2019ve used a wide variety of systems - some of the Storyteller/Storytelling lineage, many not - including Mage: the Ascension, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Changeling: the Lost, D&amp;D (at least 8 distinct editions), Masks: A New Generation, Seventh Sea, Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Don\u2019t Rest Your Head, Everway, Amber DRPG, Firefly, Ars Magica, Monster of the Week, Night Witches, Sign, multiple scenario-specific custom systems designed by me for convention play and/or LARP, a much larger variety of other scenario-specific custom systems designed by others for convention play and/or LARP, and so many others that I have no doubt I would hit triple figures if I counted up everything I\u2019ve played.<br /> <br /> A great many of those games have not involved the very specific distinction between maneuvers that M20 has, including the way I\u2019ve played and run Mage in the past.<br /> <br /> I have been able to avoid combat becoming simply \u201cI strike, I strike, I strike\u201d\u200b as a general rule (the exceptions being when we wished to simply burn through the rolls quickly to get onto something more meaningful - that\u2019s a valid choice sometimes). Even when playing Monster of the Week recently, a game that has literally one move for inflicting harm on another living being (called Kick Some Ass) with the same people I will soon be running M20 for, our combat was tense, colourful, and held meaningful decisions.<br /> <br /> My experience is that I do not need Punch, Kick, Elbow Strike, Spinning Kick and so on as distinct mechanics in the system to have more complex and interesting combat than \u201cI hit him\u201d over and over again.<br /> <br /> I accept your description of your experiences as fundamentally true. Will you do the same for mine?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t believe I have been quarrelling with you about your experience, just simply trying to explain my own reasoning in such a way that it can be understood.<br /> <br /> if you think your experience is superior to mine and you have no interest in considering what I am saying, then don\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T01:31:33-07:00","id":1522389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522388#post1522388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t believe I have been quarrelling with you about your experience,</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a yes/no question, Saikou. If you wish to be understood, you should start by directly answering questions that have been directly asked.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T01:38:10-07:00","id":1522390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522389#post1522389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a yes/no question, Saikou. If you wish to be understood, you should start by directly answering questions that have been directly asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> the question comes completely out of left field and implies a pretty large misunderstanding has taken place, as why would you ask it if you didn\u2019t think the answer could be no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T03:02:39-07:00","id":1522391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522390#post1522390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. Now that this is established\u2026<br /> <br /> For the purpose of determining how I should act in order to achieve a high probability of a good experience for my group in our upcoming game, yes, I consider my experiences to be superior to yours.<br /> <br /> For other purposes, possibly my experiences are not superior to yours. It would depend on the purpose. If you are considering how to achieve good results in your own game, it is likely that your experiences will have more bearing - they will be superior, in that sense.<br /> <br /> But just because my experiences will have more weight in my decisions concerning my game does not mean other people\u2019s experiences cannot be examined for useful insight. Therefore I asked my original questions in this thread, Somebody who has engaged with that particular mechanic might have had knowledge that I lacked, or a perspective I had not considered. The fact is that not much, if anything, has been said about M20 combat maneuvers that I had not considered, but I wouldn\u2019t know if I didn\u2019t ask.<br /> <br /> When it comes to you deciding how you should run your games, it\u2019s up to you to determine whether any other perspectives offer you any extra insight. I would suggest some curiosity concerning other people\u2019s experiences, as there is a chance you will learn something that way (just as I might have learnt something if somebody had answered my original question in an unexpected way) but that is still your decision to make.<br /> <br /> And ultimately, I don\u2019t care what you do in your games, if your experiences do not bring me new insight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522390#post1522390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the question comes completely out of left field and implies a pretty large misunderstanding has taken place, as why would you ask it if you didn\u2019t think the answer could be no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes it is important to clearly state these things. Without the clear statement, nobody can be held accountable to what they say.<br /> <br /> At some point, I may post here concerning how I alter the system and/or what happens when I do so. Now that you have admitted to the truth of my experiences, hopefully you will act accordingly. If you think you have perspective that would provide insight, you should present that <i>as your experience</i>. Speaking from your experience means telling us what happened when you did something similar, not telling us what will happen when we do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:19:57-07:00","id":1522426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522336#post1522336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does having a Kick maneuver add to the game instead of just having a general &quot;strike&quot; maneuver that doesn't care which limb you use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having a general strike maneuver means that there is no distinction, mechanically, from kicks, to punches, to elbows, etc.<br /> <br /> While that is not the end of the world, I just think that it is more fun when the game try to represent reality better and a punch is not the same as a kick, so I (particularly) prefer to have maneuvers.<br /> <br /> Now, you can argue that some maneuvers aren't ideal mechanically, and I agree with that. But instead of removing them and reducing combat to &quot;strikes&quot;, if one want to change the system as it is, I'd say it's better to try to change maneuvers stats.<br /> <br /> Regarding dirty fighting and martial arts: if I'm playing a martial artist mage, I want him to be on another level compared to regular people that has some martial practice and maneuvers add to this. And more dots doesn't seem enough.<br /> <br /> One last argument is that other splats have easy access to natural weapons, and giving mages maneuvers that makes them better at hand to hand gives them at least something. It also fits a very cool matrix style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 09-11-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T22:37:10-07:00","id":1522444,"title":"","content":"What is the difficulty of blocking a kick? The book states that the difficulty of blocking a punch is 6 while the difficulty of blocking a table is 8. I'm quite confused by the ill-defined combat rule of M20.<br /> Is it possible that the difficulty of blocking a kick is 7? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T01:07:17-07:00","id":1522446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522444#post1522444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the difficulty of blocking a table is 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a typo? Blocking a table?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, no, I see. That is an actual example in the book, which I can see now that I\u2019ve had a chance to pull it out.<br /> <br /> Looks like exactly what the difficulty to block a given attack is, is left entirely up to the ST, apart from \u201cfist\u201d being 6 and \u201ctable\u201d being 8. I wouldn\u2019t be inclined to increase the difficulty of a block just because the difficulty of the attack increased, though. Not as a general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-12-2023, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T11:14:35-07:00","id":1522473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522426#post1522426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that is not the end of the world, I just think that it is more fun when the game try to represent reality better and a punch is not the same as a kick, so I (particularly) prefer to have maneuvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but if the only thing this adds is an appeal to your personal preferences on granularity, are you acknowledging that it therefore doesn't add anything for those of us that think the game doesn't get better with this level of granularity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if I'm playing a martial artist mage, I want him to be on another level compared to regular people that has some martial practice and maneuvers add to this. And more dots doesn't seem enough. </div> </div> </div>But... those aren't magical maneuvers. A Sleeper with Brawl 3 and a mage with Brawl 3 are equals unless the mage uses magic to enhance themselves further. The mage is on another level by applying magic (or having specific Backgrounds/Merits of supernatural origin, etc.)... just like anything else. Virtual Adepts aren't better hackers than regular human hackers because of some special L337 coding stuff that's just special training. They use their magic to do stuff Sleepers can't do, or do normal things way better than what Sleepers do. Why should fighting be any different? Magic can boost your Physical Attributes, give your attacks bonus damage, reduce the difficulty of your combat Ability of choice across the board, boost your Initiative, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want a martial arts mage that kicks serious ass, the hours of practice they do should be ritual castings to boost their combat prowess with magic. Not only is that how the game works in general, it's also going to get you way farther than a long list of combat maneuvers anyone can learn ever will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One last argument is that other splats have easy access to natural weapons, and giving mages maneuvers that makes them better at hand to hand gives them at least something. It also fits a very cool matrix style. </div> </div> </div>The only thing other splats can't get is Do. Martial Arts as a separate Ability didn't start in Mage. IIRC WtA got up to three different unique combat styles as well. If you want Bullet Time combat tricks... that's what Time 3 is for. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522444#post1522444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difficulty of blocking a kick?</div> </div> </div> </div>While up to the ST, I would keep a Kick at 6. Blocking isn't really about trying to just stop an attack, it's about controlling the energy of an attack to minimize the damage dealt. The most basic blocks are all about redirection: you don't try to stop a punch by catching it in your fist, you sweep your arm into their arm at an angle that pushes their arm out of line with your body: either so the strike hits a part of your body more capable of enduring it, or so it misses completely. The same is true of defending against a kick. <br /> <br /> What I see the book trying to do, is deal with larger objects. I would say a tackle or similar full body contact move would justify being a 7 because redirecting that energy without doing what amounts to a Dodge is significantly harder. Maneuvering yourself into place so you can apply pressure to keep the attack from landing fully is generally going to go up as the size and mass of whatever is coming at you goes up. With a such a small scale of 6 to 8 diff to deal with, the abstraction is going to be significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T11:29:47-07:00","id":1522474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522473#post1522473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want a martial arts mage that kicks serious ass, the hours of practice they do should be ritual castings to boost their combat prowess with magic. Not only is that how the game works in general, it's also going to get you way farther than a long list of combat maneuvers anyone can learn ever will</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their argument was more that they like the array of manoeuvres that Martial Arts ability allows them to unlock, and such a thing on the mundane side gives them a richer and more dynamic experience.<br /> <br /> To say \u201cyeah but you can do that with magic\u201d sort of misses the point they were making in favour of the system that is in place.<br /> <br /> especially since having non-magic options can be preferable in a lot of scenarios, especially when the domino effect is in full swing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T11:40:18-07:00","id":1522475,"title":"","content":"How does a list of maneuvers Sleepers can learn just as easily as mages help, &quot;be on another level,&quot; which is what Revan said was desirable? The specific comparison between regular folks and mages was made, so I addressed that as separate from just liking having maneuvers in general.<br /> <br /> If you want to feel like Neo from the Matrix (as close as WoD combat will let you anyway)... &quot;do that with magic&quot; is not missing the point. That's the point of the game titled Mage. You do magic. That's your thing That's what separates you from everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Domino effect doesn't matter to a mage that uses their daily martial arts training regime to cast combat boosting magic on themselves. You do that ahead of time so you don't have to worry about exactly those sorts of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T13:27:13-07:00","id":1522480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522475#post1522475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a list of maneuvers Sleepers can learn just as easily as mages help, &quot;be on another level,&quot; which is what Revan said was desirable? The specific comparison between regular folks and mages was made, so I addressed that as separate from just liking having maneuvers in general.<br /> <br /> If you want to feel like Neo from the Matrix (as close as WoD combat will let you anyway)... &quot;do that with magic&quot; is not missing the point. That's the point of the game titled Mage. You do magic. That's your thing That's what separates you from everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Domino effect doesn't matter to a mage that uses their daily martial arts training regime to cast combat boosting magic on themselves. You do that ahead of time so you don't have to worry about exactly those sorts of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the guy said he wanted them to be on another level compared to regular people, and regular people, sleeper or otherwise, aren\u2019t proficient with martial arts.<br /> <br /> the statement is about what they find martial arts manoeuvres add to the experience for them. Telling them that this is the wrong thing to feel because they should be using magic instead is not really a fair thing to say. Similarly you don\u2019t have to magic all the time in mage, there are mundane abilities in there for a reason.<br /> <br /> and sure, you didn\u2019t literally say he was wrong, but that is what is implied if your counter to \u201cI like martial arts manoeuvres\u201d is \u201cyou should be using magic\u201d<br /> <br /> as for your combat boosting effects cast every morning\u2026not always the best option. I don\u2019t know about you but when I walk down the street I don\u2019t to cause gusts of wind from turning too quickly or for my touch to shatter steel, if nothing else it will get the technocracy on your tail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-12-2023, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T14:10:32-07:00","id":1522482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522480#post1522480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the guy said he wanted them to be on another level compared to regular people, and regular people, sleeper or otherwise, aren\u2019t proficient with martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of people in the US with formal martial arts training (not even including pure sports training like most boxing or fencing instruction) is about the same as the number of people with a graduate level degree (across all fields). That's not the majority of people by far, but walking down the street and expecting nobody to have enough dots in Brawl or MA to have extra maneuvers would be a wildly bad assumption to make. The maneuvers in the MA list alone are not going to put you on a completely other level of fighting. Having high stats will mean you win fairly easily against &quot;regular&quot; folks, with or without maneuvers, but it's never going to feel as powerful as the reference point Revan provided than using magic will accomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the statement is about what they find martial arts manoeuvres add to the experience for them. </div> </div> </div>It's a statement that defies logic, so I challenged it. Challenging such statements is a form of gaining understanding. Something you say you're all about doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Telling them that this is the wrong thing to feel because they should be using magic instead is not really a fair thing to say. </div> </div> </div>When you can go a few posts without lying about what I actually said, I'll give a shit about what you consider &quot;a fair thing to say.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly you don\u2019t have to magic all the time in mage, there are mundane abilities in there for a reason. </div> </div> </div>Which is why a &quot;martial arts mage,&quot; spends their limited time focusing on martial arts magic in the regular prep rituals; instead of the hundreds of other thing they could be making sure they have a magical edge in. That's why a huge amount of what I gave as examples are combining magical and mundane skills, not just prepping some fireballs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and sure, you didn\u2019t literally say he was wrong, but that is what is implied if your counter to \u201cI like martial arts manoeuvres\u201d is \u201cyou should be using magic\u201d </div> </div> </div>Is it fun to admit that you know I didn't say something, but still accuse me of saying it because you decided &quot;implications&quot; can mean whatever you want them to mean?<br /> <br /> I didn't counter, &quot;I like MA maneuvers&quot; with, &quot;you should be using magic.&quot; I countered, &quot;martial arts maneuvers let me feel like my mage is superior to normal fighters,&quot; with, &quot;you should be using magic, because normal fighters have access to all those maneuvers too, and what they don't have is magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as for your combat boosting effects cast every morning\u2026not always the best option. I don\u2019t know about you but when I walk down the street I don\u2019t to cause gusts of wind from turning too quickly or for my touch to shatter steel, if nothing else it will get the technocracy on your tail. </div> </div> </div>So... I'm wrong because you house rule the game? Or do you have a citation of where casting magic to give your strikes more damage causes noticeable wind currents when you turn or shatters steel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T15:14:33-07:00","id":1522487,"title":"","content":"[/QUOTE]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The number of people in the US with formal martial arts training (not even including pure sports training like most boxing or fencing instruction) is about the same as the number of people with a graduate level degree (across all fields). That's not the majority of people by far, but walking down the street and expecting nobody to have enough dots in Brawl or MA to have extra maneuvers would be a wildly bad assumption to make. The maneuvers in the MA list alone are not going to put you on a completely other level of fighting. Having high stats will mean you win fairly easily against &quot;regular&quot; folks, with or without maneuvers, but it's never going to feel as powerful as the reference point Revan provided than using magic will accomplish.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl perhaps, though martial arts is a bit more niche, most practitioners would only go as far as a single dot.<br /> <br /> but all that aside, what exactly is wrong about enjoying the fact they have access to the snake step for a vastly improved dodge option or a vital strike to enforce some lethal damage with their hands alone and no need to invoke effects?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a statement that defies logic, so I challenged it. Challenging such statements is a form of gaining understanding. Something you say you're all about doing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>which is why I\u2019m addressing it, in an effort to aid in your desire to understand<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you can go a few posts without lying about what I actually said, I'll give a shit about what you consider &quot;a fair thing to say.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lying does imply intent, which is not an accurate accusation. Do you genuinely think I am intentionally creating falsehoods about you? Is it not more likely that things are being misinterpreted, likely in both directions?<br /> <br /> I am not your enemy man. I have no desire to hurt you. It may help to be aware that I have a cognitive disability, Dyspraxia specifically if you need to know. Part of the problems this gives me is an inability to recall exact words at the point of use, and so I often find myself in need of second best terms in order to push the thought out of my head and on to the page before it goes away.<br /> this coupled with dyslexia, which makes it difficult for me to even recall the exact wording of something I read even as I read it, leads to quite a frequent rate of misinterpretation<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t often feel comfortable bringing this up because in the past others have used it as a justification to admonish me. i\u2019ve even been told I should stop engaging in WoD entirely as the hobby which is 90% reading since I obviously am incapable of reading. But I feel the need to explain myself to you for your own peace of mind, so you understand that you are not being maliciously attacked here.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why a &quot;martial arts mage,&quot; spends their limited time focusing on martial arts magic in the regular prep rituals; instead of the hundreds of other thing they could be making sure they have a magical edge in. That's why a huge amount of what I gave as examples are combining magical and mundane skills, not just prepping some fireballs.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>it would help to understand what you mean if you gave some sphere effects in these examples<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it fun to admit that you know I didn't say something, but still accuse me of saying it because you decided &quot;implications&quot; can mean whatever you want them to mean?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I added this in as a way to show I recognise you have a tendency to fixate on exact wording at the expense of intent. This was my attempt to better communicate what my intent was in that statement.<br /> <br /> to elaborate further, your main complaint to their statement is mundane manoeuvres should not be considered as extraordinary, only magic should be considered as extraordinary. I get this from your response of \u201cbut those aren\u2019t magic\u201d as he describes using martial arts to be at another level, (which I paraphrase as to mean extraordinary in case the departure from exact wording should frustrate). Now, you are saying that using martial arts is insufficient to being extraordinary, this is what I understand from your statements regarding how any sleeper can do it. You then make the case that magic is instead required to be extraordinary, this is what I understand from your statements that magic is what separates your from everyone else, especially in this context of being a martial artist.<br /> <br /> so taking the idea that martial arts is insufficient for being extraordinary and magic is necessary for being extraordinary, I conclude that it is therefore wrong to consider yourself extraordinary when using mundane martial arts.<br /> <br /> And this is how I came to this understanding, all based on statements you did make and how they must logically work together without being inconsistent. And I present them to you for review and correction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't counter, &quot;I like MA maneuvers&quot; with, &quot;you should be using magic.&quot; I countered, &quot;martial arts maneuvers let me feel like my mage is superior to normal fighters,&quot; with, &quot;you should be using magic, because normal fighters have access to all those maneuvers too, and what they don't have is magic.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why should they? If it is not necessary, then the shouldn\u2019t need to use magic, but if it is necessary, as the word \u2018should\u2019 does imply, then would that not mean not using magic means they cannot feel like their mage is superior to normal fighters?<br /> <br /> and if this is the case, that they cannot feel like their mage is superior without using magic, how is that different from saying to feel superior without using magic is simply wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522482#post1522482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... I'm wrong because you house rule the game? Or do you have a citation of where casting magic to give your strikes more damage causes noticeable wind currents when you turn or shatters steel?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are examples of the sorts of effects mages have over themselves to enhance their combat capability. As you didn\u2019t provide your own examples of what a martial arts mage might use, I provided my own.<br /> <br /> A mage with Forces magic might use Forces to enhance their jumps, encouraging a gust of wind to follow them as they move. While a mage with Matter magic might have their hands capable of causing armour to crumble at their touch.<br /> <br /> the point is more that if you have an ongoing active effecr, then it stays on in every context, not just combat, and the concequences of this can be quite troublesom, disincentivising this as a common practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T15:29:02-07:00","id":1522490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522473#post1522473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, but if the only thing this adds is an appeal to your personal preferences on granularity, are you acknowledging that it therefore doesn't add anything for those of us that think the game doesn't get better with this level of granularity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understood what you said, but no, it adds mechanics like increases and decreases of difficulty and damage. It's not like they just get the &quot;strike&quot; maneuver and splitted it into several mechanically equal maneuvers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522473#post1522473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... those aren't magical maneuvers. A Sleeper with Brawl 3 and a mage with Brawl 3 are equals unless the mage uses magic to enhance themselves further. The mage is on another level by applying magic (or having specific Backgrounds/Merits of supernatural origin, etc.)... just like anything else. Virtual Adepts aren't better hackers than regular human hackers because of some special L337 coding stuff that's just special training. They use their magic to do stuff Sleepers can't do, or do normal things way better than what Sleepers do. Why should fighting be any different? Magic can boost your Physical Attributes, give your attacks bonus damage, reduce the difficulty of your combat Ability of choice across the board, boost your Initiative, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want a martial arts mage that kicks serious ass, the hours of practice they do should be ritual castings to boost their combat prowess with magic. Not only is that how the game works in general, it's also going to get you way farther than a long list of combat maneuvers anyone can learn ever will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was comparing someone without a proper, serious training from a martial artist, not necessarily a mage and a sleeper.<br /> <br /> If you have a boxing bag at home and threw some punches regularly, you might have brawl 1 or 2. <br /> If you practiced years of Muay Thai, you should know how to punch, kick, knee, elbow, etc better than someone who haven\u2019t trained it. And this distinction will be very poor if you remove martial arts and have only a brawl trait. You *could* say that the first example is someone that have 1-2 in brawl and the thai fighter is represented by having 3+ in brawl. But that 2 dices wouldn't represent the distance between them mechanically, while the maneuvers do, due to the increased efficiency (more damage and/or rediced diff, etc) some of them have.<br /> <br /> I want my Thai fighter to be able to hurt more than someone that have no martial training. The same would apply for Jiu Jitsu. Bjj is the ultimate art of ground combat and having it under the umbrella of &quot;brawl&quot; with only grapple as ground maneuver just sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522473#post1522473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing other splats can't get is Do. Martial Arts as a separate Ability didn't start in Mage. IIRC WtA got up to three different unique combat styles as well. If you want Bullet Time combat tricks... that's what Time 3 is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and if you want your mage to be even better than regular martial artists (sleepers, mages or night folks), you can get Do. That's why I also think Do should be a trait (and one that shouldn't be as restricted as it seems to be).<br /> <br /> Other splats can get martial arts, but it isn't their thing. Why punch when you can claw and bite with agg damage?<br /> <br /> Now, other splats can't improve their natural attacks as efficiently as mages. And that's my point. While other splats *can* get martial arts, only mages can be very, <b>very</b> deadly using it, due to magick.<br /> <br /> You can remove martial arts and it's maneuvers and use brawl and magick instead. But why do that, if you can have (and it's raw) both? You can have cool maneuvers that get even better when improved by magick. And this way mages have at least a better chance to go hand to hand with other splats or any kind of strong enemy that should crush a mortal.<br /> <br /> Being very honest here, I see absolutely no advantage in removing the traits and maneuvers from the game. If a player don't want them, just don't get the trait...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T18:14:55-07:00","id":1522495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522487#post1522487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lying does imply intent, which is not an accurate accusation. Do you genuinely think I am intentionally creating falsehoods about you? Is it not more likely that things are being misinterpreted, likely in both directions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saikou, I\u2019m pretty sure that part of the problem here is that you keep trying to \u201cinterpret\u201d instead of listening to what others actually say. You\u2019re extrapolating, and trying to divine intent, and otherwise attempting to add meaning to what others say. And at least sometimes you\u2019re doing it even when you know they haven\u2019t said what you are interpreting from their words.<br /> <br /> Like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522487#post1522487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are examples of the sorts of effects mages have over themselves to enhance their combat capability. As you didn\u2019t provide your own examples of what a martial arts mage might use, I provided my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as you provide your own examples like this, you are working with what <i>you</i> said, not what Heavy Arms said.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a term for what you did there. You constructed a <i>straw man</i>. It\u2019s very poor rhetorical form.<br /> <br /> If you fill in the gaps in what somebody else said with information that makes their position look like nonsense, it\u2019s not their position that is nonsense. It\u2019s a position held only by the straw man you have constructed. It\u2019s <i>your</i> straw man, which means the nonsense is yours too.<br /> <br /> Attacking a straw man does nothing to refute their actual position. But it is a form of disinformation about their position.<br /> <br /> If you genuinely want to understand their position, and you think they have failed to provide information that is necessary to do that, the appropriate thing to do is ask. \u201cI don\u2019t know what sort of effects you are talking about. Would you mind providing an example of the sort of effect that you see a martial artist mage using to gain superior combat abilities?\u201d (Not that it is hard to find such effects yourself. Start with Magick Enhances Violence, probably the simplest approach to enhancing combat ability. The fact that a simple difficulty reduction, simply Magick making difficult feats easy, is not your first example does not make you look genuine in your attempts to understand.)<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t a result of dyspraxia. You knew that Heavy Arms didn\u2019t say anything about gusts of wind or shattering steel with a touch. Dyspraxia doesn\u2019t cause that sort of misinterpretation. Neither does dyslexia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T23:08:04-07:00","id":1522500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522487#post1522487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl perhaps, though martial arts is a bit more niche, most practitioners would only go as far as a single dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on... what? The statistics I cited are based in enrollment in martial arts studios. So places that teach karate, taekwando, and judo (by far the three most popular in the US), as well as other formal styles. Military, police, and other agencies also make up a significant portion of that with their own specialized combat training. Why are they all learning Brawl in a martial arts studio instead of... Martial Arts? How do you draw the line?<br /> <br /> How do you have Dirty Fighting locked off at Brawl 3, if successfully completely any rigorous self-defense training course requires Brawl 3 because (as explicitly stated in M20) those tactics are used to injure attackers suddenly and harshly to buy time to escape, and treat Brawl 3 as relatively rare?<br /> <br /> I finished high-school having had to use five of the moves listed in the MA list... so I apparently already had MA 3 before I was 18... and I wasn't that good or that special as a fighter. So why say that MA 2+ would be so rare? And as I've pointed out, if you look at the other combat Abilities that don't have these considerations, someone with Melee 2 has apparently mastered a vastly wider array of techniques given all the different weapons they can use without extra cost, than someone with Brawl 3 and MA 3 would really have.<br /> <br /> This is actually a significant problem with having both Brawl and Martial Arts as core traits. Exalted was the only ST family game that tried this from the beginning, and it gave up on it too. It always ends up in the same place: Brawl with Martial Arts (in whatever form) as something extra you apply on top of Brawl. This idea that you can maintain some sort of coherent narrative distinction between different ways of learning to fight just doesn't hold up. The efforts to uphold a distinction between Brawl and MA always end up hurting the verisimilitude of the game instead of helping it feel more &quot;real&quot; because the line feels more and more arbitrary over time. Street fighters that fight long enough pick up things besides dirty fighting because striking vital points is striking vital points it doesn't matter if it's a &quot;dirty&quot; knee to the balls, or a &quot;graceful&quot; strike to the vagus nerve... you're just hitting weak spots. An expert in &quot;Brawl&quot; isn't dumb and know how to hit less obvious weak spots. An expert in &quot;Martial Arts&quot; knows that in real fights against opponents that mean you harm or death, the balls aren't off limits like they are in a competitive match.<br /> <br /> And the rest of the system isn't this granular. &quot;Craft&quot; is a single Ability. Craft doesn't give a shit if you're mostly self taught with maybe some YouTube videos to help you with stuff, or if you apprentice with a master crafts-person for years. Craft 3 is Craft 3, how you get their is story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But all that aside, what exactly is wrong about enjoying the fact they have access to the snake step for a vastly improved dodge option or a vital strike to enforce some lethal damage with their hands alone and no need to invoke effects? </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't have a problem with the concept of maneuvers. I have a problem with the execution of them. I certainly think an execution of maneuvers that replaces the role of magic is a mistake in a game about mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lying does imply intent, which is not an accurate accusation. </div> </div> </div>Yous stated your intent when you admitted to treating &quot;implications&quot; as my actual statement. Travis detailed the specifics for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not your enemy man. I have no desire to hurt you. </div> </div> </div>To modify an old analogy of mine: there comes a point where it doesn't matter. If you keep deciding to practice punches near me with no intention of hitting me, and you keep hitting me anyway, your initial intent is overridden by your intent to continue despite the results. Malice and negligence aren't the same morally, but they're the same practically in how I am going to respond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it would help to understand what you mean if you gave some sphere effects in these examples </div> </div> </div>I gave examples straight out of the core book. Increasing your physical Attributes is Life 3, increasing your damage is easiest under Entropy 1 via Spot Weakness, you can increase you Initiative by increasing Dex with Life and Wits with Mind 1 (though the forum has had discussions of other methods since it seems like you should be able to do that more directly), and reducing the difficulties of your mundane rolls with magic is something described in the general rules and the combat rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> to elaborate further, your main complaint to their statement is mundane manoeuvres should not be considered as extraordinary, only magic should be considered as extraordinary. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say extraordinary because that's too subjective; Str/Dex/Sta 3 and MA 3 is extraordinary compared to Str/Dex/Sta 1 and Brawl 0. It's a relative term of limited use in this conversation. I focused on the fact that the maneuvers are also accessible to Sleepers because of the phrasing and examples Revan used don't work if that's the case.<br /> <br /> Just as a note, Revan name-check the Matrix. Let's go back to 1999 and remember what sort of stuff Trinity (who is not the strongest fighter in the main cast) did at the very beginning of the Matrix:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MXcy639mTVY\" data-code=\"MXcy639mTVY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MXcy639mTVY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That is not Martial Arts vs. Brawl and Firearms. That's magic enhancing violence. That's why the stunt crew needed wires to actually pull it off, since even highly skilled stunt fighters can't do that on their own. This level of difference requires magic. That's explicitly so in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why should they? </div> </div> </div>Because that's the tool the book provides to meet the goal stated at the level stated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are examples of the sorts of effects mages have over themselves to enhance their combat capability. </div> </div> </div>Please back this up with references to anything in the books, esp. the part where having longer duration buffs means you can't use them selectively.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Lord Revan;n1522490]I was comparing someone without a proper, serious training from a martial artist, not necessarily a mage and a sleeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this distinction will be very poor if you remove martial arts and have only a brawl trait </div> </div> </div>The Martial Arts trait wasn't even added to the WoD until KotE game out. It wasn't added to Mage until M20. A lot of us got by without it for a very long time and didn't have &quot;poor&quot; experiences because we didn't have a list of extra moves. Brawl 1-2 being amateurs and Brawl 3+ being skilled fighters worked just fine, because high Brawl characters had big dice-pools, that let them use multiple actions to easily defeat low Brawl characters: If you have 4 dice for your Dex + Brawl pool (regardless of edition), you're going to lose to someone with 8 dice because you're stuck praying the dice save your ass multiple times as there's no tactical move you have that turns a straight up fight in your favor when they can attack and defend, and you can either do one barely on their level, or both extremely poorly.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the simple idea that well trained fighters are also going to have high Physical Attributes and high Wits to help them perform considerably better than &quot;average&quot; types. Garou aren't scary because they get Brawl boosts in their combat forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want my Thai fighter to be able to hurt more than someone that have no martial training. </div> </div> </div>Does your martial artist not also do full body training? Putting 7 dots in Physical Attributes at creation with 3 dots in Brawl will destroy an &quot;average&quot; person with 2s in their Physicals and Brawl 0-2. No maneuvers required for that.<br /> <br /> Also, lets remember that Travis and I aren't advocating for nothing special for highly trained martial artists... just a different way of expressing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other splats can get martial arts, but it isn't their thing. </div> </div> </div>Odd thing to say when it started in a VtM supplement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why punch when you can claw and bite with agg damage? </div> </div> </div>Most supernaturals don't start with the innate ability to bite and claw for Agg. Yes, Garou do, they get a lot of combat stuff in their package. Vampires only bite for agg, and have to grapple to do that, or need to buy powers for more options. Changelings don't have any default claw/bite attacks as a splat, let alone Agg ones, and neither do Wraiths, as again, those are bought powers. Should I continue into the later games? Or is the point sufficient?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's my point. While other splats *can* get martial arts, only mages can be very, <b>very</b> deadly using it, due to magick. </div> </div> </div>That's... not really anything backed up by the rules. Brujah have a Combo Discipline to get Agg natural attacks without having to get someone to teach them Protean or Serpentis, which is completely compatible with Martial Arts... and uses Potence and Celerity. It's very deadly. Changelings also have plenty of ways they'd being obnoxiously deadly with Martial Arts if their books included them. The Stargazers invented a martial art specifically to be compliment their forms. The idea that mages are unique here just does not follow with any of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can remove martial arts and it's maneuvers and use brawl and magick instead.<br /> ...<br /> Being very honest here, I see absolutely no advantage in removing the traits and maneuvers from the game. If a player don't want them, just don't get the trait... </div> </div> </div>As has been discussed, repeatedly, your issue is that you assume nothing is replacing what is being removed; despite the house rule being discussed absolutely doing so; just a with a focus on narrative important rather than a very particular concept of &quot;realism.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T00:13:01-07:00","id":1522502,"title":"","content":"I have been lurking in this thread because between the discussion of debate etiquette there are some interesting points about the actual mechanics. Having a Stargazer player who uses some Kailindo has me interested in possible alternatives.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to bring two points in I haven't either seen discussed yet or missed:<br /> <br /> 1. There is a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Combat\" target=\"_blank\">WOD supplement</a> completely focused on expanded combat options, including supernatural MA. IIRC it's based on the Street Fighter RPG system. I haven't used it and was hoping to see some discussion on how it compares- but maybe it's also of interest to some of the parties in this thread. It's pretty old, though.<br /> <br /> 2. On a meta level, having more combat options has the benefit of allowing a player to choose their options tactically. As long as the effects are diversified enough to make a difference, choosing the right option at the right time can be really <i>fun</i>. Resolving this narratively is of course always an option, but does not feel the same as having crunch behind it. The fun comes from making a decision from a list of options that is diverse enough to <i>have </i>options, at least for me. Hit-Grapple-Knockdown is good enough for most characters, but for a dedicated fighter character this would be like having a sorcerer with a total of three spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T00:27:51-07:00","id":1522503,"title":"","content":"On your point regarding Craft, there actually is a leve of granularity in the system. Upon choosing a craft, you must pick a speciality on what thpe of craft your are doing, be it wood work, scrap metal, glassblowing, textiles, etc. and then this is what your craft experience will be localised to. If you have craft Textiles then you will be unable to use for craft knowledge for something like metalwork or pottery, though anything tabgentle to textiles like sewing, dressmaking, etc could benefit if at a higher difficulty.<br /> <br /> and in regards to Rank 3 locking away dirty manuvrrs for Brawl, this is actually wuite a common thing for a lot of abilities. Awareness 3 is required to read auras, pilot 3 is requires for certain aircrafts, military vehicles require at least Drive 3, hypertech 3 is the minimum to start modifying Devices, Medicine 3 to heal health levels. It\u2019s a pretty consistent thing that certain uses of an ability don\u2019t unlock until higher ratings are achieved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I gave examples straight out of the core book. Increasing your physical Attributes is Life 3, increasing your damage is easiest under Entropy 1 via Spot Weakness, you can increase you Initiative by increasing Dex with Life and Wits with Mind 1 (though the forum has had discussions of other methods since it seems like you should be able to do that more directly), and reducing the difficulties of your mundane rolls with magic is something described in the general rules and the combat rules.\u200b </div> </div> </div>ok, so, persistent Life or Mind effects to increase attributes can invoke pattern bleed, and one could argue that turning it on and off every morning doesn\u2019t get the body sufficient recovery time if done for a pronged period. Pattern bleed being loss of health levels without the expenditure of quintessence. So having life effects up to increase stats all the time isn\u2019t always ideal<br /> Increasing dots above 5, entering supernatural levels for a prolonged period, results in permanent paradox in addition. Which again, is not always ideal. Revised had this as being the case for any and every attempt as such effects, though M20 softened this to attempts to make such changes permanent, but one could argue that if someone is casting these effects on themselves every morning, there comes a point where the distinction between permanent and temporary in how the body reacts starts to blend together. It does get ST dependent, but I would say it is a kind ST who allows their player to skirt the consequences of permanency like this.<br /> <br /> As for Entropy 1, it shouldn\u2019t be a big issue so long as your mage doesn\u2019t try to do any other sensory effects, as the more sensory effects the mage has going at once, the higher the difficulty climbs for Perception based rolls. But this isn\u2019t actually terribly relevant regarding the domino effect, sibce sensory effects do not impact it.<br /> <br /> I bring this up to counter your claim that such a mage would not care about the domino effect and thus would have no reason to prefer mundane martial arts over magically enhanced attacks. It is interesting to note, however, that these examples do not actually replaced martial arts so much as make the mage that uses martial arts more prone to success. The effects you describe here add to the dice pool or reduce difficulty, generally speaking such a mage without martial arts vs such a mage with martial arts would see the mage with martial arts have the upperhand generally speaking.<br /> <br /> my examples instead were an attempt to get around the need for martial arts by using magic, as describe in the martial arts section of HDYDT. Matter being used to damage armour as stated in the basics, or Forces to direct the winds as written under Chi-field push. If one were to advocate for magic to replace the need for martial arts, then it would be these kinds of effects which would be better suited to this, rather than effects which would make martial arts rolls better. Magic that only increases attributes and lowers combat diff could even be argued to rely on the martial arts ability in order to achieve the sort of feats displayed in the matrix.<br /> <br /> when it comes to the unintended consequences of prolonged effects, I refer to this passage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, too, that a small field of unusual physics will<br /> be both weird and noticeable\u2026 and probably inconvenient, as<br /> well. Sure, that deflection field on your jacket may be really<br /> useful in a fight, but it\u2019s gonna look really damned strange<br /> when you take your jacket off and it starts to slide around<br /> because it\u2019s being deflected from every other surface that isn\u2019t<br /> you! Oh, and that jacket will deflect other things too \u2013 your<br /> boyfriend\u2019s hand, the seat you try to sit down on, the gun you<br /> try to shove in the jacket\u2019s pocket\u2026\u200b </div> </div> </div>While an effect remains active, the effect\u2019s properties cannot be turned on or off outside of dismissing the effect. So any strange quirks of physics, luck, or perception you put on yourself will remain in place until you dismiss the effect. There is nothing in the book to suggest that an active effect can be temporarily switched off while it is still active.<br /> <br /> i am imagining these as ongoing effects rather than, as I believe they are intended to be, point of use effects in the midst of combat, and when taken as ongoing effects, the consequences are that they will do strange things as you walk about.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I hope that\u2019s clarified what I mean in regards to sphere magic, and why I concluded as I had.<br /> <br /> I would like to ask you, how exactly would you prefer Martial Arts to be executed? Do you wish to simply roll it in to brawl and have a roll to strike be mechanistically the same regardless of who is doing it?<br /> <br /> because if this is what is being asked for, then I have trouble seeing the difference between better executing martial arts and removing the mechanic entirely.<br /> <br /> that the only difference between a martial artist and a standard brawler is that if a brawler gets 5 successes, you describe a chokehold, and if a martial artist gets 5 successes, you describing a flying kick, this seems somewhat surface level. The difference is entirely flavour, and the mechanic has been removed effectively.<br /> <br /> if this isn\u2019t the case, then I don\u2019t understand what you propose to replace it with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-13-2023, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T06:12:55-07:00","id":1522511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522502#post1522502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. On a meta level, having more combat options has the benefit of allowing a player to choose their options tactically. As long as the effects are diversified enough to make a difference, choosing the right option at the right time can be really <i>fun</i>. Resolving this narratively is of course always an option, but does not feel the same as having crunch behind it. The fun comes from making a decision from a list of options that is diverse enough to <i>have </i>options, at least for me. Hit-Grapple-Knockdown is good enough for most characters, but for a dedicated fighter character this would be like having a sorcerer with a total of three spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this point has been addressed to an extent. My position is in line with yours, that these options present a greater array of choices which can be used to deal with a large variety of scenarios, and preparing in the even of a scenario or even coming up with a tactic to lead towards a particular scenario that relies on said manoeuvres is indeed a merit of the system as it stands.<br /> <br /> the argument against this however is that the choices presented in M20 do not actually allow for this, since some are mechanically superior than others, and the scenarios in which the lesser moves would be better options are so niche that they don\u2019t actually come up enough to justify their appearance. That instead you have a series of almost never used moves that simply clog up the sheet and leave players feeling bewildered to the point of not even wanting to play with it. Which is why there is a proposed change to make the exact way one accomplished a feat dependent on the successes rolled rather than on the feat chosen.<br /> <br /> tactics instead wouldn\u2019t be based on manuvres, but on telling the ST \u201cI want to do this to the guy\u201d and if you get a lot of successes, the ST lets you say what extra things you do in line with your stated intention prior to the roll.<br /> <br /> it shifts from choosing out of a list of options to coming up with a specific approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-13-2023, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T08:02:56-07:00","id":1522512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522511#post1522511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tactics instead wouldn\u2019t be based on manuvres, but on telling the ST \u201cI want to do this to the guy\u201d and if you get a lot of successes, the ST lets you say what extra things you do in line with your stated intention prior to the roll.<br /> <br /> it shifts from choosing out of a list of options to coming up with a specific approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. There is still the possibility of options that allow for similar tactical decision-making. We would just decouple that tactical decision from the specific moves.<br /> <br /> To an extent, such mechanics already exist. The Targeting a Location rule allows trading off difficulty for extra damage (although the +1 version of that is exactly as effective as using Kick instead of Punch - which is to say, only very debatably useful), and this lends itself to being generalised a bit - it becomes reasonable to apply that same mechanic to any time of high-risk, high-reward combat tactic. The choice to take a full-pool attack itself is a tactical choice, as arguably it is more reasonable to assume that combatants by default split their pool between attack and defence; so really a typical combat round is already asking a character to make a tactical choice between Desperate Defense (everything into defense, so much so that it rolls more dice in total against multiple attacks), all-out attack (no dice in defence), or a balance between attack and defence (with some form of split). Martial artist mages, of course, also have the choice of how to allocate their Arete; Magick Enhances Violence can easily lower either attack or defence difficulties, or damage can be enhanced in several ways.<br /> <br /> These are real tactical choices that the player is being asked to make. And compare that to the scenario that keeps coming out in defence of Kick: \u201cWhat if the character\u2019s arms are immobilised?\u201d Well, if the character can\u2019t use their arms, this isn\u2019t a tactical choice at all. They use Kick because it\u2019s the only remaining option. If they have an enhanced kicking maneuver, they\u2019ll just use that instead.<br /> <br /> Under the standard M20 rules, though, extra successes really aren\u2019t very effective. They just convert to extra damage dice, and half of those will fail to convert into actual damage (even before soak). It\u2019s my thought that if rolling extra successes allows for extra options - especially options more useful than an extra die of bashing damage - tactics that enhance the probability of rolling extra successes become more viable.<br /> <br /> What I would like to put together is a set of options that any character can use, but which become more effective when employed by characters with higher dice pools or traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T09:15:19-07:00","id":1522514,"title":"","content":"A quick analysis of what Martial Artist actually gives through maneuvers\u2026<br /> <br /> Without MA, our basic strikes are:<br /> Punch: our baseline (6 difficulty, Strength/B damage); other maneuvers will be compared to this.<br /> Kick: effectively baseline with the first level of Target a Location applied, ignoring any special effects an ST might give via fiat.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1:<br /> Strike: -1 difficulty, +1 damage (if hard style: no difficulty modifier if soft)<br /> Elbow/Knee Strike: -1 difficulty, +1 damage<br /> Snap Kick: -1 difficulty, +1 damage (only available in hard style)<br /> <br /> So the real effect here is -1 difficulty, +1 damage at MA 1. Note that this is just plain better than Brawl already, not just a parallel approach.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2:<br /> Spinning Kick: +0 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> Joint Lock: -1 difficulty, no bonus damage but inflicts Dex+MA/L instead of Strength/B<br /> Vital Strike: +1 difficulty, no extra dice to damage pool but damage becomes Lethal.<br /> <br /> Joint Lock is complicated to analyse, but the basic damaging move is effectively 1 extra damage die on top of Elbow Strike, plus a level of Target a Location.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 3:<br /> Death Strike: -1 difficulty, +2 damage, damage becomes lethal<br /> Nerve Strike: +1 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> Thunder Kick: +1 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> <br /> Apart from the option to inflict lethal damage, this is the same as Elbow Strike plus two levels of Target a Location.<br /> <br /> I know I\u2019m leaving out all the maneuvers that do something other than inflict damage, but for the purpose of working out how much sheer power Martial Arts adds, just looking at the damaging moves gives the best indicator; at least we compare apples to apples to some extent.<br /> <br /> And the truth is that, in this regard, using MA is just plain better than Brawl, but doesn\u2019t really become more so with additional dots. And if we desire to make extremely skilled martial artists stand out even without magic, this doesn\u2019t really do that, It makes MA better than the same number of dots of Brawling, but 4 and 5 dots do little more than add an extra die to the pool.<br /> <br /> (Editing in some corrections.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-13-2023, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T10:56:30-07:00","id":1522520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as a note, Revan name-check the Matrix. Let's go back to 1999 and remember what sort of stuff Trinity (who is not the strongest fighter in the main cast) did at the very beginning of the Matrix:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MXcy639mTVY\" data-code=\"MXcy639mTVY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MXcy639mTVY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That is not Martial Arts vs. Brawl and Firearms. That's magic enhancing violence. That's why the stunt crew needed wires to actually pull it off, since even highly skilled stunt fighters can't do that on their own. This level of difference requires magic. That's explicitly so in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, cool. I never said I wanted to do those things with martial arts alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Martial Arts trait wasn't even added to the WoD until KotE game out. It wasn't added to Mage until M20. A lot of us got by without it for a very long time and didn't have &quot;poor&quot; experiences because we didn't have a list of extra moves. Brawl 1-2 being amateurs and Brawl 3+ being skilled fighters worked just fine, because high Brawl characters had big dice-pools, that let them use multiple actions to easily defeat low Brawl characters: If you have 4 dice for your Dex + Brawl pool (regardless of edition), you're going to lose to someone with 8 dice because you're stuck praying the dice save your ass multiple times as there's no tactical move you have that turns a straight up fight in your favor when they can attack and defend, and you can either do one barely on their level, or both extremely poorly.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the simple idea that well trained fighters are also going to have high Physical Attributes and high Wits to help them perform considerably better than &quot;average&quot; types. Garou aren't scary because they get Brawl boosts in their combat forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, cool. It didn't exist before, I also never said it was necessary. Just a good improvement. And I already adressed that in my last post, which you seemed to ignore. Haveing 2 dice more isn't going to make much difference. And it certainly won't make as much difference as having the maneuvers. Maneuvers can add +3 to damage, while reducing difficulty and/or deaking letha damage. That's huge, compared to getting 2 more dices. You are also adding attributes in your calculations, when you shouldn't, since Dex is not directly related to having martial arts training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does your martial artist not also do full body training? Putting 7 dots in Physical Attributes at creation with 3 dots in Brawl will destroy an &quot;average&quot; person with 2s in their Physicals and Brawl 0-2. No maneuvers required for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He might or he might not. That's not the point. Strength and Dexterity do not represent martial arts training and you know that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, lets remember that Travis and I aren't advocating for nothing special for highly trained martial artists... just a different way of expressing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, I don't know exactly what the fuck you guys are advocating other than to remove the maneuvers and put everything under the umbrella of &quot;strike&quot; and &quot;grapple&quot;. And that &quot;choosing action after rolling&quot; crazyness. None of that helps in the point I'm making. Oh, and wwhen I asked for a more detailed, an example of your house-rules I was told that it's not my place to ask, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd thing to say when it started in a VtM supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter where it started. My point is that other splats aren't as focused in martial arts as mages, because they have better options by default. And when I say other splats, I mean Vampire and Wereolf, I don't know enough of the rest to make any argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most supernaturals don't start with the innate ability to bite and claw for Agg. Yes, Garou do, they get a lot of combat stuff in their package. Vampires only bite for agg, and have to grapple to do that, or need to buy powers for more options. Changelings don't have any default claw/bite attacks as a splat, let alone Agg ones, and neither do Wraiths, as again, those are bought powers. Should I continue into the later games? Or is the point sufficient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are not that combat oriented in the first place, and the ones who are, normally will relly on some kind of agg damage, like claws (protean is not that rare) and bites (every vampire have it). The only clan that would probably focus on that would be Brujah. Maybe Assamites, but they also have way better ways to kill than throwing punches. <br /> <br /> Garou have their claws and bites, the only time they wouldn't use that is when they don't want to reveal their wolf nature. But in a all out, close combat fight? Yeah, they are not going to throw punches. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not really anything backed up by the rules. Brujah have a Combo Discipline to get Agg natural attacks without having to get someone to teach them Protean or Serpentis, which is completely compatible with Martial Arts... and uses Potence and Celerity. It's very deadly. Changelings also have plenty of ways they'd being obnoxiously deadly with Martial Arts if their books included them. The Stargazers invented a martial art specifically to be compliment their forms. The idea that mages are unique here just does not follow with any of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe your argument is in line with my point. You need a specific combo discipline of Celerity 3+ Potence 3 to improve h2h combat, while <b>every</b> mage can get an improvement in hand to hand with practically any sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522500#post1522500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been discussed, repeatedly, your issue is that you assume nothing is replacing what is being removed; despite the house rule being discussed absolutely doing so; just a with a focus on narrative important rather than a very particular concept of &quot;realism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it was not being discussed and I was told to shut the fuck up when I asked. Since you failed to argue against my points, let us try again, shall we?<br /> <br /> What I understood until now you want to:<br /> <br /> - Remove all maneuvers and leave only new basic ones: &quot;strike&quot; and &quot;grapple&quot;<br /> <br /> - Remove all diff and dmg modifiers. They all have diff 6 and deal Str damage.<br /> <br /> -Roll before the player chooses what will be done<br /> <br /> Is that correct? If it's not, feel free to correct me, I might have mixed things up in this sea of texts that this thread has become.<br /> <br /> If it is, i fail to see how that can help in my point, since it only makes hand to hand combat dull and weaker.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T11:19:53-07:00","id":1522522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522514#post1522514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick analysis of what Martial Artist actually gives through maneuvers\u2026<br /> <br /> Without MA, our basic strikes are:<br /> Punch: our baseline (6 difficulty, Strength/B damage); other maneuvers will be compared to this.<br /> Kick: effectively baseline with the first level of Target a Location applied, ignoring any special effects an ST might give via fiat.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1:<br /> Strike: -1 difficulty, +1 damage (if hard style: no difficulty modifier if soft)<br /> Elbow/Knee Strike: -1 difficulty, +1 damage<br /> Snap Kick: -1 difficulty, +1 damage (only available in hard style)<br /> <br /> So the real effect here is -1 difficulty, +1 damage at MA 1. Note that this is just plain better than Brawl already, not just a parallel approach.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2:<br /> Spinning Kick: +0 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> Joint Lock: -1 difficulty, no bonus damage but inflicts Dex+MA/L instead of Strength/B<br /> Vital Strike: +2 difficulty, no extra dice to damage pool but damage becomes Lethal.<br /> <br /> Joint Lock is complicated to analyse, but the basic damaging move is effectively 1 extra damage die on top of Elbow Strike, plus a level of Target a Location.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 3:<br /> Death Strike: -1 difficulty, +2 damage, damage becomes lethal<br /> Nerve Strike: +2 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> Thunder Kick: +2 difficulty, +3 damage<br /> <br /> Apart from the option to inflict lethal damage, this is actually worse than Elbow Strike plus three levels of Target a Location.<br /> <br /> I know I\u2019m leaving out all the maneuvers that do something other than inflict damage, but for the purpose of working out how much sheer power Martial Arts adds, just looking at the damaging moves gives the best indicator; at least we compare apples to apples to some extent.<br /> <br /> And the truth is that, in this regard, using MA is just plain better than Brawl, but doesn\u2019t really become more so with additional dots. And if we desire to make extremely skilled martial artists stand out even without magic, this doesn\u2019t really do that, It makes MA better than the same number of dots of Brawling, but 4 and 5 dots do little more than add an extra die to the pool.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>minor correction, Thunder kick actually does far more damage than you have considered.<br /> <br /> the damage done is strength, plus 3, plus successes rolled on the attack as bashing damage. So if you got 4 successes on the hit, that translates to (assuming 3 strength) 3+3+4 dice, plus the usual 3 overflow successes, giving you a total of 13 damage dice.<br /> you essentially double the amount of damage each overflow die provides.<br /> it\u2019s an incredibly powerful attack for a mundane ability, which is why it has such a long cool down period.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T15:20:37-07:00","id":1522536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522522#post1522522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> minor correction, Thunder kick actually does far more damage than you have considered.<br /> <br /> the damage done is strength, plus 3, plus successes rolled on the attack as bashing damage. So if you got 4 successes on the hit, that translates to (assuming 3 strength) 3+3+4 dice, plus the usual 3 overflow successes, giving you a total of 13 damage dice.<br /> you essentially double the amount of damage each overflow die provides.<br /> it\u2019s an incredibly powerful attack for a mundane ability, which is why it has such a long cool down period.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s fair.<br /> <br /> Thunder Kick is a maneuver that previously had me wondering whether it was written without considering that successes already add to damage, and whether doubling up the extra dice from successes was really the intent. And how was the original version written, back in the days before extra successes with melee attacks added to damage as a general rule? I\u2019d noted that research was to be done there.<br /> <br /> But the truth is that I wrote that last post lying in bed at night, and by the time I got down to Thunder Kick I was on the edge of sleep and completely forgot about all of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-13-2023, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T04:56:28-07:00","id":1522565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522520#post1522520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it was not being discussed and I was told to shut the fuck up when I asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you weren\u2019t. You were admonished for failing to take up the information already provided for you (at the time) while still asking. I stand by that.<br /> <br /> All that has really been discussed has been to remove the unarmed combat maneuvers, convert those that have subsumed a necessary mechanic (like grappling) into a replacement, somehow enhance the options for using rolled successes beyond converting to extra damage dice, and move the detailed description of what a character does to after the determining the outcome rolls have been made. That leaves a wide variety of possible implementations, and maybe some of us will discuss more details in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T05:30:37-07:00","id":1522566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522565#post1522565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that has really been discussed has been to remove the unarmed combat maneuvers, convert those that have subsumed a necessary mechanic (like grappling) into a replacement, somehow enhance the options for using rolled successes beyond converting to extra damage dice, and move the detailed description of what a character does to after the determining the outcome rolls have been made. That leaves a wide variety of possible implementations, and maybe some of us will discuss more details in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>One compromise option could be to use extra successes to buy additional effects that have an impact for subsequent combat rounds (stun, knockdown, incapacitate, disarm, disable limb, etc) without specifying the exact move. That would leave it flexible to apply to different styles of MA and keep it narratively open. Would be some work to balance out the effect cost table, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T09:04:47-07:00","id":1522575,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here\u2019s the gist of my current thinking for my game. Note that I\u2019m not suggesting this should replace M20 RAW for everyone else\u2019s games. You do what you like.<br /> <br /> MA and Brawl maneuvers all go away. If I find that there\u2019s any specific mechanic in any of them that the game really suffers without, I can look at reimplementing as a stand-alone rule, but I doubt that since all those mechanics are locked away from many characters anyway.<br /> <br /> The Targeting a Location rule gets generalised into a rule that a player can take +1, +2, or +3 on an attack roll in order to get the same number of successes if their attack achieves at least a basic degree of success <i>after defences are applied</i>. I haven\u2019t run the number on this in detail to check the balance. It\u2019s certainly better than getting the same value into damage dice (because extra successes can become damage dice anyway). Players no longer have to describe this as targeting a location; it\u2019s just choosing to accept a higher risk of failure in order to increase the probability of a higher degree of success. As long as you say how your character is taking this risk (before your roll) you can get the modifiers: target a vulnerable (but hard to hit) location, reckless attack, a high-speed flurry of blows without attention to accuracy, whatever. It is possible that I could be convinced to allow higher than a +4 modifier here, which would certainly work well for mages who can use Magick Enhances Violence to offset the penalty, but I\u2019m initially wary of that.<br /> <br /> Various other modifiers to difficulty can still exist. I currently can\u2019t think of any that desperately need to be removed.<br /> <br /> Of the basic maneuvers:<ul><li>Claw and Bite just become weapons.</li> <li>Punch becomes the basic attack-to-damage.</li> <li>Kick is subsumed into the above difficulty trade-off rule.</li> <li>Flank and Rear were really circumstantial modifiers all along, and should never have been called maneuvers.</li> <li>Reading an Opponent can become a separate action working pretty much the same.</li> <li>The Grappling rules suck, frankly, and I\u2019m not going to try to deal with them here. (Grappling rules always suck. They usually bypass the damage system, and are horribly broken one way or another as a result.) Suffice to say that I\u2019m going to replace them wholesale.</li> <li>Sweep and Tackle need to be replaced with a more general rule for knocking people down.</li> <li>Disarm needs to be replaced with a more general rule for depriving opponents of their equipment.</li> </ul>To work out exactly what the outcome of an attack is, declare basic intent (optionally declare anything that modifies the difficulty or die pool), roll the dice, then allocate dice to buy effects and describe in detail how your character achieves those effects.<br /> <br /> Now, because there\u2019s a risk/reward thing going on above, I think I need to make sure that missing that first success bites. To achieve that, certain effects may cost several successes to buy <i>unless bought with the first success</i>. The first success must be used in line with the intent declared before the attack roll <br /> <br /> Effects that can be bought:<ul><li>Deal damage: first success, or 2 successes, for Strength damage<ul><li>+1 damage die: 1 success</li> <li>upgrade to lethal damage: ? successes</li> </ul></li> <li>Outmaneuver: -1/success to difficulties of your future attacks against the target, and +1/success to your target\u2019s difficulties for attacks against you.<ul><li>This is basically how you achieve a flanking position.</li> <li>Generally a symmetrical modifier - if you have +1 against your opponent, your opponent has -1 against you, etc.</li> <li>A character can typically use movement on their turn to automatically negate -1 against them - essentially turning to face a flanking enemy, taking a step back out of danger, etc. This can\u2019t produce a modifier in your favour, unless the ST decides that unusual circumstances apply. Negating a greater penalty may require spending successes on outmaneuvering.</li> </ul></li> <li>Move opponent: first success, or 2 successes, to physically shift someone who does not want to be moved<ul><li>Extra successes can move them further</li> </ul></li> <li>Knock down: 2 success including the first, or 3 successes</li> <li>Disarm: 2 successes including the first, or 3 successes<ul><li>1 extra success to determine where the disarmed item falls</li> <li>2 extra successes to take the weapon for yourself</li> </ul></li> </ul>Now, what will extra training do for you? Well, I\u2019m thinking that Martial Arts specialties will allow you to count 10s as two successes as long as you are spending those successes on an effect relevant to your specialty. A specialty in a Hard Style means a 10 is 2 successes for dealing damage. A specialty in Throws (or call it Judo if you prefer) counts 10s as double for knock down and move opponent. And so on. And multiple specialties can be bought, per Well-Trained Craftsman.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s probably not as strong as some of the top-tier maneuvers for highly-trained martial artists. However, I also intend to allow characters to choose between 1/2E and Revised era multiple action rules (I started a thread about that some months ago) which definitely boosts characters with large pools. That may be enough to make up for the loss, especially given that I don\u2019t want martial arts without Magick to compete with many other supernatural types. (I am not building for a crossover game.)<br /> <br /> I wonder whether specialties doubling 10s is enough. However, I\u2019ve often wondered whether specialties really matter outside of combat, too. If this isn\u2019t good enough for martial artists, how is it good enough for a super-scientist or an Olympic athlete?<br /> <br /> Players who want to name specific moves their character likes to make can simply build what they want with appropriate modifiers and costs, and then use their chosen name to declare their intent. They pull off the maneuver if they roll the required number of successes.<br /> <br /> This is still a work in progress. The list of combat effects that can be bought with successes needs to be expanded, and I haven\u2019t really calibrated the costs properly yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T10:33:48-07:00","id":1522581,"title":"","content":"How would you be approaching defensive actions? With so many moves requiring 2 successes to do any of them, this gives defenders a real advantage if using the standard rules of defensive successes cancel out attacking successes, and may tilt combat towards not a whole lot happening since defending is so favoured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-14-2023, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:06:52-07:00","id":1522612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521633-do-you-use-brawling-and-martial-arts-maneuvers?p=1522581#post1522581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you be approaching defensive actions? With so many moves requiring 2 successes to do any of them, this gives defenders a real advantage if using the standard rules of defensive successes cancel out attacking successes, and may tilt combat towards not a whole lot happening since defending is so favoured.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cSo many\u201d so far is only Knock Down and Disarm. Note the \u201cfirst success\u201d thing. If you start out with the intent to shove your opponent, and then get a lot of successes and decide you want to shove them so hard they hit a wall and take your Strength in damage, that\u2019s intended to be more expensive.<br /> <br /> For those effects that do require more than one (usually the first) success to achieve, I need to run the numbers carefully to see what the changes do to the probabilities. It does need calibration, as I said.<br /> <br /> However, these are effects that correspond to maneuvers in the standard rules that have higher difficulties. That means an attacker can simply accept a +1 to difficulty for a risky move to get a bonus success, and then the probabilities are <i>exactly the same</i> as in the standard rules.<br /> <br /> In fact, as written there, I\u2019ve made them far easier, because I haven\u2019t yet written in the need to achieve more successes than the target\u2019s Strength for a disarm, or the difficulties involved in disarming when you are unarmed, or the various complications involved in sweeps and tackles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 09-14-2023, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:11:24-07:00","id":1522614,"title":"","content":"I will most likely edit that post as I flesh out bits of this set of house rules. It\u2019s not because I want to win arguments by retroactively changing what I said; just that nobody wants me to post cut-and-pasted variations of that post a dozen times as it progresses.<br /> <br /> But I also make no promises about keeping it completely up to date with what we actually do in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T05:28:02-07:00","id":1522627,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, has anyone actually added up how hard the standard M20 disarm maneuver is?<br /> <br /> Unarmed, you\u2019re rolling Dex+Brawl at difficulty 8, with -1 die (which is essentially an application of the optional Weapon Length rule from the sidebar on page 420), and you need to roll more successes than the opponent\u2019s Strength. If you\u2019ve got Dex 4, Brawl 4, you\u2019ve still got over a 75% chance of failing (or botching) that roll. 74.2% chance of failure or botch at Dex + Brawl = 9, 68.09% at 10.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts (at 3 dots) makes it easier, because MA basically reduces the difficulty of everything by 1, but Dex 5, MA 5 is still only a 54.95% chance against that Strength 2 mook.<br /> <br /> Of course, an unarmed disarm should be hard, but don\u2019t tell me anybody is making that a regular part of their character\u2019s toolset.<br /> <br /> If the disarm roll gives at least one success, but not enough to disarm, you do get to inflict regular damage, though - which makes this an existing example of examining the rolled result before determining exactly what the character does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T03:48:09-07:00","id":1522694,"title":"","content":"This is a long thread, but I'm sure someone already mentioned, the Akashic-Brotherhood's, &quot;Do&quot;, which has some special-maneuvers, and most of all, you had your successes to damage. Which, in our games did cause a problem because we had a house-rule that we already added successes to damage, so, what was the point of Do in our games?<br /> <br /> I did, toy with the idea of having gladiators, being able to had successes to damage, given their intensive-training in melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T18:00:35-07:00","id":1522810,"title":"","content":"I have a martial arts background, so not only do I encourage using them but I also help and encourage coming up with ones not in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}